WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.402
Joe: From exclusive
items to portion sizes,

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.037
we wanted to find all the differences

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.940
between KFC in the US and Italy.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.742
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.112
New season, Italy. New host.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:13.880
I want to introduce you to a familiar

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.049
Food Insider face: Claudia.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.253
Let's start with the
Original Recipe chicken.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.222
If you're buying just
the original chicken,

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:25.425
you can get a two-piece. One is huge.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.360
We also have lots of bucket options,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.063
but most of them combine
the Original Recipe,

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.564
wings, and tenders.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.333
If you only want the original chicken,

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.336
the largest size we have
is a six-piece bucket.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.971
Looks a bit scary.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.740
The other bucket options
include a variety of chicken,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.076
such as tenders and hot wings.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.178
For example, if you
want to feed two people,

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.113
you can get the 10-piece bucket.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:51.251
This contains four tenders
and six crispy tenders.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.153
And if you want to feed four people,

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.821
you can get this big boy here.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.790
This one is a 16-piece bucket

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.459
and contains four Original Recipe,

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:03.196
four tenders, four crispy
tenders, and four wings.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.865
This is actually the
biggest thing on the menu.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:09.002
Then in the US, KFC's chicken
comes in four portion sizes.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:12.005
You can start off by getting
a one-piece à la carte,

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.007
then a two-piece with a combo,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.508
a three-piece with a combo,

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.811
and a four-piece with a combo,

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.646
all of which come with
a side of your choice,

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.147
a biscuit, and a drink.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:25.251
Then for the buckets,
we have an eight-piece,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.120
the 12-piece,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.760
and last but not least,
this luscious bucket,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.962
16 pieces of chicken.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.298
Dinner is served in America.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:41.167
You can get those in
either original or crispy.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.769
That makes our biggest bucket

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.506
166% bigger than Italy's.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:49.309
I've actually never really had KFC before.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.111
Chicken is not so popular in Italy,

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:54.047
especially fried chicken served like that.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.516
So I'm really curious to try it and see.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.019
Yeah, nice.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.989
Not a lot of spices. It's
just, like, fried chicken,

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:06.226
which is what we were promised.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:08.928
Let's see how one chicken drumstick weighs

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:09.829
compared to Italy.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.598
Claudia: 64 grams.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.032
Joe: 97 grams.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.336
Is anyone surprised that the
chicken in the United States

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.905
is bigger than every other country

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.607
we've done this "Food Wars" with?

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:22.509
In Italy, we also have hot wings,

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:25.044
and they come in a five-piece

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.780
and in a 18-piece bucket.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.250
This one is designed for three people.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.552
18 wings in the US is definitely

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.254
for one person, not three.

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:37.524
I could have six wings
and then have a full meal.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.959
So, they're advertised as hot wings.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.197
I think to an Italian palate,

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.666
yeah, you could say these are spicy.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.201
We also got wings here in the US.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:51.971
Now, currently, at least the
KFC I went to here in Burbank

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:55.708
has one size of wings, the eight-piece.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.976
Go ahead and take the bones out.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:02:59.746
Crispy.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.614
Heat I can notice that isn't overwhelming.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.615
Perfectly fine.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:03.917
Next are the fries.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.818
In Italy, you can get three sizes:

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:08.087
a small, medium, and large.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:11.191
In the US we got two sizes of fries:

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.927
the individual and the large.

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:15.795
Claudia: Let's weigh our biggest size.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.631
[laughs] I never grow tired of that.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.633
Is this the lowest we've gotten?

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.001
We've gone to the same KFC every time,

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.970
but apparently they
have fired that scooper

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.206
because he or she was being too generous.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:29.409
In Italy, KFC offers drinks in two sizes:

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:30.977
a medium and a large.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:34.547
Drinks in the US, you get
two fountain-drink sizes,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.482
the regular and the large.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.718
I will point out to you,
Claudia, and the rest of Italy,

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:42.555
that our regular, the smallest
drink you can get at a KFC,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.991
is 591 milliliters,

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:48.861
which is much bigger than your large.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:52.031
But if you really want
your thirst quenched,

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:56.202
you can get yourself the big boy. Guszh!

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.871
That is a half gallon, 64 fluid ounces,

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:03.476
or 1,892.7 milliliters

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.510
of beverage.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.213
Claudia: Let's measure the
large one to see if that's true.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.415
Joe: Supposed to be 887.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.384
Let me just see if we can
get it up to 800. Whoa.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.885
This is just 800.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.688
The messes that this
show forces me to make.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:21.194
If you are incredible at balancing
and you don't want a cap,

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.161
I guess this is OK

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.765
if you're just going to sit
at your table like [slurps].

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.270
Here's everything that you
can get at KFC in Italy

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.138
that you won't find in the US.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.440
Here's everything you'll
find at a KFC in the US

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.142
you won't find in Italy.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:40.179
We have one exclusive chicken
option you can't get in Italy.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.282
That is the extra-crispy.

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:43.716
This is probably close to what you get,

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.817
the Original Recipe.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.119
And then you got the extra-crispy.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.087
I mean, obviously, it's night and day.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.289
Volume up on this one.

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:52.692
This is regular [crunching],

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:57.130
and of course the extra-crispy
[louder crunching].

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.733
If you're wondering, yes, way better,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.568
way more flavorful. Mm!

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:05.371
We don't have extra-crispy
chicken here in Italy,

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.206
but if you order tenders,

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.209
you're going to get original and crispy.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.078
It does look much crispier.

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:16.582
It also looks, it just
looks much sadder as well,

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.584
because it's literally flopping.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.586
At least I can see the chicken.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.322
I can see some meat in there.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:25.558
This one is completely
hidden in the batter.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.060
Like, it could be anything.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:31.130
Another exclusive are the KFC nuggets.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.299
You can get these in
varieties of five, eight,

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.568
12, and 36.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:36.969
I went with the five-piece.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.572
Now, Claudia, take a good look at this.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.841
You in Italy have popcorn chicken.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:44.243
Besides potential size differences,

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.546
I really don't know what else
is different about these.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:48.414
In Italy we don't have nuggets,

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.983
but we have popcorn chicken.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:54.721
We got the large, but it comes
also in small and medium.

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:56.356
Quietly sometime last year,

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.991
KFC just took popcorn
chicken off the menu,

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.293
and I'm pretty bummed about that.

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.762
I mean, I like the nuggets,
but the popcorn chicken, man.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:04.430
It's just something because
they're a lot smaller,

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.265
and then the chicken-to-skin ratio

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:07.934
is more in favor of the skin,

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:09.702
so you get a lot of that
savory skin in there.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:10.737
RIP, popcorn chicken.

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:13.072
You're very lucky, Claudia.
You are very lucky.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:15.508
Were you guys the guinea pigs for this,

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:19.345
or are we the guinea pigs for
a new recipe or something?

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:22.715
I think I prefer a whole piece.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:25.785
I think bingeing on
little bits of chicken,

00:06:25.785 --> 00:06:28.087
it's so un-Italian

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:31.290
that I'm not sure that I'll
be getting used to that.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.560
Snacking on little bits of fried chicken

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.496
while in a convenient to-go box

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:37.964
while driving or walking around

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:39.832
is so American, and I love it.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.634
I gotta try these.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.136
This is what America's all about.

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:45.705
Let's move on to the chicken sandwiches.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:48.541
In Italy, we have the Zinger.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:52.945
This is supposed to be Italy's
version of the spicy chicken

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.414
that you guys have in the US.

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:57.116
I don't know, Joe, how does
that look like? Similar?

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.252
Yes, Claudia, your Zinger sandwich

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:02.822
looks a little bit like
our spicy chicken sandwich.

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:05.091
Here's ours, and we only
have pickles on ours,

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:06.492
so no lettuce and tomato.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:09.362
But after I took a bite,

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.798
you can see there's, like, some red here,

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.499
so that's supposed to be the spice.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:16.769
There's the tiniest, tiniest,
tiniest spice, to be honest.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.972
Then, moving on, we have
this tiny little thing,

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.073
the Krunky.

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:22.642
Crunchy or Krunky.

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:24.410
This one here is on the value menu,

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:27.246
so it's a cheaper option.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:30.983
And then we've got the Colonel,
named after Colonel Sanders.

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:33.252
We don't really have colonels here.

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.955
I think we do, but we
keep them for the army.

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.990
I don't think they've ever
opened a chicken restaurant.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.892
Then we got the Double Colonel.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:42.728
Does that mean that another person joined?

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:46.332
Then we have the Kentucky
chicken and bacon.

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:48.000
I have to say, this is the biggest bacon

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.937
that I've seen in
Italian fast-food chains.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:53.473
This to me feels quite, quite fake.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:55.775
You can also get this one in a double.

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:58.311
And then we have the chicken grilled.

00:07:58.311 --> 00:08:01.914
So much sauce. Sad, sad
lettuce hanging off mayo.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.883
You can also get the double crispy,

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:07.386
which is two chicken tenders in a bun.

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:08.855
Here are sandwiches you can get in the US

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:10.656
you can't get in Italy,
starting down here.

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:12.258
The classic Chicken Little.

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:15.228
I don't know, it's just a
tender in between two buns.

00:08:15.228 --> 00:08:16.729
Here's what I would do: I would go to KFC,

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:19.999
I'd stand in line, I'd order
my meal and get one of these,

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:21.834
and then demand they give me this

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.836
while I wait for the rest of my food.

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:25.004
It's nothing. It's nothing.

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.072
It's like an appetizer.

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:29.342
And then, of course, just
the regular chicken sandwich.

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:31.110
I have said on record several times

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.046
that I think KFC might have the best

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:36.415
fast-food chicken sandwich in America.

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:37.416
There's also apparently an

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.552
ultimate barbecue fried chicken sandwich.

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:41.487
That was new. I think it came and went.

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:45.358
As an Italian, I'm not so
big on chicken burgers.

00:08:45.358 --> 00:08:47.693
I think the idea of
having chicken in a burger

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:50.863
doesn't really resonate so well with us.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.765
So it almost hurts my eyes.

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.700
There's just too much brown in it.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.069
Like, I want to see more color.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:59.805
Yeah, that's absolutely not the case here.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:02.241
As you can see, our chicken is deep-fried

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.977
and covered in a mayo-y sauce.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:07.813
We're eating chicken
all the time in America.

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:08.648
Yeah, we eat a lot of beef,

00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:10.316
but we also eat a lot of chicken,

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:13.719
and it is in no way diet
food here. Not at all.

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:17.256
We also used to have twisted
wraps here at KFC in Italy,

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:19.692
but suddenly they're
not on the menu anymore.

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:21.127
They're still worth mentioning, though,

00:09:21.127 --> 00:09:24.430
because of the hilarious
advertising campaign.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.432
When KFC launched them in Italy,

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:29.268
they actually designed
Italian leather handbags

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:31.938
supposed to hold your Twisters,

00:09:31.938 --> 00:09:35.141
which is a bit of a knockoff
to the Fendi Baguette bag.

00:09:35.141 --> 00:09:37.443
All right, we might not have
Italian bags for our wraps,

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:39.912
but we do have KFC Crocs.

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:41.180
Look how cool those look.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.014
[crickets]

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.482
We do have a couple wrap options.

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:45.985
You can only get them
through the KFC application,

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:47.253
which is not how I ordered.

00:09:47.253 --> 00:09:49.388
Anyway, you can get the classic
one with a crispy tender.

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:52.592
There's also a spicy one
that I assume is spicier.

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:54.427
And, apparently, you can
get two of them for $5,

00:09:54.427 --> 00:09:57.964
which is a pretty good
deal. But I didn't get that.

00:09:57.964 --> 00:10:00.733
Here's a few hilarious things
you can't get in Italy.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:02.301
Over here's the Famous Bowl.

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:04.203
Yes, Claudia, I know you're
dying to know all about this,

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:05.438
so I will tell you now.

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:09.675
It is nuggets, mashed
potatoes, gravy, corn,

00:10:09.675 --> 00:10:12.812
cheese, all in one convenient tub.

00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:15.414
So, this would be, I guess,
what's considered a bite.

00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:17.850
It's really heavy.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.987
It's gotta be 90% mashed potato.

00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:21.821
It's a lot.

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:25.858
Another American exclusive
is this, a chicken pot pie.

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:27.760
Look at the size of this thing.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:32.465
I think this would just
profoundly confuse every Italian.

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.634
Here's the thing about the
mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:36.235
You have to get them together.

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:38.838
Having them separately
seems very strange to me.

00:10:38.838 --> 00:10:41.641
It is a classic US side dish,

00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:43.809
especially with things like fried chicken.

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:46.512
Apparently when Colonel
Sanders sold the business,

00:10:46.512 --> 00:10:48.948
he compared the mashed
potatoes in a Manhattan store

00:10:48.948 --> 00:10:51.817
to "wallpaper paste" topped with "sludge."

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:53.085
But that was back in the '70s,

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:54.954
so hopefully they've
made some improvements.

00:10:54.954 --> 00:10:56.489
I'd say that they have.

00:10:56.489 --> 00:10:59.759
I mean, I know, like, those
mashed potatoes look so dry.

00:10:59.759 --> 00:11:03.262
I understand you want to put
some sort of liquid on them.

00:11:03.262 --> 00:11:04.930
I'd just not have any of it.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:05.765
But for once,

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:08.668
the potatoes don't look
radioactively yellow,

00:11:08.668 --> 00:11:10.770
so that should be a good sign.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:15.041
We happen to have some Italian-style
sides here on the menu,

00:11:15.041 --> 00:11:17.510
although I have no idea who
called this Italian style,

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.979
because none of these
really look Italian to me.

00:11:19.979 --> 00:11:21.480
We have cheese puffs.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.517
To me, these look like fried Babybels.

00:11:24.517 --> 00:11:26.585
That's the only cheese that I can think of

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:28.154
that has this shape.

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:32.191
I think it's some kind of mozzarella.

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:33.492
Yeah, OK.

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:34.760
Yeah, we have bread.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.897
Just, like funny bread.

00:11:37.897 --> 00:11:39.965
It looks very dry, just by looking at it.

00:11:39.965 --> 00:11:43.069
And then we have corn on the cob.

00:11:43.069 --> 00:11:45.304
The US has off the cob.

00:11:45.304 --> 00:11:47.707
This is not Italian.

00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:50.476
I've never seen an Italian
person having corn on the cob.

00:11:50.476 --> 00:11:52.678
In Italy, we also have four salads,

00:11:52.678 --> 00:11:54.914
but we were not able to get them today.

00:11:54.914 --> 00:11:56.682
Those are grilled chicken,

00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:59.018
crispy chicken, and original chicken,

00:11:59.018 --> 00:12:02.021
which, we don't know how that
differs from the crispy one,

00:12:02.021 --> 00:12:04.590
and a veggie salad.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.659
Right, Claudia, look at that.

00:12:06.659 --> 00:12:07.760
Look at that mac and cheese.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.028
It's American mac and cheese.

00:12:09.028 --> 00:12:12.665
I mean, I don't really have
thoughts about mac and cheese,

00:12:12.665 --> 00:12:15.401
because to me that's just not Italian.

00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:17.236
We just sort of gave up on it and be like,

00:12:17.236 --> 00:12:19.138
"You want it? It's yours."

00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:21.841
Yeah, I get it. Like, bright yellow.

00:12:21.841 --> 00:12:25.644
But Claudia, what you can't tell

00:12:25.644 --> 00:12:26.946
is how good this tastes.

00:12:29.148 --> 00:12:32.985
Other US sides you can get here: coleslaw.

00:12:32.985 --> 00:12:34.787
Claudia was talking about corn on the cob.

00:12:34.787 --> 00:12:38.424
We got corn off the cob, aka sweet corn.

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:41.293
I'm just thinking, in terms
of the American experience,

00:12:41.293 --> 00:12:44.930
I don't want to be all,
like, doing this at my desk

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.365
when I get KFC for lunch, you know?

00:12:46.365 --> 00:12:48.100
I just want to eat it and get going, so.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:50.402
Another thing we have here, biscuits.

00:12:50.402 --> 00:12:52.471
And I feel like you get these
with these types of meals

00:12:52.471 --> 00:12:54.006
because it's good at sopping up things,

00:12:54.006 --> 00:12:55.941
like good at sopping up the gravy.

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:58.811
On their own, they're
just so ... [thudding].

00:12:58.811 --> 00:13:01.147
I want to see if I can eat
one without any liquid,

00:13:01.147 --> 00:13:03.182
like, how long it takes me
to eat a dry one. Ready?

00:13:03.182 --> 00:13:05.618
This is how dry these
are. Ready? Time me. Go.

00:13:11.157 --> 00:13:12.458
Only halfway through!

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:21.367
Ugh, it hurts to talk.

00:13:21.367 --> 00:13:22.468
Time.

00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:24.937
Yeah, not my favorite.

00:13:24.937 --> 00:13:26.872
Another exclusive you
can get here in the US

00:13:26.872 --> 00:13:28.974
is a piece of à la carte chicken.

00:13:28.974 --> 00:13:31.777
I feel like if you went into
a KFC in Italy and was like,

00:13:31.777 --> 00:13:33.579
"I just want one drumstick,"
they'd give it to you.

00:13:33.579 --> 00:13:35.314
I don't think they'd
really push back on it.

00:13:35.314 --> 00:13:36.882
But our menu specifically has,

00:13:36.882 --> 00:13:38.851
you get an individual piece of chicken.

00:13:38.851 --> 00:13:41.020
You can get a drumstick,
a thigh, or a breast.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:44.657
You get chicken in this hand,
Famous Bowl in this hand,

00:13:44.657 --> 00:13:46.525
and walk right into traffic.

00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:48.394
Sauce talk, let's go.

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:50.462
Discorso di la salsa.

00:13:50.462 --> 00:13:52.565
In Italy, we have some exclusive sauces,

00:13:52.565 --> 00:13:54.633
starting from the original.

00:13:54.633 --> 00:13:57.636
I know you guys in the
US have the KFC sauce.

00:13:57.636 --> 00:13:59.772
Does this look similar?

00:14:01.173 --> 00:14:04.443
I think if I were making sauces,
I would've just continued,

00:14:04.443 --> 00:14:07.146
you know, trialing others after this one.

00:14:09.181 --> 00:14:11.617
Yeah, it's, like, a
mayo-y barbecue ketchup.

00:14:11.617 --> 00:14:14.954
And then we have the smoky barbecue sauce.

00:14:14.954 --> 00:14:17.590
And then we have the sweet imperial sauce.

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:20.860
That's a sweet and sour sauce.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:23.529
Very lemony, but fresh.

00:14:23.529 --> 00:14:24.864
Yeah, it's a nice one. I like this.

00:14:24.864 --> 00:14:28.667
Then move on to the 2 hot 4 U.

00:14:28.667 --> 00:14:29.935
Jelly-like.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:33.439
It's not too hot for you,
it's just too bad for me.

00:14:33.439 --> 00:14:36.041
Moving on, we also have garlic sauce.

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:37.910
I know you guys associate Italy

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:39.745
and Italian cuisine with garlic.

00:14:39.745 --> 00:14:41.513
Please stop doing that.

00:14:41.513 --> 00:14:43.582
We don't really like it.

00:14:43.582 --> 00:14:46.018
Then we have a fresh pepper one.

00:14:46.018 --> 00:14:48.087
This one apparently contains cheese.

00:14:48.988 --> 00:14:50.422
Tastes like not much, to be honest.

00:14:50.422 --> 00:14:52.491
We also have creamy curry.

00:14:52.491 --> 00:14:55.461
Finally, we couldn't
get the only olive oil,

00:14:55.461 --> 00:14:58.097
but we do have olive oil and white vinegar

00:14:58.097 --> 00:15:01.367
and olive oil and balsamic vinegar.

00:15:01.367 --> 00:15:04.870
I don't know if you want to
consider olive oil a sauce.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:06.605
I have mixed feeling about it,

00:15:06.605 --> 00:15:08.741
because that's definitely more dressing.

00:15:08.741 --> 00:15:11.977
Are you curious to see how
chicken olive oil tastes like?

00:15:11.977 --> 00:15:12.978
Let's try it.

00:15:12.978 --> 00:15:16.081
Olive oil and balsamic vinegar. Let's see.

00:15:17.683 --> 00:15:19.451
Kind of brought it back
to life a little bit,

00:15:19.451 --> 00:15:21.353
because it had cooled down.

00:15:21.353 --> 00:15:22.888
Yeah, I should do this
more often, actually.

00:15:22.888 --> 00:15:25.991
It tastes less fried for some reason.

00:15:25.991 --> 00:15:27.660
Because I always associate olive oil

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:28.994
with, like, grilled chicken.

00:15:28.994 --> 00:15:31.797
So if you want to trick
your mind into thinking

00:15:31.797 --> 00:15:34.300
that you're eating grilled
chicken and not fried,

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:37.636
maybe all you have to do is
pour some olive oil on it.

00:15:37.636 --> 00:15:38.604
Joe: Honey mustard.

00:15:38.604 --> 00:15:41.140
Honey barbecue.

00:15:42.174 --> 00:15:43.876
That's good. Buffalo ranch.

00:15:43.876 --> 00:15:46.345
If you are unaware, we have a sauce here

00:15:46.345 --> 00:15:48.347
that usually is on wings
called the Buffalo sauce.

00:15:48.347 --> 00:15:50.816
It's a vinegary hot sauce

00:15:50.816 --> 00:15:54.453
that is a little north of mild.

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:56.789
And the reason that
Buffalo ranch is a thing

00:15:56.789 --> 00:15:59.792
is because when you eat Buffalo
wings and they're spicy,

00:15:59.792 --> 00:16:04.630
you dip the wings in ranch, a
second sauce, to cool it down.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:06.031
So we as Americans are used

00:16:06.031 --> 00:16:08.200
to pairing Buffalo sauce on the wings

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.468
with ranch dressing.

00:16:09.468 --> 00:16:11.303
So they were like, let's
just put it in one,

00:16:11.303 --> 00:16:13.806
because God forbid we have two sauces.

00:16:13.806 --> 00:16:15.207
But if you want to have
just regular ranch,

00:16:15.207 --> 00:16:16.976
everyone on the internet
come at me, all right?

00:16:16.976 --> 00:16:19.712
Ranch is just OK. It all tastes the same.

00:16:19.712 --> 00:16:20.946
Also we have a hot sauce.

00:16:20.946 --> 00:16:22.047
A honey sauce.

00:16:22.047 --> 00:16:24.550
We have a lot of dessert
options here in Italy.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:27.019
Most of them are just ice cream.

00:16:27.019 --> 00:16:29.621
We start from a plain ice cream cone.

00:16:29.621 --> 00:16:31.190
Then you can get sundaes.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.258
They come plain, caramel flavor,

00:16:33.258 --> 00:16:35.561
Nutella, strawberry, and chocolate.

00:16:35.561 --> 00:16:37.529
And then we have these, the Kream Balls.

00:16:37.529 --> 00:16:40.632
They come with Nutella flavor, caramel,

00:16:40.632 --> 00:16:42.601
strawberry, and chocolate.

00:16:42.601 --> 00:16:44.403
They're kind of similar to a sundae,

00:16:44.403 --> 00:16:47.439
but they have this crunchy bottom.

00:16:47.439 --> 00:16:49.008
And apparently the caramel one

00:16:49.008 --> 00:16:50.576
is supposed to have lots of layers.

00:16:50.576 --> 00:16:51.610
This is the caramel one.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:54.813
But I'm not sure we can
judge the number of layers,

00:16:54.813 --> 00:16:57.049
because it has absolutely melted.

00:16:57.049 --> 00:17:01.120
So, we got a Nutella Kream
Ball and a caramel one.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.889
You know those backpacks for cats?

00:17:03.889 --> 00:17:06.725
I think it's the same thing here.

00:17:06.725 --> 00:17:09.094
I'm curious about the crunchy bottom.

00:17:09.094 --> 00:17:11.130
Oh, yeah, that is crunchy.

00:17:13.432 --> 00:17:15.667
Actually it reminds me a little bit of

00:17:15.667 --> 00:17:17.770
the Algida, the Cornetto.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:20.272
It may have another name in the US.

00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:23.609
And they have that
crunchy bit at the bottom.

00:17:23.609 --> 00:17:27.012
I mean, for us Italian, Nutella
is like the OG chocolate.

00:17:27.012 --> 00:17:29.748
Before chocolate always comes Nutella,

00:17:29.748 --> 00:17:31.450
just no questions asked.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:34.086
It's always been like this.
And before cream as well.

00:17:34.086 --> 00:17:37.089
The only exclusive dessert
option we have in America

00:17:37.089 --> 00:17:39.124
is this: a chocolate cake.

00:17:39.124 --> 00:17:40.259
And it just occurred to me,

00:17:40.259 --> 00:17:42.094
I've actually never had this cake.

00:17:42.094 --> 00:17:43.695
Let's see how we did.

00:17:46.198 --> 00:17:47.533
Perfect.

00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:49.101
Cooked beautifully.

00:17:49.101 --> 00:17:52.404
It's got the right amount
of bounce, isn't dried out.

00:17:52.404 --> 00:17:53.705
And now we taste it.

00:17:57.176 --> 00:17:58.710
Exquisite.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.447
You keep baking like that,
you can win this competition.

00:18:01.447 --> 00:18:03.315
I started off as Gordon Ramsay.

00:18:03.315 --> 00:18:05.651
Every impression I do of
anyone is just kind of that.

00:18:05.651 --> 00:18:06.718
This is actually pretty good.

00:18:06.718 --> 00:18:10.155
Yeah, they had those
balls, those Kream Balls,

00:18:10.155 --> 00:18:12.591
which is kind of a weird thing to call it.

00:18:12.591 --> 00:18:14.293
No, I don't want any of those.

00:18:14.293 --> 00:18:16.528
I get it. I like dessert
just as much as the next guy.

00:18:16.528 --> 00:18:19.631
But KFC, I want to load
up on fried chicken.

00:18:19.631 --> 00:18:21.433
I want to load up on mac and cheese.

00:18:21.433 --> 00:18:23.135
I want to load up on mashed potatoes.

00:18:23.135 --> 00:18:24.603
I want to load up on corn.

00:18:24.603 --> 00:18:27.172
If only someone could put
it all in one bowl for me.

00:18:27.172 --> 00:18:29.208
Dessert? No, I want to eat fried chicken

00:18:29.208 --> 00:18:31.443
until I'm about to burst,
and then I'm out. So.

00:18:31.443 --> 00:18:33.278
The exclusive drinks in Italy are

00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:36.682
7Up, Lipton iced tea, and beer.

00:18:36.682 --> 00:18:38.383
Fountain drinks you can get in the US.

00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:39.551
We do have a bunch of exclusives.

00:18:39.551 --> 00:18:41.587
I didn't get every single one, relax.

00:18:41.587 --> 00:18:43.122
All right, starting down here.

00:18:43.122 --> 00:18:44.590
Sweet tea.

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:46.158
Oh, yeah, their lemonade.

00:18:46.158 --> 00:18:47.126
It's really good. It's addictive.

00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:51.163
And our lemonade is not
carbonated, it's still.

00:18:51.163 --> 00:18:52.631
Mountain Dew, it's fantastic.

00:18:52.631 --> 00:18:54.333
And the reason I saved this one for last,

00:18:54.333 --> 00:18:59.037
it's something you can get
exclusively at the KFC in the US,

00:18:59.037 --> 00:19:01.240
it's Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.408
It's so good. Like, you
just know it's super sweet,

00:19:03.408 --> 00:19:05.310
and super chemically, but I love it.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:08.347
Other drinks you can get at
a US KFC that we did not get

00:19:08.347 --> 00:19:11.083
was Starry and blackberry lemonade,

00:19:11.083 --> 00:19:12.518
which is currently unavailable.

00:19:14.119 --> 00:19:16.755
Which country's getting
a better deal on its KFC?

00:19:16.755 --> 00:19:19.224
Let's compare a few
menu items to find out.

00:19:19.224 --> 00:19:21.927
Looking at the chicken
sandwich combo meal,

00:19:21.927 --> 00:19:23.862
which comes with a side
and a medium drink,

00:19:23.862 --> 00:19:27.466
this whole thing in Los
Angeles would cost you $10.99.

00:19:27.466 --> 00:19:31.003
Note, if you got each item
individually, added up,

00:19:31.003 --> 00:19:33.372
it would be $12.77.

00:19:33.372 --> 00:19:36.041
In Italy, you can also get a similar meal

00:19:36.041 --> 00:19:37.843
that is called a Zinger meal,

00:19:37.843 --> 00:19:39.578
and that includes a sandwich,

00:19:39.578 --> 00:19:41.513
a side of choice, and a drink.

00:19:41.513 --> 00:19:43.849
This will cost you 10 euros and 40 cents.

00:19:43.849 --> 00:19:48.220
At the time of recording,
that is equal to $11.52.

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:52.124
So that is 5% more
expensive than the US meal.

00:19:52.124 --> 00:19:54.293
If you order these items individually,

00:19:54.293 --> 00:19:56.995
that will cost you 13 euros and 60 cents,

00:19:56.995 --> 00:19:59.932
and that's about $15.06.

00:19:59.932 --> 00:20:02.901
We also took a look at
KFC's most expensive items.

00:20:02.901 --> 00:20:05.470
In Italy, the most
expensive item on the menu

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.506
is the 16-piece bucket.

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:10.576
This one costs 42 euros 90 cents,

00:20:10.576 --> 00:20:14.213
which is about $47.51.

00:20:14.213 --> 00:20:16.048
This is supposed to feed four people

00:20:16.048 --> 00:20:19.351
for $11.87 per person.

00:20:19.351 --> 00:20:21.353
The most expensive item on the US menu

00:20:21.353 --> 00:20:23.322
is the 16-piece chicken meal,

00:20:23.322 --> 00:20:25.657
which includes 16 pieces of chicken,

00:20:25.657 --> 00:20:26.959
original or crispy,

00:20:26.959 --> 00:20:28.894
four large sides, eight biscuits,

00:20:28.894 --> 00:20:32.497
and it costs you $52.99.

00:20:32.497 --> 00:20:35.100
Now, this is meant to feed
seven to eight people.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:35.934
Sure.

00:20:35.934 --> 00:20:39.271
And it costs roughly $6.62 per person,

00:20:39.271 --> 00:20:43.008
which is 44% cheaper than
Italy's per-person cost.

00:20:43.008 --> 00:20:45.777
Italy KFC puts a lot of effort

00:20:45.777 --> 00:20:48.213
into its meals and special offers

00:20:48.213 --> 00:20:50.482
so they can be a better
value for the money.

00:20:50.482 --> 00:20:54.353
Personally, in Italy, we're not
really used to having meals.

00:20:54.353 --> 00:20:58.657
We are very accustomed to
just having a big main course.

00:20:58.657 --> 00:21:01.660
That to me still feels a
bit of an American thing.

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.362
But this is American food,

00:21:03.362 --> 00:21:06.331
so I guess we are using
their customs as well.

00:21:06.331 --> 00:21:07.899
If you're operating under the assumption

00:21:07.899 --> 00:21:10.669
that this is for seven people,
it's a pretty good deal.

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:14.106
But you and I both know
this ain't for seven people.

00:21:15.841 --> 00:21:18.043
We want to see if there
are any similarities

00:21:18.043 --> 00:21:21.280
in the nutrition of
KFC for both countries.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.414
Now, this is our chicken sandwich,

00:21:22.414 --> 00:21:25.584
and it has 650 calories.

00:21:25.584 --> 00:21:26.652
And if you'll notice,

00:21:26.652 --> 00:21:28.420
there's a lot of salt
and fat in this sandwich,

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:31.056
over half your daily recommended intake.

00:21:31.056 --> 00:21:33.292
KFC Italy doesn't disclose their calories

00:21:33.292 --> 00:21:34.426
on their website.

00:21:34.426 --> 00:21:37.062
Actually, I think disclosing
nutritional information,

00:21:37.062 --> 00:21:38.497
like calories and everything,

00:21:38.497 --> 00:21:40.766
I find that quite an American thing.

00:21:40.766 --> 00:21:42.367
That doesn't mean it's good or bad.

00:21:42.367 --> 00:21:43.969
It's just like, we don't really

00:21:43.969 --> 00:21:46.305
tend to count calories in things.

00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:49.341
Every "Food Wars" we've
done, all the nutrition info,

00:21:49.341 --> 00:21:51.176
all the ingredients info, in the US,

00:21:51.176 --> 00:21:52.911
you can get it, no problem.

00:21:52.911 --> 00:21:55.280
Other countries, they don't provide it.

00:21:57.082 --> 00:21:58.850
Let's take a look at some ingredients

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.752
that KFC uses here in Italy.

00:22:00.752 --> 00:22:03.822
Here are all the
ingredients for the fries.

00:22:03.822 --> 00:22:05.691
Nine is a lot.

00:22:05.691 --> 00:22:08.160
Potatoes and frying oil, how about two?

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:11.830
Two ingredients, and a bit
of salt, and one chemical.

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:14.700
Let's just use one, you
know, if we have to.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:18.437
And here are all the ingredients
of the fries in the US.

00:22:18.437 --> 00:22:20.439
33 ingredients.

00:22:20.439 --> 00:22:23.975
That's 24 more than the
ingredients in Italy's fries.

00:22:23.975 --> 00:22:25.210
That's nuts.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:26.912
Claudia: Nine ingredients for this thing,

00:22:26.912 --> 00:22:28.814
and it doesn't even hold its shape.

00:22:28.814 --> 00:22:31.316
I would expect it to be perfect.

00:22:31.316 --> 00:22:33.485
There's a lot of flavors
and colorings that we use,

00:22:33.485 --> 00:22:36.288
like paprika, turmeric,
and annatto extract color,

00:22:36.288 --> 00:22:38.190
which is funny we put that into the fries,

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:41.093
but when making this, KFC also
uses bleached white flour,

00:22:41.093 --> 00:22:42.728
which removes all the color,

00:22:42.728 --> 00:22:43.962
so it seems kind of counterproductive.

00:22:43.962 --> 00:22:45.330
Like, they're taking all the color out

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:46.865
with the bleached flour, right?

00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:48.367
And they're putting all
those chemicals back in

00:22:48.367 --> 00:22:50.369
to make them look like fries.

00:22:50.369 --> 00:22:51.703
I don't know why we do that either.

00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:53.705
So, let's have a look at the ingredients

00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:55.774
for a chicken drumstick.

00:22:55.774 --> 00:22:58.777
Italy's chicken uses a
lot of flavor enhancers,

00:22:58.777 --> 00:23:00.746
gums, and stabilizers.

00:23:00.746 --> 00:23:03.682
For example, xanthan gum and guar gum.

00:23:03.682 --> 00:23:05.350
They're used in meat products

00:23:05.350 --> 00:23:08.353
to keep the chicken tender
during the cooking process.

00:23:08.353 --> 00:23:10.789
These gums are also used for chicken

00:23:10.789 --> 00:23:14.226
that has a batter around
it, so that when it's fried,

00:23:14.226 --> 00:23:15.994
it absorbs less oil.

00:23:15.994 --> 00:23:18.864
As I said before, Italians
don't really look at ingredients

00:23:18.864 --> 00:23:21.233
or nutritional value of things.

00:23:21.233 --> 00:23:22.367
And that is why I think there is

00:23:22.367 --> 00:23:25.737
a lot of work done beforehand for us

00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:27.939
in order to make the food
as simple as possible,

00:23:27.939 --> 00:23:29.841
so that if you do look at the ingredients,

00:23:29.841 --> 00:23:32.144
you are not so shocked by it.

00:23:32.144 --> 00:23:35.614
And here are the ingredients
of the chicken in the US.

00:23:35.614 --> 00:23:37.315
Surprisingly smaller than Italy's list,

00:23:37.315 --> 00:23:40.252
although the US has not noted
what oil they use for frying,

00:23:40.252 --> 00:23:41.453
like Italy has.

00:23:41.453 --> 00:23:44.289
So it would probably add
a few more ingredients.

00:23:44.289 --> 00:23:46.691
Now, KFC actually uses pressure frying

00:23:46.691 --> 00:23:48.860
instead of deep frying,
like the other chains,

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:50.962
as it allows for faster cooking time

00:23:50.962 --> 00:23:52.831
and always keeps the meat moister,

00:23:52.831 --> 00:23:54.332
as less steam evaporates.

00:23:54.332 --> 00:23:56.501
Let's take a closer look
at a few ingredients

00:23:56.501 --> 00:23:58.403
that some of us may not recognize.

00:23:58.403 --> 00:24:01.239
OK, first up, sodium phosphate.

00:24:01.239 --> 00:24:03.575
Now, it helps stabilize the pH of the food

00:24:03.575 --> 00:24:04.976
to keep them together.

00:24:04.976 --> 00:24:07.779
But it's also popular
over-the-counter medicine

00:24:07.779 --> 00:24:09.614
for bowel movements.

00:24:09.614 --> 00:24:11.349
So don't be surprised if eating KFC

00:24:11.349 --> 00:24:14.186
makes you rush to the bathroom.

00:24:14.186 --> 00:24:17.856
Next up, monosodium glutamate,

00:24:17.856 --> 00:24:21.126
flavor enhancer commonly added
to soups and processed meats.

00:24:21.126 --> 00:24:23.495
Ugh. We're putting these
names on-screen, right?

00:24:23.495 --> 00:24:26.665
Ah, this word looks like this

00:24:26.665 --> 00:24:28.667
and is probably pronounced

00:24:28.667 --> 00:24:32.604
dime-thigh-polo-sigh-lexane.

00:24:32.604 --> 00:24:34.639
Computer: Dimethylpolysiloxane.

00:24:34.639 --> 00:24:37.209
It's an antifoaming agent
derived from silicone,

00:24:37.209 --> 00:24:40.512
usually added to oils,
jams, and canned vegetables.

00:24:40.512 --> 00:24:43.348
Disodium dihydrogen pyrophosphate.

00:24:43.348 --> 00:24:45.183
This should be a contest. Anyway. OK.

00:24:45.183 --> 00:24:47.686
Prevents potatoes in the
fries from turning brown

00:24:47.686 --> 00:24:49.521
due to oxidization,

00:24:49.521 --> 00:24:52.257
which is natural for most
fruits and vegetables.

00:24:52.257 --> 00:24:53.859
And just to add that all these ingredients

00:24:53.859 --> 00:24:55.694
have been approved by health professionals

00:24:55.694 --> 00:24:57.562
and there are no safety concerns,

00:24:57.562 --> 00:25:00.565
as long as they're eaten
in lower quantities,

00:25:00.565 --> 00:25:03.435
which, in general, is good
advice for eating fast food.

00:25:03.435 --> 00:25:06.771
Chickens in the US are free of
added hormones and steroids.

00:25:06.771 --> 00:25:09.241
However, KFC does not disclose much else

00:25:09.241 --> 00:25:10.942
about how the chicken is prepared,

00:25:10.942 --> 00:25:13.778
nor how much chicken is used per item.

00:25:13.778 --> 00:25:17.215
As of 2019, Yum Brands,
the parent company of KFC,

00:25:17.215 --> 00:25:20.619
stopped purchasing chicken
raised using antibiotics.

00:25:20.619 --> 00:25:22.888
So I guess they're heading
in the right direction.

00:25:24.856 --> 00:25:28.660
KFC opened their first outlet in the '70s

00:25:28.660 --> 00:25:30.662
in Naples for some reason.

00:25:30.662 --> 00:25:32.998
And then that didn't work
out, and they closed.

00:25:32.998 --> 00:25:35.600
And then they came back to Italy in 2014.

00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:39.671
The objective was to open
100 branches in four years.

00:25:39.671 --> 00:25:41.306
They're not quite there yet.

00:25:41.306 --> 00:25:43.208
As of 2022, the stats say

00:25:43.208 --> 00:25:46.678
that they've opened 68
branches here in Italy.

00:25:46.678 --> 00:25:48.380
Although it's been here since 2014,

00:25:48.380 --> 00:25:50.615
it does still feel pretty new.

00:25:50.615 --> 00:25:53.518
Like, Italians are not so big on chicken,

00:25:53.518 --> 00:25:54.886
especially grilled chicken.

00:25:54.886 --> 00:25:58.690
It does still feel like
a very foreign idea.

00:25:58.690 --> 00:26:01.326
KFC is so popular in the US,

00:26:01.326 --> 00:26:03.562
maybe the most popular chicken chain,

00:26:03.562 --> 00:26:04.763
fried-chicken chain at least.

00:26:04.763 --> 00:26:06.898
I think it's the

00:26:06.898 --> 00:26:10.535
fried-chicken chain to beat in the US.

00:26:10.535 --> 00:26:12.938
There's other chicken places
that do chicken sandwiches,

00:26:12.938 --> 00:26:15.840
chicken burgers. But as
far as chicken on the bone,

00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:17.909
I don't know who's even
competing with KFC.

00:26:17.909 --> 00:26:19.678
Ah, I guess there's Popeyes.

00:26:19.678 --> 00:26:20.946
Oh, yeah, Popeyes.

00:26:20.946 --> 00:26:23.281
No, I think KFC is way
more popular than Popeyes.

00:26:23.281 --> 00:26:24.616
I didn't say it's better.

00:26:24.616 --> 00:26:27.352
If a KFC opens in a new town,

00:26:27.352 --> 00:26:29.754
for example, in my hometown
they opened last year,

00:26:29.754 --> 00:26:31.323
there are huge lines.

00:26:31.323 --> 00:26:33.158
There are a lot of people
that want to try it

00:26:33.158 --> 00:26:34.459
because it's really the idea

00:26:34.459 --> 00:26:37.062
of the American fast-food
chain that's arriving.

00:26:37.062 --> 00:26:39.130
So it's exciting. It's different.

00:26:39.130 --> 00:26:40.665
Again, it's one of those
things that I think

00:26:40.665 --> 00:26:42.734
you do try it because of the hype.

00:26:42.734 --> 00:26:45.870
KFC adaptability is
weird. A couple years ago,

00:26:45.870 --> 00:26:47.706
there used to be a lot
more stuff on the menu.

00:26:47.706 --> 00:26:49.140
And now there's a lot less.

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:51.910
So their adaptability is
less about making stuff

00:26:51.910 --> 00:26:54.112
that kind of caters to people's tastes,

00:26:54.112 --> 00:26:56.548
and more like, "No
one's getting the wings,

00:26:56.548 --> 00:26:57.983
let's just do the nuggets.

00:26:57.983 --> 00:26:59.751
Let's take all this stuff off the menu,

00:26:59.751 --> 00:27:02.020
let's pare it down, go,
go, go," for efficiency,

00:27:02.020 --> 00:27:04.422
and probably because it's
cheaper to have less ingredients.

00:27:04.422 --> 00:27:08.259
So they've adapted to, I don't know,

00:27:08.259 --> 00:27:11.062
shifts in the market or
people's interest in KFC.

00:27:11.062 --> 00:27:13.898
They really don't deviate
too far, dish-wise,

00:27:13.898 --> 00:27:18.003
from, like, a fried chicken
or a chicken in a bun.

00:27:18.003 --> 00:27:20.472
KFC is actually the chain that has made

00:27:20.472 --> 00:27:23.341
the least effort to Italianize the menu.

00:27:23.341 --> 00:27:24.776
I don't know. Actually, weirdly,

00:27:24.776 --> 00:27:26.878
I think that for this it works,

00:27:26.878 --> 00:27:29.147
because the idea of eating fried chicken

00:27:29.147 --> 00:27:31.983
is so foreign to us that I
don't know how you would,

00:27:31.983 --> 00:27:33.585
how would you make that Italian?

00:27:33.585 --> 00:27:35.086
You'd maybe put some, like,

00:27:35.086 --> 00:27:37.989
fried courgette flowers with the chicken?

00:27:37.989 --> 00:27:38.990
I don't know.

00:27:38.990 --> 00:27:42.193
For me to even think about
a similar Italian thing,

00:27:42.193 --> 00:27:46.164
that, weirdly, I think this
may be working the way it is.

00:27:46.164 --> 00:27:49.734
So we'll see when they
will reach 100 branches.

00:27:49.734 --> 00:27:51.403
Maybe sooner than we think.

00:27:51.403 --> 00:27:53.371
Claudia: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:27:53.371 --> 00:27:55.340
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:27:55.340 --> 00:27:58.309
between McDonald's in the US and Italy.

00:27:58.309 --> 00:28:00.078
This is "Food Wars."

00:28:01.813 --> 00:28:04.649
Drinks at McDonald's in
Italy come in three sizes,

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:06.618
250 milliliters,

00:28:06.618 --> 00:28:08.019
400 milliliters,

00:28:08.019 --> 00:28:10.121
and 500 milliliters.

00:28:10.121 --> 00:28:11.122
We're now going to measure

00:28:11.122 --> 00:28:14.459
a 500-ml Coke to see if that's true.

00:28:14.459 --> 00:28:16.061
Oh, oh.

00:28:16.061 --> 00:28:17.829
I think we're surpassing that.

00:28:17.829 --> 00:28:21.566
It's just right below the 600 mark,

00:28:21.566 --> 00:28:23.068
but almost there.

00:28:23.068 --> 00:28:24.636
So quite generous.

00:28:24.636 --> 00:28:27.238
Drinks in the US also come in four sizes.

00:28:27.238 --> 00:28:30.341
The extra small, which is 355 milliliters,

00:28:30.341 --> 00:28:32.077
or 12 fluid ounces.

00:28:32.077 --> 00:28:36.414
The small, 474 milliliters,
or 16 fluid ounces.

00:28:36.414 --> 00:28:40.652
And the medium, 621
milliliters, or 21 fluid ounces.

00:28:40.652 --> 00:28:44.422
And the large, 946 milliliters,

00:28:44.422 --> 00:28:46.224
or 32 fluid ounces.

00:28:46.224 --> 00:28:50.462
Since we were the ones that
filled this up at the restaurant

00:28:50.462 --> 00:28:53.298
and I don't think we got it all full up,

00:28:53.298 --> 00:28:54.432
I'm going to go ahead and fill this

00:28:54.432 --> 00:28:56.968
what I think is reasonable.

00:28:56.968 --> 00:28:59.738
I can't do to the top
because the cap is recessed.

00:29:05.410 --> 00:29:08.646
OK. 32? Surely you jest.

00:29:08.646 --> 00:29:11.416
But there's the 32 line. Not even close.

00:29:11.416 --> 00:29:14.986
It's closer to 24 than it is 32.

00:29:14.986 --> 00:29:18.123
So, fries in Italy come in three sizes.

00:29:18.123 --> 00:29:21.159
The regular, which is
technically the small,

00:29:21.159 --> 00:29:22.927
medium, and large.

00:29:22.927 --> 00:29:25.897
Here in America, our
fries come in four sizes.

00:29:25.897 --> 00:29:28.466
The kids, which comes in the Happy Meal.

00:29:28.466 --> 00:29:29.968
Look at this little guy.

00:29:29.968 --> 00:29:30.869
Little guy!

00:29:30.869 --> 00:29:33.705
The small, the medium, and the large.

00:29:33.705 --> 00:29:35.306
All the "Food Wars" heads watching

00:29:35.306 --> 00:29:36.708
know that in the China episode,

00:29:36.708 --> 00:29:39.878
our large McDonald's fry was 175 grams.

00:29:39.878 --> 00:29:41.146
In the Japan episode,

00:29:41.146 --> 00:29:43.948
our large McDonald's fry was 190 grams.

00:29:43.948 --> 00:29:46.317
So clearly there's some
difference in grammage

00:29:46.317 --> 00:29:48.653
depending on, I don't know,
the McDonald's we go to,

00:29:48.653 --> 00:29:49.821
the scooper, who knows?

00:29:49.821 --> 00:29:52.891
So we're going to weigh
our large right now.

00:29:52.891 --> 00:29:54.726
Ready? Fantastic.

00:29:57.462 --> 00:29:59.864
Eh, let's go 185.

00:29:59.864 --> 00:30:02.634
Not a bad scoop. We got
a good scooper this time.

00:30:02.634 --> 00:30:04.402
Seems pretty small, actually.

00:30:04.402 --> 00:30:05.570
What about McNuggets?

00:30:05.570 --> 00:30:08.740
In Italy you can get a bag of four,

00:30:08.740 --> 00:30:10.708
a box of six pieces,

00:30:10.708 --> 00:30:13.645
nine pieces, and 20 pieces.

00:30:13.645 --> 00:30:14.846
Claudia, in the US,

00:30:14.846 --> 00:30:17.382
our McNuggets are
available in these sizes:

00:30:17.382 --> 00:30:20.685
the four-piece, the
six-piece, 10-piece, 20-piece,

00:30:20.685 --> 00:30:23.955
which you also have, but we go
up one more here in America.

00:30:23.955 --> 00:30:26.357
Our largest size, the 40-piece.

00:30:26.357 --> 00:30:28.693
Now, if my calculations are correct,

00:30:28.693 --> 00:30:31.563
this is double your largest size.

00:30:31.563 --> 00:30:33.832
The iconic Big Mac.
Both countries have it,

00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:37.235
but we're going to compare
ours to Italy's by weighing it.

00:30:37.235 --> 00:30:41.439
226 grams for a US Big Mac.

00:30:41.439 --> 00:30:42.974
And here is an Italian Big Mac,

00:30:42.974 --> 00:30:45.577
or Il Big Mac, as is written here,

00:30:45.577 --> 00:30:47.912
and we're going to weigh it now.

00:30:47.912 --> 00:30:49.547
209 grams.

00:30:51.416 --> 00:30:54.319
Here are all the items on
the McDonald's Italy menu

00:30:54.319 --> 00:30:56.120
that you won't find in the US.

00:30:56.120 --> 00:30:59.324
And here are all the McDonald's
menu items from the US

00:30:59.324 --> 00:31:01.292
you won't find in Italy.

00:31:01.292 --> 00:31:04.495
Get a good look, Claudia.

00:31:04.495 --> 00:31:06.064
Let's start from the burgers.

00:31:06.064 --> 00:31:08.466
We have a bunch of Italian burgers

00:31:08.466 --> 00:31:10.501
that you won't get in the US.

00:31:10.501 --> 00:31:13.538
The first one we got here
is a chicken Big Mac.

00:31:13.538 --> 00:31:17.108
Oh, right. Just destroyed chicken Big Mac.

00:31:17.108 --> 00:31:19.477
Has that been inverted?

00:31:19.477 --> 00:31:21.679
Is that supposed to look like this?

00:31:25.083 --> 00:31:27.752
The cheese helps a little
bit. Sauce as well.

00:31:27.752 --> 00:31:31.823
Moving on, we have a bacon Big Mac.

00:31:31.823 --> 00:31:34.092
Yeah, there's two strips of bacon,

00:31:34.092 --> 00:31:37.195
but they're not quite
big, so it does look like

00:31:37.195 --> 00:31:39.097
maybe it's just one
that's been cut in half.

00:31:39.097 --> 00:31:44.068
We got a crispy McBacon,
which is like cheeseburger,

00:31:44.068 --> 00:31:47.972
double patty, and some bacon
again, a bit on the side.

00:31:47.972 --> 00:31:50.808
It's funny actually because growing up,

00:31:50.808 --> 00:31:52.710
I thought that the crispy McBacon

00:31:52.710 --> 00:31:56.514
was the iconic McDonald's item,

00:31:56.514 --> 00:31:59.851
and it's weird that it is
actually an Italian exclusive.

00:31:59.851 --> 00:32:01.719
Here are all the burgers in the US

00:32:01.719 --> 00:32:02.887
that you can't get in Italy.

00:32:02.887 --> 00:32:04.956
Starting down here, the
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:32:04.956 --> 00:32:06.758
It really is just a cheeseburger

00:32:06.758 --> 00:32:09.327
that is a quarter pound of meat.

00:32:09.327 --> 00:32:10.662
It's a great go-to burger.

00:32:10.662 --> 00:32:15.133
Meat, cheese, onions,
pickles, ketchup, and mustard.

00:32:15.133 --> 00:32:16.634
And if you want more meat,

00:32:16.634 --> 00:32:18.303
you can get the double Quarter Pounder.

00:32:18.303 --> 00:32:20.271
Correct. Not the half pounder,

00:32:20.271 --> 00:32:22.907
the double Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:32:22.907 --> 00:32:25.910
Two patties, more meat, more cheese.

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:26.945
Fantastic sandwich.

00:32:26.945 --> 00:32:28.413
And then we've got the first one

00:32:28.413 --> 00:32:30.048
of the My Selection range,

00:32:30.048 --> 00:32:34.585
which is a range that was
designed with Joe Bastianich.

00:32:34.585 --> 00:32:37.855
He's an American TV personality and chef.

00:32:37.855 --> 00:32:42.660
This one is speck and Asiago,
so yeah, very traditional.

00:32:42.660 --> 00:32:46.898
Speck is a type of cured
meat. It's like a smoked ham.

00:32:46.898 --> 00:32:48.933
Yeah, it's a smoked ham
from the north of Italy.

00:32:48.933 --> 00:32:50.702
It's actually very, very nice,

00:32:50.702 --> 00:32:52.603
just very salty with that smoky flavor.

00:32:52.603 --> 00:32:54.238
It's one of my favorites.

00:32:54.238 --> 00:32:55.807
And then we have Asiago,

00:32:55.807 --> 00:32:58.876
which is a cheese made
pretty much in the same area.

00:32:58.876 --> 00:33:01.346
There's also mayo and zucchini in there.

00:33:04.382 --> 00:33:06.150
A bit dry, I think.

00:33:06.150 --> 00:33:08.953
You do taste the cold cut, the speck.

00:33:08.953 --> 00:33:11.456
Just brings that saltiness, smokiness.

00:33:11.456 --> 00:33:13.491
Very nice, and the cheese
also is quite good.

00:33:13.491 --> 00:33:14.792
Yeah, actually I don't
know if you've noticed,

00:33:14.792 --> 00:33:18.162
but it is much bigger than the others.

00:33:18.162 --> 00:33:21.332
You can even take, like, bacon Big Mac.

00:33:21.332 --> 00:33:23.101
Even though it's supposed
to have two patties,

00:33:23.101 --> 00:33:25.303
it is much bigger.

00:33:25.303 --> 00:33:28.139
And then we have another
My Selection burger.

00:33:28.139 --> 00:33:30.408
This one is called My BBQ.

00:33:30.408 --> 00:33:32.777
This one has got barbecue sauce,

00:33:32.777 --> 00:33:34.712
yes, I can see it,

00:33:34.712 --> 00:33:38.182
Gouda cheese, and bacon,

00:33:38.182 --> 00:33:42.120
and it's all topped off
with some balsamic vinegar.

00:33:42.120 --> 00:33:46.290
It does still have the
same sort of fancy patty

00:33:46.290 --> 00:33:48.393
that we had before.

00:33:48.393 --> 00:33:51.796
Right, and after these very
nice and fancy burgers,

00:33:51.796 --> 00:33:54.465
we have a gluten-free burger.

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:56.768
Oh. [record scratching]

00:33:56.768 --> 00:33:59.504
Wait, why does it come in a bag?

00:33:59.504 --> 00:34:03.541
Ooh. Yeah. Very -- ooh.

00:34:03.541 --> 00:34:05.043
Yeah, not excited about this.

00:34:05.043 --> 00:34:07.111
Just, I don't like the bread.

00:34:08.112 --> 00:34:10.415
I'm sure you can find
better gluten-free bread.

00:34:10.415 --> 00:34:12.050
There are so many around.

00:34:12.050 --> 00:34:15.720
And if you want vegetables on your burger

00:34:15.720 --> 00:34:17.088
for some strange reason,

00:34:17.088 --> 00:34:20.324
you can get the Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe,

00:34:20.324 --> 00:34:24.262
with lettuce and tomato and mayo.

00:34:24.262 --> 00:34:26.297
Oh, did you see that squirt coming out?

00:34:26.297 --> 00:34:27.732
Hit, like, a pocket of
mayonnaise on that one.

00:34:27.732 --> 00:34:28.800
That's kind of weird.

00:34:28.800 --> 00:34:29.634
It tastes great.

00:34:29.634 --> 00:34:31.069
And if you just want to
go all in on the meat,

00:34:31.069 --> 00:34:35.273
you can get a double
Quarter Pounder with bacon.

00:34:35.273 --> 00:34:36.908
Look at this.

00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:37.742
Right?

00:34:40.244 --> 00:34:41.646
It's really good. Enough said.

00:34:41.646 --> 00:34:44.248
And, surprise, another thing on our menu

00:34:44.248 --> 00:34:46.951
you guys don't have: the McDouble.

00:34:46.951 --> 00:34:48.619
McDonald's has a double cheeseburger,

00:34:48.619 --> 00:34:50.321
which is double the
meat, double the cheese,

00:34:50.321 --> 00:34:52.490
but also there's a McDouble on the menu.

00:34:52.490 --> 00:34:53.624
What's the difference, you ask?

00:34:53.624 --> 00:34:56.461
Well, McDouble only has
one slice of cheese.

00:34:56.461 --> 00:34:58.830
As you can see from here, on top,

00:34:58.830 --> 00:35:02.633
you got ketchup, mustard,
and pickles, no cheese.

00:35:02.633 --> 00:35:04.669
The cheese is in between here.

00:35:04.669 --> 00:35:06.637
I get it. Times are tough in this economy,

00:35:06.637 --> 00:35:09.874
but get the extra slice
of cheese, guys. Come on.

00:35:09.874 --> 00:35:11.075
I mean, we're not robots here.

00:35:11.075 --> 00:35:13.144
We gotta have some pleasure in our lives,

00:35:13.144 --> 00:35:16.080
and I think you should get
that extra slice of cheese.

00:35:16.080 --> 00:35:18.483
Absorb the cost of it.
It's perfectly fine.

00:35:18.483 --> 00:35:20.885
You're doing great. Come on!

00:35:20.885 --> 00:35:23.554
Next one is another one
of those My Selection.

00:35:23.554 --> 00:35:28.226
It's a chicken, avocado, and bacon burger.

00:35:28.226 --> 00:35:30.928
Hm, it's got a different bun, this one.

00:35:30.928 --> 00:35:32.630
Ooh, fancy.

00:35:32.630 --> 00:35:34.465
All right, yeah, avocado is there.

00:35:34.465 --> 00:35:35.933
There's, like, cabbage.

00:35:35.933 --> 00:35:37.635
Mm, bit less excited about that.

00:35:37.635 --> 00:35:41.772
And this one has
caciocavallo Silano cheese.

00:35:41.772 --> 00:35:43.241
I don't know. We can call this --

00:35:43.241 --> 00:35:45.810
you know sauce talk. The cheese talk.

00:35:45.810 --> 00:35:50.214
Caciocavallo comes from the
same family of mozzarella.

00:35:50.214 --> 00:35:52.183
They're called pasta filata cheeses,

00:35:52.183 --> 00:35:55.553
and it's just basically the
way that you make cheese,

00:35:55.553 --> 00:35:58.456
when you split the milk
into curds and whey.

00:35:58.456 --> 00:35:59.857
It's made in a different way.

00:35:59.857 --> 00:36:02.160
And you could say that caciocavallo

00:36:02.160 --> 00:36:04.162
is like an aged mozzarella.

00:36:04.162 --> 00:36:05.897
So it's a very versatile cheese

00:36:05.897 --> 00:36:08.799
that I think is not
very well known abroad.

00:36:08.799 --> 00:36:11.869
So, yeah, thank you, McDonald's,
for making that a thing

00:36:11.869 --> 00:36:14.005
on your menu so everybody
can know about it.

00:36:14.005 --> 00:36:18.376
So, here's the cheese that we
were talking about. [laughs]

00:36:18.376 --> 00:36:19.644
It's just always a shame.

00:36:19.644 --> 00:36:24.182
It's been put there with,
like, avocado and this cabbage.

00:36:24.182 --> 00:36:28.186
Next one, we've got
double chicken barbecue.

00:36:28.186 --> 00:36:30.855
After seeing all these big
ones, they do look quite small.

00:36:30.855 --> 00:36:32.823
And then we have a chicken burger.

00:36:32.823 --> 00:36:34.992
This one is different from a McChicken

00:36:34.992 --> 00:36:39.230
because it has Caesar
sauce and no lettuce.

00:36:39.230 --> 00:36:41.465
I think this is glue.

00:36:41.465 --> 00:36:42.900
It looks like -- there is a type of glue

00:36:42.900 --> 00:36:44.802
that looks exactly like that.

00:36:44.802 --> 00:36:48.673
We also thought it'd be
fun to compare Happy Meals.

00:36:48.673 --> 00:36:50.775
Here's the US one.

00:36:50.775 --> 00:36:52.743
Open up this box, take a look around.

00:36:52.743 --> 00:36:54.378
I'm pretty sure this is Pokémon.

00:36:54.378 --> 00:36:56.948
This one comes with kid fries,

00:36:56.948 --> 00:36:58.983
nuggets, which, we got a six-piece,

00:36:58.983 --> 00:37:01.552
and this is their Pokémon toy.

00:37:01.552 --> 00:37:02.386
So, they get the six-piece.

00:37:02.386 --> 00:37:03.621
It's funny, like, a six-piece still seems

00:37:03.621 --> 00:37:05.056
kind of like a lot for a kid.

00:37:05.056 --> 00:37:07.158
Pokémon-themed toys
coming at you these days.

00:37:07.158 --> 00:37:08.259
What is this?

00:37:09.227 --> 00:37:12.496
OK, so we got Pikachu.

00:37:12.496 --> 00:37:14.732
Does this have any value?
Because there's rare ones.

00:37:14.732 --> 00:37:16.067
There's ones that have
a lot of value to them.

00:37:16.067 --> 00:37:18.536
But not the ones at McDonald's, right?

00:37:18.536 --> 00:37:20.671
Cyclizar? Any value?

00:37:22.340 --> 00:37:25.276
We got Tandemaus.

00:37:28.079 --> 00:37:29.046
Yeah.

00:37:29.046 --> 00:37:33.584
And, of course, Sandaconda.

00:37:34.552 --> 00:37:36.454
I'll go look on eBay after this

00:37:36.454 --> 00:37:38.589
and see if these are worth anything.

00:37:38.589 --> 00:37:41.359
Culturally, I have no idea what this is.

00:37:41.359 --> 00:37:42.860
I don't know what -- this is a thing?

00:37:45.196 --> 00:37:46.631
No, I have no idea who.

00:37:49.400 --> 00:37:51.469
I don't remember any of those names.

00:37:54.038 --> 00:37:56.440
Charlizard?

00:37:56.440 --> 00:37:57.808
Cylizard?

00:37:57.808 --> 00:38:00.244
Is this Cylizard?

00:38:00.244 --> 00:38:01.746
Charmagarg.

00:38:03.381 --> 00:38:04.215
OK.

00:38:04.215 --> 00:38:07.051
In a Happy Meal in Italy,
you can find four items.

00:38:07.051 --> 00:38:10.454
Obviously there is a drink,
then there is a main course

00:38:10.454 --> 00:38:13.457
that could be either
nuggets [or] a hamburger.

00:38:13.457 --> 00:38:16.360
And exclusive to Italy is a chicken burger

00:38:16.360 --> 00:38:19.430
and a McToast, which is what we got today.

00:38:19.430 --> 00:38:20.865
We're going to see that in a moment.

00:38:20.865 --> 00:38:21.932
Then there is a side.

00:38:21.932 --> 00:38:25.002
It can either be fries or baby carrots.

00:38:25.002 --> 00:38:26.370
And a dessert.

00:38:26.370 --> 00:38:30.675
This can be either fresh fruit, Actimel,

00:38:30.675 --> 00:38:34.045
which is technically a drink
but it's a dessert here,

00:38:34.045 --> 00:38:35.746
and Parmesan.

00:38:35.746 --> 00:38:40.184
Here's our McToast. Nice.

00:38:40.184 --> 00:38:43.954
The surprise of the day.

00:38:43.954 --> 00:38:47.291
Yeah, they're just doing some
Hot Wheels collaboration.

00:38:47.291 --> 00:38:49.560
So let's have a look at what is it.

00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:52.430
I don't know, do you think
I can find a Vespa in here?

00:38:52.430 --> 00:38:56.867
Oh, cute little skateboard,

00:38:56.867 --> 00:38:57.702
pink one.

00:38:58.536 --> 00:39:00.004
Nyoom.

00:39:00.004 --> 00:39:03.507
We also have one exclusive
wrap option here in Italy.

00:39:03.507 --> 00:39:06.344
It's a McWrap with crisp chicken breast

00:39:06.344 --> 00:39:09.013
and Parmesan, or Parmigiano-Reggiano.

00:39:09.013 --> 00:39:11.582
It's made in collaboration
with Giallozafferano,

00:39:11.582 --> 00:39:15.619
which is the No. 1
recipe website in Italy.

00:39:15.619 --> 00:39:19.190
To be honest, I think
they could have come up

00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:22.426
with a better recipe, maybe, for the wrap.

00:39:22.426 --> 00:39:25.996
The wrap does look very
sad, just the actual bread.

00:39:25.996 --> 00:39:27.498
Chicken looks OK.

00:39:27.498 --> 00:39:29.433
Italy clearly has plenty of exclusive

00:39:29.433 --> 00:39:32.169
chicken-sandwich options, but
we have a few of our own here,

00:39:32.169 --> 00:39:35.306
namely the McCrispy and the spicy McCrispy

00:39:35.306 --> 00:39:37.808
and a deluxe version of each sandwich.

00:39:37.808 --> 00:39:38.642
Let's take a look.

00:39:38.642 --> 00:39:40.778
It looks closer to a chicken sandwich

00:39:40.778 --> 00:39:42.747
you would find at a Chick-fil-A,

00:39:42.747 --> 00:39:47.251
and then now Burger King has
the chicken king, I think?

00:39:47.251 --> 00:39:50.621
McDonald's did all the
research that they do

00:39:50.621 --> 00:39:54.525
to release this, the McCrispy sandwich.

00:39:54.525 --> 00:39:57.695
Now, as you can tell,
it's just pickles on here.

00:39:57.695 --> 00:40:02.066
A crispier, more natural-looking
piece of fried chicken,

00:40:02.066 --> 00:40:05.503
and no sauce. Does it
always have no sauce?

00:40:08.139 --> 00:40:09.974
I don't like that. I don't like
a place that gives you food

00:40:09.974 --> 00:40:12.710
and, like, assembly requirements.

00:40:13.544 --> 00:40:15.045
For the most part, I
should get the sandwich

00:40:15.045 --> 00:40:15.880
the way it's supposed to be.

00:40:15.880 --> 00:40:17.481
So this put your own sauce in it,

00:40:17.481 --> 00:40:18.783
it's like, no, you put it on.

00:40:18.783 --> 00:40:20.985
Here's the deluxe of it.

00:40:22.186 --> 00:40:24.155
Yay, it has mayo. Whoa.

00:40:24.155 --> 00:40:25.956
This to me is like,
yeah, do this every time.

00:40:25.956 --> 00:40:27.591
This should just be the
sandwich. I don't ...

00:40:30.861 --> 00:40:33.631
If you're like me and
you want to spice it up,

00:40:33.631 --> 00:40:34.832
ah,

00:40:36.434 --> 00:40:39.003
they have the spicy -- oh, come on.

00:40:39.003 --> 00:40:40.938
There's spicy sauce on here somewhere.

00:40:40.938 --> 00:40:44.542
Then, of course, they
got the spicy deluxe,

00:40:44.542 --> 00:40:46.143
which of course has spicy sauce

00:40:46.143 --> 00:40:47.111
and all those veggies in there.

00:40:47.111 --> 00:40:49.613
So, yeah. McDonald's, still a contender

00:40:49.613 --> 00:40:51.549
in the chicken-sandwich game, I feel.

00:40:51.549 --> 00:40:54.885
Now we're on to the exclusive
sides here in Italy.

00:40:54.885 --> 00:40:58.355
The first one that we got is cheesy fries.

00:40:58.355 --> 00:41:01.926
The same fry, just with a
bit more bacon we got here.

00:41:01.926 --> 00:41:04.929
Yeah, cheddar and bacon.

00:41:04.929 --> 00:41:06.664
This is, like, I don't know,

00:41:06.664 --> 00:41:09.900
a very sad Italian take on poutine.

00:41:09.900 --> 00:41:13.637
On the menu next for sides,
we've got panzerotti.

00:41:13.637 --> 00:41:17.274
So, actually very excited
about these because,

00:41:17.274 --> 00:41:19.743
ooh,

00:41:19.743 --> 00:41:22.046
panzerotti are from my hometown,

00:41:22.046 --> 00:41:23.614
Bari, in the south of Italy.

00:41:23.614 --> 00:41:25.983
The main difference is
that usually panzerotti,

00:41:25.983 --> 00:41:28.385
the traditional ones, they are this big.

00:41:28.385 --> 00:41:31.288
They're usually pretty wide.
It's, like, a main meal.

00:41:31.288 --> 00:41:34.124
Panzerotti normally, they
have, tomatoes and mozzarella

00:41:34.124 --> 00:41:38.329
is the most common filling,
but in Bari, again,

00:41:38.329 --> 00:41:42.233
where they are from, you can
get them with ground beef,

00:41:42.233 --> 00:41:44.201
mozzarella, and cooked ham.

00:41:44.201 --> 00:41:46.170
These are actually my favorites.

00:41:46.170 --> 00:41:48.939
I used to go and get them after school.

00:41:50.140 --> 00:41:52.042
That's just, they are the perfect snack.

00:41:55.846 --> 00:41:57.381
Quite good, actually.

00:41:57.381 --> 00:41:59.817
Filling is OK, but I
think a real panzerotto,

00:41:59.817 --> 00:42:01.919
when you bite into it,

00:42:01.919 --> 00:42:04.522
basically all the filling
should almost come out.

00:42:04.522 --> 00:42:06.123
It should, like, pop.

00:42:06.123 --> 00:42:07.892
Like, the first reaction
when you eat a panzerotti,

00:42:07.892 --> 00:42:09.426
this is like,

00:42:09.426 --> 00:42:11.629
and then you sort of put your hand here

00:42:11.629 --> 00:42:14.198
and just avoid a complete mess.

00:42:14.198 --> 00:42:15.966
This brings us to the next snack,

00:42:15.966 --> 00:42:19.637
which is Parmigiano-Reggiano, or Parmesan.

00:42:19.637 --> 00:42:21.739
This is one of the most
counterfeit cheeses

00:42:21.739 --> 00:42:23.674
in the world, so.

00:42:23.674 --> 00:42:25.709
In Italy but also in Europe,

00:42:25.709 --> 00:42:27.678
because of this whole protection thing,

00:42:27.678 --> 00:42:30.581
anything that's called even
Parmesan, not the real name,

00:42:30.581 --> 00:42:33.384
Parmigiano-Reggiano, is
in fact the real thing,

00:42:33.384 --> 00:42:35.986
so at least we are safe on that side.

00:42:35.986 --> 00:42:39.156
Having said that, I think
most of the Parmesan,

00:42:39.156 --> 00:42:43.894
Parmigiano that you will
find around in supermarkets,

00:42:43.894 --> 00:42:46.030
it's been aged for the bare minimum,

00:42:46.030 --> 00:42:47.398
which is 12 months.

00:42:47.398 --> 00:42:48.899
So it is good, it is the real thing,

00:42:48.899 --> 00:42:50.334
but if you can choose,

00:42:50.334 --> 00:42:53.938
just have something that's
been aged for a bit longer.

00:42:53.938 --> 00:42:55.873
I think in Italy we do eat a lot of cheese

00:42:55.873 --> 00:43:00.277
as a snack as it is, and I
do have definitely memories

00:43:00.277 --> 00:43:01.845
of me coming back from school

00:43:01.845 --> 00:43:04.515
and then just in the afternoon grabbing

00:43:04.515 --> 00:43:05.983
some cheese off the fridge

00:43:05.983 --> 00:43:09.853
and having a couple of slices
or even more than that.

00:43:09.853 --> 00:43:11.088
I think my mom still does that,

00:43:11.088 --> 00:43:13.857
so, sorry for exposing you, Mom.

00:43:17.328 --> 00:43:18.596
Love it.

00:43:18.596 --> 00:43:21.699
Over here we got another exclusive.

00:43:21.699 --> 00:43:24.802
There are actually three
salads on the menu.

00:43:24.802 --> 00:43:28.305
One is just a plain salad,
one is a salad with tomatoes,

00:43:28.305 --> 00:43:31.842
and then we got one with crispy
chicken breast and Parmesan.

00:43:31.842 --> 00:43:36.013
We could also select a dressing,
and we added olive oil.

00:43:36.013 --> 00:43:39.016
You could also get a tiny
bottle of balsamic vinegar

00:43:39.016 --> 00:43:40.784
or just vinegar.

00:43:40.784 --> 00:43:44.088
We actually have no
exclusive sides in the US.

00:43:44.088 --> 00:43:47.057
Every side option on our menu
can also be found in Italy.

00:43:47.057 --> 00:43:48.792
I will say, though, I love that they have

00:43:48.792 --> 00:43:52.496
a stick of cheese as a side,
kind of like a palate cleanser.

00:43:52.496 --> 00:43:53.530
I would love that.

00:43:53.530 --> 00:43:56.433
I would love to snack on cheese.
I love snacking on cheese.

00:43:56.433 --> 00:43:58.702
We should have more cheese,
is what I'm trying to say.

00:43:58.702 --> 00:44:00.537
We can bring it back with the sauces.

00:44:00.537 --> 00:44:03.440
It's time for sauce talk, Italy edition.

00:44:03.440 --> 00:44:05.943
La la la sauce talk!

00:44:06.810 --> 00:44:08.779
That had to offend somebody.

00:44:08.779 --> 00:44:10.447
Sauce talk.

00:44:10.447 --> 00:44:13.083
We have several exclusive sauces

00:44:13.083 --> 00:44:17.054
here in the United States,
including spicy Buffalo,

00:44:17.054 --> 00:44:21.625
and then we have ranch, honey
mustard, sweet 'n' sour.

00:44:21.625 --> 00:44:24.395
Now, I have two because one

00:44:24.395 --> 00:44:26.597
is from the movie "Loki," apparently.

00:44:26.597 --> 00:44:28.766
And of course you just get honey.

00:44:28.766 --> 00:44:31.802
Of all these, I'd probably
go sweet 'n' sour,

00:44:31.802 --> 00:44:34.672
but barbecue, which they
do have, is my favorite.

00:44:34.672 --> 00:44:37.975
We have one exclusive sauce in Italy,

00:44:37.975 --> 00:44:41.145
which is spicy mustard sauce.

00:44:41.145 --> 00:44:41.979
Yeah.

00:44:45.849 --> 00:44:48.252
Yeah, it is a bit spicy.

00:44:48.252 --> 00:44:51.355
Not so much, though.
Doesn't numb your tongue.

00:44:51.355 --> 00:44:54.525
I think actually it has a sweet
aftertaste for some reason.

00:44:54.525 --> 00:44:55.926
For the early risers,

00:44:55.926 --> 00:44:58.195
there are plenty of
exclusive breakfast items

00:44:58.195 --> 00:45:01.932
at the US McDonald's,
and they're all savory.

00:45:01.932 --> 00:45:04.535
Now, first thing I'm going to
talk about are the biscuits.

00:45:04.535 --> 00:45:07.037
I'm not the person to
describe American biscuits

00:45:07.037 --> 00:45:09.807
to the rest of the world.
They should have hired a poet.

00:45:09.807 --> 00:45:12.910
This is the bacon, egg,
and cheese biscuit,

00:45:12.910 --> 00:45:14.445
but you can get a biscuit version

00:45:14.445 --> 00:45:18.215
of any meat or cheese
combination that you want.

00:45:18.215 --> 00:45:20.017
In the middle here, though,

00:45:20.017 --> 00:45:23.353
Italy, Claudia, everyone,

00:45:23.353 --> 00:45:24.555
look at what I'm about to show you.

00:45:24.555 --> 00:45:26.957
You know what pancakes are.
You know what syrup is.

00:45:26.957 --> 00:45:29.026
You obviously know what
breakfast sandwiches are.

00:45:29.026 --> 00:45:31.228
This right here is a McGriddle,

00:45:31.228 --> 00:45:33.664
and they replaced the buns with this.

00:45:33.664 --> 00:45:35.232
These bun pancakes.

00:45:35.232 --> 00:45:37.868
This is a pancake, Italy. A pancake.

00:45:37.868 --> 00:45:42.206
These, here. And they somehow
injected syrup in them,

00:45:42.206 --> 00:45:44.475
so it's not like syrup like a sauce,

00:45:44.475 --> 00:45:47.578
it's just, like, already syrup somehow,

00:45:47.578 --> 00:45:50.214
and it is savory and
sweet at the same time.

00:45:50.214 --> 00:45:52.216
It is so delicious.

00:45:52.216 --> 00:45:54.818
It's a McGriddle. It's
fantastic. I love these.

00:45:54.818 --> 00:45:56.386
This is a bacon, egg,
and cheese McGriddle,

00:45:56.386 --> 00:45:59.490
but once again, you can get
it in any various sausage,

00:45:59.490 --> 00:46:02.126
egg, and/or cheese
combination that you want.

00:46:02.126 --> 00:46:03.660
McGriddles. Check 'em out.

00:46:03.660 --> 00:46:06.096
I am the McGriddle No. 1 fan over here.

00:46:06.096 --> 00:46:10.801
And the OG breakfast sandwich,
this is the egg McMuffin.

00:46:10.801 --> 00:46:13.337
They got the Big Breakfast
with or without hotcakes.

00:46:13.337 --> 00:46:14.538
I went with hotcakes.

00:46:14.538 --> 00:46:19.076
You got eggs, bacon,
pancakes, English muffin,

00:46:19.076 --> 00:46:20.344
this thing's fantastic.

00:46:20.344 --> 00:46:24.214
And if you want to just
get hotcakes and sausage,

00:46:24.214 --> 00:46:25.249
you can also do that.

00:46:25.249 --> 00:46:28.786
And each order of pancakes

00:46:28.786 --> 00:46:32.055
comes with our hotcakes syrup.

00:46:32.055 --> 00:46:36.560
I think an unsung hero of the
McDonald's breakfast menu,

00:46:36.560 --> 00:46:39.229
been a fan of this for years,

00:46:39.229 --> 00:46:42.132
it is the sausage breakfast burrito.

00:46:42.132 --> 00:46:44.334
Now, let's be honest.

00:46:44.334 --> 00:46:45.803
Italy, in case you're wondering,

00:46:45.803 --> 00:46:50.507
this in no way represents
an actual burrito.

00:46:50.507 --> 00:46:52.276
I want to make that perfectly clear.

00:46:52.276 --> 00:46:53.811
I would not put this in the same category

00:46:53.811 --> 00:46:56.613
as any sort of burrito,
breakfast or otherwise,

00:46:56.613 --> 00:47:00.684
but it's its own thing, and
I think it is fantastic.

00:47:00.684 --> 00:47:04.555
It is in a flour tortilla.

00:47:04.555 --> 00:47:07.191
Scrambled eggs, sausage, yes, I know,

00:47:07.191 --> 00:47:11.929
peppers, cheese, and the secret weapon

00:47:13.831 --> 00:47:15.699
is this, their Mexican-style salsa.

00:47:15.699 --> 00:47:20.604
Again, there is nothing
authentically Mexican about this,

00:47:20.604 --> 00:47:23.674
but it tastes great.

00:47:23.674 --> 00:47:25.576
This was a go-to for years.

00:47:25.576 --> 00:47:27.744
I could put away about four of these.

00:47:30.614 --> 00:47:32.850
McDonald's also does offer oatmeal,

00:47:32.850 --> 00:47:35.853
specifically fruit and maple oatmeal.

00:47:35.853 --> 00:47:36.720
Moving on.

00:47:36.720 --> 00:47:40.324
The Italian McDonald's
also sells breakfast items.

00:47:40.324 --> 00:47:42.960
We've got ... [laughs]

00:47:42.960 --> 00:47:44.728
That's super sad.

00:47:44.728 --> 00:47:48.365
We got scrambled eggs with
bacon and a muffin and bread,

00:47:48.365 --> 00:47:50.567
which does look more like a muffin.

00:47:50.567 --> 00:47:53.737
And then we have a McMuffin
with bacon and egg.

00:47:53.737 --> 00:47:56.240
Yeah, Italians don't really
have savory breakfast.

00:47:56.240 --> 00:47:58.775
It's definitely a habit.

00:47:58.775 --> 00:48:03.046
Like, you just associate
breakfast with sweet items.

00:48:03.046 --> 00:48:06.817
All right, US also has their
own exclusive McCafé items.

00:48:08.085 --> 00:48:10.420
Where'd they go?

00:48:10.420 --> 00:48:13.423
The McDonald'ses near our studio

00:48:13.423 --> 00:48:16.460
did not have the McCafé food items.

00:48:24.268 --> 00:48:26.536
McDonald's in Italy has
really made an effort

00:48:26.536 --> 00:48:29.239
with the McCafé menu items,

00:48:29.239 --> 00:48:33.043
and there are really a lot
of items on the menu here.

00:48:33.043 --> 00:48:34.845
So let's start from the croissants.

00:48:34.845 --> 00:48:36.613
We've got quite a few on the menu.

00:48:36.613 --> 00:48:39.516
I think this one here,

00:48:39.516 --> 00:48:41.685
because you can see a little bit of brown,

00:48:41.685 --> 00:48:45.455
this is the cocoa one with sourdough.

00:48:48.959 --> 00:48:50.861
Pretty safe to eat.

00:48:50.861 --> 00:48:52.362
This is the plain one.

00:48:52.362 --> 00:48:55.365
Does look more like a
French-style croissant.

00:48:55.365 --> 00:48:58.902
Nice layers in there as well, some air.

00:48:58.902 --> 00:49:02.139
Over here, it's quite hard to tell,

00:49:02.139 --> 00:49:05.108
but there is a subtle,
subtle layer of jam.

00:49:05.108 --> 00:49:08.779
This is berries and cereal.

00:49:08.779 --> 00:49:11.615
So, the dough, it's a little bit stiffer,

00:49:11.615 --> 00:49:16.386
and, yeah, does smell a little bit

00:49:16.386 --> 00:49:18.388
more like cereals.

00:49:18.388 --> 00:49:22.159
Same amount of jam as in the others.

00:49:22.159 --> 00:49:24.394
Not very generous, actually.

00:49:24.394 --> 00:49:26.763
I think this one is the
last one that we got,

00:49:26.763 --> 00:49:27.931
so it's the custard.

00:49:27.931 --> 00:49:32.135
This looks like we have
a bit more in there.

00:49:32.135 --> 00:49:33.136
Obviously, it's hard to tell

00:49:33.136 --> 00:49:37.941
because the custard is the
same color as the dough,

00:49:37.941 --> 00:49:40.677
has kind of turned the dough yellow.

00:49:43.246 --> 00:49:46.016
Nice. Lots of lemon in there.

00:49:46.016 --> 00:49:47.985
Another pastry option that you can get

00:49:47.985 --> 00:49:50.487
is this cream braid.

00:49:50.487 --> 00:49:54.024
This is quite a typical
thing as well in Italy.

00:49:54.024 --> 00:49:56.927
Like, you do get these kind of pastries.

00:49:56.927 --> 00:50:00.163
You can get them also savory
in different regions of Italy.

00:50:00.163 --> 00:50:02.599
Let's see if they were
generous with the cream here.

00:50:02.599 --> 00:50:05.335
Mm, yeah, I'll say so.

00:50:07.137 --> 00:50:08.438
I prefer this cream.

00:50:08.438 --> 00:50:11.575
In Italy, you can also get some cakes.

00:50:11.575 --> 00:50:16.079
We have tiramisu, which is,
yeah, traditional Italian thing,

00:50:16.079 --> 00:50:17.681
but not a breakfast item.

00:50:17.681 --> 00:50:20.517
Like, I wouldn't really have
breakfast with tiramisu.

00:50:20.517 --> 00:50:24.855
I know you guys want to hear
the opinion of an Italian,

00:50:24.855 --> 00:50:29.092
so we're going to try this
tiramisu and see if it's proper.

00:50:31.194 --> 00:50:32.796
Yes, quite good, actually.

00:50:32.796 --> 00:50:35.632
We do have other cakes as well.

00:50:35.632 --> 00:50:39.536
We have this one, which is
torta della nonna in Italian,

00:50:39.536 --> 00:50:41.405
and that literally translates to

00:50:41.405 --> 00:50:43.740
"grandma's cake" in English.

00:50:43.740 --> 00:50:46.977
This one has lemon custard and pine nuts.

00:50:48.745 --> 00:50:49.813
I think it's a bit of a joke

00:50:49.813 --> 00:50:51.782
that this is actually
called grandma's cake

00:50:51.782 --> 00:50:54.084
just because every Italian grandma

00:50:54.084 --> 00:50:56.219
that's good in the kitchen
will be able to make something,

00:50:56.219 --> 00:50:58.688
like, 100 times better than this.

00:50:58.688 --> 00:51:01.758
We've got a strawberry cheesecake.

00:51:01.758 --> 00:51:06.029
Let's move on to this
three-layer chocolate cake.

00:51:06.029 --> 00:51:07.964
It's an absolute beast.

00:51:11.601 --> 00:51:12.736
It's a bit too much.

00:51:12.736 --> 00:51:15.072
I wouldn't have this for breakfast.

00:51:15.072 --> 00:51:17.541
And then we have a few more items here

00:51:17.541 --> 00:51:19.042
at the McCafé in Italy.

00:51:19.042 --> 00:51:22.612
We have a marshmallow doughnut,

00:51:22.612 --> 00:51:25.315
which looks like the most artificial thing

00:51:25.315 --> 00:51:26.917
I've ever seen.

00:51:26.917 --> 00:51:29.386
Then we've got a Nutella muffin.

00:51:29.386 --> 00:51:31.388
It is true that Italians love Nutella,

00:51:31.388 --> 00:51:33.590
and they eat it all the time.

00:51:33.590 --> 00:51:36.293
Again, when I was a child,
my parents used to hide it.

00:51:38.028 --> 00:51:41.031
Mm, sad. [laughs]

00:51:41.031 --> 00:51:45.268
And the last item that
we've got is macarons.

00:51:45.268 --> 00:51:48.105
We have chocolate macarons,
raspberry macarons,

00:51:48.105 --> 00:51:50.107
and pistachios macarons,

00:51:50.107 --> 00:51:52.375
or pistacchio, as we do say here.

00:51:55.846 --> 00:51:59.583
Oh, the inside is, like,

00:51:59.583 --> 00:52:01.651
dangerously green.

00:52:01.651 --> 00:52:04.187
They don't taste so much
like pistachio, to be honest.

00:52:04.187 --> 00:52:06.189
Desserts, McDonald's US,

00:52:06.189 --> 00:52:08.058
we have these exclusives.

00:52:08.058 --> 00:52:10.594
Starting down here, the baked apple pie.

00:52:10.594 --> 00:52:11.862
The day they stopped frying these

00:52:11.862 --> 00:52:13.096
is the day I stopped eating them.

00:52:13.096 --> 00:52:14.698
Now they're pulling this with, like,

00:52:14.698 --> 00:52:16.633
trying to make it look like
it's a homemade pastry.

00:52:16.633 --> 00:52:19.669
It's not. This was just spit out

00:52:19.669 --> 00:52:23.306
of an AI oven machine.

00:52:23.306 --> 00:52:27.177
Blip, blip, blip. One a second. No human.

00:52:27.177 --> 00:52:29.312
I'm the first human hand to touch this.

00:52:29.312 --> 00:52:31.081
Also chocolate chip cookies.

00:52:31.081 --> 00:52:34.584
They come in orders of
one, three, the trilogy,

00:52:34.584 --> 00:52:36.486
or a tote of 13.

00:52:36.486 --> 00:52:38.321
One good thing about the
McDonald's we went to today

00:52:38.321 --> 00:52:41.057
is the McFlurry machine
was totally working,

00:52:41.057 --> 00:52:43.994
and I got this one, the M&amp;M's McFlurry.

00:52:43.994 --> 00:52:45.128
We use the mini M&amp;M's,

00:52:45.128 --> 00:52:46.396
which are better than regular M&amp;M's,

00:52:46.396 --> 00:52:47.664
I don't know why, they just are.

00:52:47.664 --> 00:52:50.767
Sundaes, sundaes, sundaes.

00:52:50.767 --> 00:52:53.103
Maybe my favorite as a
kid, the caramel sundae.

00:52:54.171 --> 00:52:57.307
Mm. Ooh, that's my childhood right there.

00:52:57.307 --> 00:52:59.476
And you can get a fudge one as well.

00:52:59.476 --> 00:53:01.144
For Italian exclusive desserts,

00:53:01.144 --> 00:53:04.447
we have a pistachios McFlurry,

00:53:04.447 --> 00:53:06.683
then a Baci Perugina McFlurry.

00:53:06.683 --> 00:53:10.954
Baci Perugina are very popular chocolates.

00:53:10.954 --> 00:53:13.790
They are made in Perugia, which
is in the center of Italy,

00:53:13.790 --> 00:53:15.225
a town in the center.

00:53:15.225 --> 00:53:18.028
And here we have a coffee sundae.

00:53:18.028 --> 00:53:21.364
It's quite nice that they
actually gave us the espresso

00:53:21.364 --> 00:53:23.066
so that we can make our own.

00:53:23.066 --> 00:53:24.634
A bit like an affogato, in a way.

00:53:24.634 --> 00:53:27.037
The other sundaes are caramel, berries,

00:53:27.037 --> 00:53:30.273
another Baci Perugina again,
and the fior di latte,

00:53:30.273 --> 00:53:33.243
which is basically the
Italian version of vanilla.

00:53:34.311 --> 00:53:35.145
Ooh.

00:53:38.181 --> 00:53:39.783
Nice, yeah.

00:53:39.783 --> 00:53:42.786
Now on to the cold drink
options, starting down here,

00:53:42.786 --> 00:53:44.421
all the soda options
you get here in the US.

00:53:44.421 --> 00:53:47.190
Of course, we have way more than Italy.

00:53:47.190 --> 00:53:49.626
Starting with Dr Pepper.

00:53:49.626 --> 00:53:50.860
Oh, OK there.

00:53:52.295 --> 00:53:53.296
So fantastic.

00:53:53.296 --> 00:53:55.265
Diet Coke. No.

00:53:56.633 --> 00:53:57.467
Ugh.

00:53:57.467 --> 00:54:00.403
This completely unnatural-looking thing

00:54:00.403 --> 00:54:03.240
is Hi-C Orange Lavaburst.

00:54:03.240 --> 00:54:06.743
It's not carbonated,
but it's also not juice.

00:54:06.743 --> 00:54:09.379
I can't explain it. It's Hi-C.

00:54:10.513 --> 00:54:12.415
You can also get a sweet tea

00:54:12.415 --> 00:54:15.785
and an unsweetened iced tea at McDonald's.

00:54:15.785 --> 00:54:17.087
What I did feel like getting was this,

00:54:17.087 --> 00:54:19.522
the frozen Fanta blue raspberry.

00:54:21.124 --> 00:54:23.760
Oh, God, it's so sweet and so syrupy.

00:54:23.760 --> 00:54:25.829
Don't drink this, don't
give it to children,

00:54:25.829 --> 00:54:27.063
don't have it ever.

00:54:27.063 --> 00:54:28.732
They also have a Coke
version, frozen Coke.

00:54:28.732 --> 00:54:30.166
Also don't bother.

00:54:30.166 --> 00:54:31.668
Lemonade, though.

00:54:31.668 --> 00:54:33.503
So, we found out that lemonade in America

00:54:33.503 --> 00:54:35.438
is the least different
from lemonade in the UK.

00:54:35.438 --> 00:54:37.340
Again, this is not carbonated,

00:54:37.340 --> 00:54:39.209
it's not really juice,
it's something different.

00:54:39.209 --> 00:54:42.245
I don't know what
lemonade is like in Italy.

00:54:45.415 --> 00:54:47.217
Oh, man, it's so tart and so good.

00:54:47.217 --> 00:54:49.386
On to coffee drinks,

00:54:49.386 --> 00:54:51.321
or should I say cold coffee drinks,

00:54:51.321 --> 00:54:52.455
from here to here.

00:54:52.455 --> 00:54:53.923
I understand that's not a thing in Italy,

00:54:53.923 --> 00:54:55.692
which I think is hilarious.

00:54:55.692 --> 00:54:58.528
This giant glass right
here is iced coffee.

00:54:58.528 --> 00:55:00.697
You can also get it caramel flavored

00:55:00.697 --> 00:55:01.998
or French vanilla flavored.

00:55:01.998 --> 00:55:05.535
I went with black, the
ace of spades right here.

00:55:05.535 --> 00:55:06.369
Mm.

00:55:07.904 --> 00:55:10.206
Oh, man, they do something
with their coffee there.

00:55:10.206 --> 00:55:13.476
They do something where it
tastes like it's really roasted.

00:55:13.476 --> 00:55:14.978
I mean, I'm sure it's not.

00:55:14.978 --> 00:55:16.780
You can also get a iced latte.

00:55:16.780 --> 00:55:18.882
This over here is a frappé.

00:55:18.882 --> 00:55:21.584
You can get a mocha frappé
or a caramel frappé.

00:55:21.584 --> 00:55:24.087
Basically if you're an adult
and you want a milkshake,

00:55:24.087 --> 00:55:24.921
you get a frap.

00:55:24.921 --> 00:55:27.157
You can also get smoothies at McDonald's.

00:55:27.157 --> 00:55:30.527
We have a mango pineapple smoothie

00:55:30.527 --> 00:55:32.362
and a strawberry banana smoothie.

00:55:32.362 --> 00:55:35.131
In Italy, we have a few exclusive drinks.

00:55:35.131 --> 00:55:37.500
Let's start with the cold options.

00:55:37.500 --> 00:55:41.471
We have Lipton iced tea
both in lemon and peach.

00:55:41.471 --> 00:55:43.340
Then we have some fruit juices.

00:55:43.340 --> 00:55:44.874
We have pear,

00:55:44.874 --> 00:55:47.844
ace, which is very popular here in Italy.

00:55:47.844 --> 00:55:49.879
It should be very orange.

00:55:49.879 --> 00:55:52.382
It's a mix of orange, carrots, and lemon.

00:55:52.382 --> 00:55:54.084
Yeah, very orange.

00:55:54.084 --> 00:55:57.320
And it's named ace, which is A-C-E,

00:55:57.320 --> 00:56:00.557
after the three vitamins
that these fruits,

00:56:00.557 --> 00:56:03.460
or vegetables, I guess,
these carrots, contains.

00:56:03.460 --> 00:56:05.929
And then we got peach fruit juice.

00:56:05.929 --> 00:56:10.100
And here are our McDonald's
hot coffee drinks.

00:56:10.100 --> 00:56:12.168
"Coffee," right, Italy?

00:56:12.168 --> 00:56:13.703
All right, we get it.

00:56:13.703 --> 00:56:15.438
We went a little overboard
with our coffee drinks

00:56:15.438 --> 00:56:18.508
here in America, and McDonald's,
of course, is no different.

00:56:18.508 --> 00:56:21.711
You can get a caramel macchiato,

00:56:21.711 --> 00:56:24.280
a caramel cappuccino.

00:56:24.280 --> 00:56:28.051
Why are we doing so much
caramel stuff in America, right?

00:56:28.051 --> 00:56:30.487
Ah, caramel latte.

00:56:30.487 --> 00:56:32.856
You can also get it in vanilla.

00:56:32.856 --> 00:56:33.690
Don't.

00:56:33.690 --> 00:56:35.291
You can also get a mocha latte.

00:56:35.291 --> 00:56:38.661
We have a premium roast coffee.

00:56:38.661 --> 00:56:40.463
As I said before, I don't
know what they're doing

00:56:40.463 --> 00:56:42.198
at McDonald's, but

00:56:44.434 --> 00:56:45.802
I like the coffee.

00:56:45.802 --> 00:56:49.272
But you can also get,
finally, a black hot tea.

00:56:49.272 --> 00:56:52.142
What is this? The UK?

00:56:52.142 --> 00:56:53.176
Ugh.

00:56:53.176 --> 00:56:54.878
The hot drinks exclusive to Italy

00:56:54.878 --> 00:56:58.648
are obviously the king
of hot drinks, espresso.

00:56:58.648 --> 00:57:00.583
Then we've got a Moroccan coffee,

00:57:00.583 --> 00:57:03.019
which is not Moroccan in the sense of

00:57:03.019 --> 00:57:06.656
it's not Moroccan-style
coffee, but weirdly enough,

00:57:06.656 --> 00:57:08.558
and to be honest, I never
really understood this,

00:57:08.558 --> 00:57:11.461
it's named after a type
of Moroccan leather

00:57:11.461 --> 00:57:13.897
that looks this color.

00:57:13.897 --> 00:57:17.133
Honestly, it's like an
espresso with some milk.

00:57:17.133 --> 00:57:20.336
And then we got ginseng
coffee and barley coffee,

00:57:20.336 --> 00:57:22.772
which technically shouldn't
really be called coffee

00:57:22.772 --> 00:57:26.342
because it contains no
coffee, it has just barley,

00:57:26.342 --> 00:57:28.778
and this is like an alternative for people

00:57:28.778 --> 00:57:30.747
that cannot drink coffee

00:57:30.747 --> 00:57:33.650
and they still want to have something

00:57:33.650 --> 00:57:35.852
like a little espresso after lunch.

00:57:35.852 --> 00:57:37.654
Yeah, it smells very cereally.

00:57:40.690 --> 00:57:42.459
I don't know. I'm not a big fan.

00:57:42.459 --> 00:57:46.329
And then we got just a
standard latte macchiato.

00:57:46.329 --> 00:57:49.566
This is the closest thing
you will get to a latte

00:57:49.566 --> 00:57:51.468
that you will find here in Italy,

00:57:51.468 --> 00:57:55.705
so it's just a lot of
milk with a bit of coffee

00:57:55.705 --> 00:57:57.607
and some foam at the top.

00:57:59.809 --> 00:58:03.813
In Italy, a Big Mac will cost
you 6 euros and 10 cents.

00:58:03.813 --> 00:58:08.818
In dollars, that's about $6.76.

00:58:08.818 --> 00:58:12.388
A Big Mac in the US will cost you $6.29.

00:58:12.388 --> 00:58:16.793
That's a 3% price increase
from Italy to the US.

00:58:16.793 --> 00:58:19.062
What if you turn that into a combo meal?

00:58:19.062 --> 00:58:22.966
In Italy, a small Big Mac
meal with medium fries

00:58:22.966 --> 00:58:26.369
and a medium drink will
cost you 8 euros 90,

00:58:26.369 --> 00:58:29.405
and that's $9.86.

00:58:29.405 --> 00:58:31.608
Does a combo meal make
a difference in the US?

00:58:31.608 --> 00:58:33.710
A medium Big Mac combo meal over here

00:58:33.710 --> 00:58:36.012
will cost you $11.42.

00:58:36.012 --> 00:58:38.448
You can also save some
money if you buy in bulk.

00:58:38.448 --> 00:58:41.584
Here in Italy, you can
get a two-person Mac menu,

00:58:41.584 --> 00:58:45.788
which includes two Big Macs,
two large portions of fries,

00:58:45.788 --> 00:58:49.092
two large Coca-Colas, six nuggets,

00:58:49.092 --> 00:58:51.194
for 18 euros.

00:58:51.194 --> 00:58:53.763
In the US, we only do Big Mac combo meals,

00:58:53.763 --> 00:58:54.697
as mentioned before.

00:58:54.697 --> 00:58:57.233
So in order to get the
same order in Italy,

00:58:57.233 --> 00:58:59.903
you would have to order two Big Mac meals

00:58:59.903 --> 00:59:01.905
plus six nuggets on the side.

00:59:01.905 --> 00:59:05.842
It would cost around $36, which
in Italy is about 33 euros.

00:59:05.842 --> 00:59:08.811
Price-wise, I think they
are definitely better value

00:59:08.811 --> 00:59:10.413
than other fast-food chains.

00:59:10.413 --> 00:59:11.981
Well, not to believe Five Guys,

00:59:11.981 --> 00:59:16.152
I know that one has a reputation
for being quite expensive,

00:59:16.152 --> 00:59:18.288
but I think the burger
is, like, half the price.

00:59:18.288 --> 00:59:20.924
For the panzerotti, I think
that was more than 3 euros,

00:59:20.924 --> 00:59:23.026
3 euros something, which, honestly,

00:59:23.026 --> 00:59:27.297
for, like, three of those as a
side, it is a little bit sad.

00:59:27.297 --> 00:59:31.067
But again, I grew up in
the town of panzerotti,

00:59:31.067 --> 00:59:34.737
and I used to have, like,
a full one this size

00:59:34.737 --> 00:59:37.707
for, like, 2 euros. That was 15 years ago,

00:59:37.707 --> 00:59:39.943
so maybe now it would
translate into something

00:59:39.943 --> 00:59:42.312
like maybe 5 or 6.

00:59:42.312 --> 00:59:45.848
Once upon a time, McDonald's
was the cheaper option.

00:59:45.848 --> 00:59:48.851
It was a lot of food
for not a lot of money.

00:59:48.851 --> 00:59:51.721
As many people probably
pointed out on social media,

00:59:51.721 --> 00:59:56.292
this food is no longer
inexpensive. It's not expensive.

00:59:56.292 --> 00:59:57.827
Maybe because of the competition,

00:59:57.827 --> 00:59:59.228
maybe because of inflation,

00:59:59.228 --> 01:00:00.863
probably because of corporate greed,

01:00:00.863 --> 01:00:03.666
McDonald's and most fast food, I find,

01:00:03.666 --> 01:00:06.102
is not a good value anymore.

01:00:09.105 --> 01:00:10.306
Let's compare some items to see

01:00:10.306 --> 01:00:12.342
what the nutrition is of McDonald's food.

01:00:12.342 --> 01:00:14.110
A sandwich that exists in both countries

01:00:14.110 --> 01:00:17.714
and is theoretically
identical is the Big Mac.

01:00:17.714 --> 01:00:21.484
In the US, a Big Mac
contains 590 calories,

01:00:21.484 --> 01:00:25.288
34 grams of total fat, 46 grams of carbs,

01:00:25.288 --> 01:00:26.889
and 9 grams of sugar.

01:00:26.889 --> 01:00:28.758
How about an Italian Big Mac?

01:00:28.758 --> 01:00:33.062
One of those here contains 509 calories.

01:00:33.062 --> 01:00:37.033
Of these, there are 26 grams of total fat,

01:00:37.033 --> 01:00:41.437
42 grams of carbs, of
which 9 grams are sugars,

01:00:41.437 --> 01:00:45.475
and then there are 920
milligrams of sodium.

01:00:45.475 --> 01:00:46.909
What if we made it a combo meal?

01:00:46.909 --> 01:00:49.245
Starting with the fries,
a medium fry in the US

01:00:49.245 --> 01:00:53.116
contains 320 calories,
15 grams of total fat,

01:00:53.116 --> 01:00:55.485
43 grams of carbs, no sugar,

01:00:55.485 --> 01:00:57.453
and 260 milligrams of sodium.

01:00:57.453 --> 01:01:02.125
While a medium fries in
Italy contains 330 calories,

01:01:02.125 --> 01:01:06.663
16 grams of total fat, 41 grams of carbs,

01:01:06.663 --> 01:01:09.899
of which 0.4 grams are sugars,

01:01:09.899 --> 01:01:13.636
and 212 milligrams of sodium.

01:01:13.636 --> 01:01:16.139
And let's add the medium
Coke into the mix.

01:01:16.139 --> 01:01:19.108
It contains 210 calories, no fat,

01:01:19.108 --> 01:01:21.611
56 carbs, 56 of those are sugar,

01:01:21.611 --> 01:01:23.212
and 55 milligrams of sodium.

01:01:23.212 --> 01:01:24.681
That's funny there's salt in the soda.

01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:26.015
We'll do the same here.

01:01:26.015 --> 01:01:29.419
Here's what's inside a
medium Coke in Italy.

01:01:29.419 --> 01:01:32.488
It's 168 calories,

01:01:32.488 --> 01:01:34.824
zero grams of fat,

01:01:34.824 --> 01:01:38.828
42 grams of carbs, 42 grams of sugar,

01:01:38.828 --> 01:01:40.463
so it's all sugar,

01:01:40.463 --> 01:01:42.532
and zero grams of sodium.

01:01:42.532 --> 01:01:45.735
That leaves the total for
the Italian meal at this:

01:01:45.735 --> 01:01:48.037
1,007 calories,

01:01:48.037 --> 01:01:49.839
42 grams of fat,

01:01:49.839 --> 01:01:52.542
125 grams of carbs,

01:01:52.542 --> 01:01:55.344
51.4 grams of sugars,

01:01:55.344 --> 01:01:59.682
and 1,132 milligrams of sodium.

01:01:59.682 --> 01:02:03.019
While in the US, the total
ends up looking like this.

01:02:07.223 --> 01:02:09.525
Let's talk about ingredients now.

01:02:09.525 --> 01:02:12.595
McDonald's Italy shares a
lot of information, actually,

01:02:12.595 --> 01:02:14.630
about its ingredients.

01:02:14.630 --> 01:02:17.767
That's because the majority
of the items on the menu

01:02:17.767 --> 01:02:21.738
are made with 100% Italian products.

01:02:21.738 --> 01:02:24.173
The beef, like the one
that's used in the Big Mac,

01:02:24.173 --> 01:02:28.044
is sourced from over
15,000 different farms

01:02:28.044 --> 01:02:29.679
located in northern Italy

01:02:29.679 --> 01:02:34.417
around the regions of
Lombardy, where we are now,

01:02:34.417 --> 01:02:36.152
the capital of which is Milan,

01:02:36.152 --> 01:02:37.754
and Piedmont.

01:02:37.754 --> 01:02:39.455
There are apples from South Tyrol,

01:02:39.455 --> 01:02:41.057
which is where speck is made,

01:02:41.057 --> 01:02:42.759
just on the border with Austria.

01:02:42.759 --> 01:02:44.427
And just to give some recognition

01:02:44.427 --> 01:02:46.763
to the southern regions,
because I'm from there,

01:02:46.763 --> 01:02:49.832
so no bias at all, we've got some apricots

01:02:49.832 --> 01:02:53.536
from the Vesuvio National
Park, so in Campania,

01:02:53.536 --> 01:02:55.671
and Sicilian oranges.

01:02:55.671 --> 01:02:58.574
And when we talk about
DOP, this red label here,

01:02:58.574 --> 01:03:00.376
it's what you are looking for.

01:03:00.376 --> 01:03:04.514
It's a label that's used for
a lot of traditional products

01:03:04.514 --> 01:03:09.118
around the EU, and that means
that they have to be made

01:03:09.118 --> 01:03:11.687
following certain specific standards,

01:03:11.687 --> 01:03:15.191
most of the time in a very artisanal way.

01:03:15.191 --> 01:03:18.294
That also means that certain
products like Parmesan

01:03:18.294 --> 01:03:20.897
cannot be made outside of a specific area.

01:03:20.897 --> 01:03:23.099
That has to do with the climate.

01:03:23.099 --> 01:03:24.400
So, for example, for cheese,

01:03:24.400 --> 01:03:27.136
the main argument is that
it's a raw-milk cheese,

01:03:27.136 --> 01:03:30.706
and in raw-milk cheeses, you
do taste what the cows eat.

01:03:30.706 --> 01:03:33.242
So obviously, the grass
has a different taste

01:03:33.242 --> 01:03:35.411
depending on where you are in the world.

01:03:35.411 --> 01:03:38.314
But we do have some
American-sourced ingredients

01:03:38.314 --> 01:03:39.448
for McDonald's.

01:03:39.448 --> 01:03:42.752
The potatoes used for our
fries are grown in Washington

01:03:42.752 --> 01:03:44.921
at 100 Circles Farm,

01:03:44.921 --> 01:03:47.089
which is owned by Bill Gates, apparently.

01:03:47.089 --> 01:03:49.492
They grow the potatoes in circles so big

01:03:49.492 --> 01:03:51.527
you can see it from space.

01:03:51.527 --> 01:03:54.897
The potatoes are then cut into
fries at 70 miles per hour,

01:03:54.897 --> 01:03:58.000
which is faster than a cheetah.

01:03:58.000 --> 01:04:00.369
That's the unit of measurement?

01:04:00.369 --> 01:04:02.338
That not-so-secret ingredient
to McDonald's fries

01:04:02.338 --> 01:04:06.075
is beef flavoring, which they've
been doing since the 1950s.

01:04:06.075 --> 01:04:07.577
You want to see if there's
any differences in the US

01:04:07.577 --> 01:04:09.912
and Italy's Big Mac?

01:04:09.912 --> 01:04:12.148
These are all the ingredients
in a Big Mac in the US.

01:04:12.148 --> 01:04:15.585
Altogether, that's 68 ingredients
that make up a Big Mac.

01:04:15.585 --> 01:04:16.485
That's a lot.

01:04:16.485 --> 01:04:17.987
28 of those ingredients are in the bun,

01:04:17.987 --> 01:04:19.622
which is quite a lot for bread.

01:04:19.622 --> 01:04:22.024
The Big Mac sauce also
has a lot of ingredients,

01:04:22.024 --> 01:04:24.927
26 altogether, and it seems like we added

01:04:24.927 --> 01:04:27.964
a lot of relish to ours, which
bulks out the ingredients.

01:04:27.964 --> 01:04:31.133
In Italy, there are 54
ingredients in a Big Mac.

01:04:31.133 --> 01:04:32.101
Here they are.

01:04:33.135 --> 01:04:36.072
We only have 20 ingredients
in the bun, actually,

01:04:36.072 --> 01:04:40.076
because we don't fortify the
flour like you do in the US.

01:04:40.076 --> 01:04:43.179
Our Big Mac sauce has 15 ingredients,

01:04:43.179 --> 01:04:47.683
which is still nine less
than the US Big Mac, Joe.

01:04:47.683 --> 01:04:50.119
Most of the other ingredients are similar,

01:04:50.119 --> 01:04:52.154
but we don't have as many colorings

01:04:52.154 --> 01:04:54.924
or thickeners as you do in the US.

01:04:54.924 --> 01:04:57.860
Some of the ingredients
listed in our US Big Mac sauce

01:04:57.860 --> 01:05:00.730
caught our attention, so we
want to explain what they are.

01:05:00.730 --> 01:05:03.833
First up, propylene glycol alginate

01:05:03.833 --> 01:05:05.635
is derived from brown seaweed

01:05:05.635 --> 01:05:07.503
and is a thickener used in foods

01:05:07.503 --> 01:05:09.939
to give a smooth natural texture.

01:05:09.939 --> 01:05:12.108
Next up we got hydrolyzed corn,

01:05:12.108 --> 01:05:14.377
which is a plant protein
from corn or maize

01:05:14.377 --> 01:05:17.847
and is used as a flavoring
for its umami taste.

01:05:17.847 --> 01:05:21.117
Sodium citrate helps cheese to
melt without becoming greasy.

01:05:23.686 --> 01:05:26.188
I did grow up with McDonald's.

01:05:26.188 --> 01:05:29.825
I definitely celebrated a
couple birthdays over there.

01:05:29.825 --> 01:05:33.062
I had my share of Happy Meals

01:05:33.062 --> 01:05:36.165
with lots of little girly toys.

01:05:36.165 --> 01:05:37.967
It is definitely considered healthier

01:05:37.967 --> 01:05:39.936
than other fast-food chains

01:05:39.936 --> 01:05:43.072
because it has been around
for quite some time,

01:05:43.072 --> 01:05:44.607
but also, obviously,

01:05:44.607 --> 01:05:48.044
because it has Italianized
a lot over the years,

01:05:48.044 --> 01:05:49.979
incorporating things like Parmesan

01:05:49.979 --> 01:05:52.415
or like traditional cheeses and cold cuts.

01:05:52.415 --> 01:05:53.749
So just appealing a little bit more

01:05:53.749 --> 01:05:56.252
to the taste of Italians.

01:05:56.252 --> 01:06:01.057
I have been to stores
in the US and the UK,

01:06:01.057 --> 01:06:03.993
and Italian McDonald's seem, I don't know,

01:06:03.993 --> 01:06:05.494
a little bit fancier.

01:06:05.494 --> 01:06:07.830
It's everywhere and made burgers and fries

01:06:07.830 --> 01:06:11.300
and sodas to go the most
popular meal in the country,

01:06:11.300 --> 01:06:13.669
and then how many places followed suit?

01:06:13.669 --> 01:06:16.305
With Burger King and
Wendy's and all the like.

01:06:16.305 --> 01:06:18.207
And now we got
chicken-sandwich-version ones,

01:06:18.207 --> 01:06:19.041
we got fried chicken.

01:06:19.041 --> 01:06:23.245
McDonald's McDonald's-ified
the entire country

01:06:23.245 --> 01:06:24.513
and the world.

01:06:24.513 --> 01:06:28.250
McDonald's is like Nike or Christianity.

01:06:28.250 --> 01:06:29.986
It's everywhere!

01:06:29.986 --> 01:06:32.121
Claudia: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:06:32.121 --> 01:06:34.223
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:06:34.223 --> 01:06:37.126
between Burger King in Italy and the US.

01:06:37.126 --> 01:06:38.661
This is "Food Wars."

01:06:40.930 --> 01:06:43.899
In Italy, our drinks come in three sizes,

01:06:43.899 --> 01:06:46.302
small, medium, and large.

01:06:46.302 --> 01:06:47.737
We're going to measure the large one

01:06:47.737 --> 01:06:50.773
to see how much it actually contains.

01:06:50.773 --> 01:06:53.275
There's supposed to be 500 ml.

01:06:53.275 --> 01:06:55.711
I think we're getting
close to 600, actually.

01:06:55.711 --> 01:06:58.080
140 ml extra.

01:06:58.080 --> 01:06:59.081
Burger King in the US.

01:06:59.081 --> 01:07:01.684
Our fountain drinks come in four sizes,

01:07:01.684 --> 01:07:05.421
value, small, medium, and large,

01:07:05.421 --> 01:07:07.356
and the large is 38 fluid ounces,

01:07:07.356 --> 01:07:10.259
or 1,120 milliliters.

01:07:10.259 --> 01:07:12.294
And now I would like
to measure the largest

01:07:12.294 --> 01:07:15.164
and see if that's exactly
how much they gave us.

01:07:18.134 --> 01:07:20.136
It's almost exactly 32 fluid ounces.

01:07:20.136 --> 01:07:21.670
It's not close to 38 ounces.

01:07:21.670 --> 01:07:23.172
Yeah, it says 38 in the bottom here.

01:07:23.172 --> 01:07:25.574
Hey, someone who works at Burger King

01:07:25.574 --> 01:07:28.010
or someone who works in fast food,

01:07:28.010 --> 01:07:32.915
why, why, why, do they say
here's how big the cup is

01:07:32.915 --> 01:07:34.583
and then clearly it's not that amount?

01:07:34.583 --> 01:07:36.752
What am I missing here?
Every single place does it.

01:07:36.752 --> 01:07:39.021
Here in Italy we have
three sizes of fries,

01:07:39.021 --> 01:07:41.157
small, medium, and large.

01:07:41.157 --> 01:07:45.194
Burger King in the US,
they got four fries sizes.

01:07:45.194 --> 01:07:48.464
Over here's the value, then the small,

01:07:48.464 --> 01:07:50.966
the medium, and the large.

01:07:53.636 --> 01:07:55.404
So, I know that in "Food Wars" history,

01:07:55.404 --> 01:07:57.273
Burger King has actually lied to us.

01:07:57.273 --> 01:07:59.875
So let's see if they've been
honest with me today in Italy

01:07:59.875 --> 01:08:02.111
and measure every single one of them.

01:08:02.111 --> 01:08:04.747
The sizes are working now.

01:08:04.747 --> 01:08:07.083
The small is actually
smaller than the medium.

01:08:07.083 --> 01:08:08.017
I have no proof of this.

01:08:08.017 --> 01:08:11.554
I think they saw our US
versus UK Burger King episode,

01:08:11.554 --> 01:08:15.524
saw us then call out #frygate2021,
whenever we did that.

01:08:15.524 --> 01:08:16.358
#frygate2020!

01:08:16.358 --> 01:08:19.562
And they're running
scared, but they still,

01:08:19.562 --> 01:08:21.163
trying to pull it over.

01:08:21.163 --> 01:08:22.098
A US Whopper.

01:08:22.098 --> 01:08:23.799
The Whopper's a fantastic sandwich.

01:08:27.303 --> 01:08:30.806
On to the nuggets. In Italy,
they come in three sizes,

01:08:30.806 --> 01:08:33.676
a six-piece, nine-piece, and 20-piece.

01:08:33.676 --> 01:08:37.413
In the US, our nuggets
come in three sizes,

01:08:37.413 --> 01:08:39.482
two if you go into the
restaurant apparently.

01:08:39.482 --> 01:08:41.717
You can get the four-piece
or the eight-piece,

01:08:41.717 --> 01:08:44.954
but also on Uber Eats,
an exclusive apparently,

01:08:44.954 --> 01:08:46.455
you can get a 16-piece.

01:08:46.455 --> 01:08:49.492
Both Italy and the US serve onion rings.

01:08:49.492 --> 01:08:52.294
In Italy, they come in a eight-piece,

01:08:52.294 --> 01:08:56.265
12-piece, and 16-piece.

01:09:00.035 --> 01:09:01.871
So, we have four onion-ring sizes,

01:09:01.871 --> 01:09:03.472
and I want to point out that for us,

01:09:03.472 --> 01:09:04.707
we just do it by cup size.

01:09:04.707 --> 01:09:06.342
We're not doing it by
number of onion rings

01:09:06.342 --> 01:09:07.176
like they do in Italy.

01:09:07.176 --> 01:09:10.212
I have to say, they were very generous

01:09:10.212 --> 01:09:11.680
with the onion rings at ours.

01:09:11.680 --> 01:09:12.515
I mean, this is the value.

01:09:12.515 --> 01:09:15.384
This thing is overflowing
with onion rings.

01:09:15.384 --> 01:09:17.453
We have a small, medium, and large.

01:09:19.588 --> 01:09:22.825
Here's everything that you can
find at Burger King in Italy

01:09:22.825 --> 01:09:24.527
that you won't find in the US.

01:09:24.527 --> 01:09:25.561
And here's everything you can find

01:09:25.561 --> 01:09:29.398
on the menu at a US Burger
King you can't get in Italy.

01:09:29.398 --> 01:09:31.133
Let's start with the burgers.

01:09:31.133 --> 01:09:33.669
In Italy, we have the
Italian King collection,

01:09:33.669 --> 01:09:35.671
which comprises these two burgers here.

01:09:35.671 --> 01:09:39.341
The first one is the Parma
ham and scamorza burger.

01:09:39.341 --> 01:09:43.212
Scamorza is a cheese from
south Italy, where I'm from.

01:09:43.212 --> 01:09:46.015
So, scamorza, it's a bit
like a mozzarella in a way,

01:09:46.015 --> 01:09:48.851
like they come from the
same family of cheeses.

01:09:48.851 --> 01:09:49.985
They're made in a similar way,

01:09:49.985 --> 01:09:54.223
but scamorza, it's aged for, like, a week,

01:09:54.223 --> 01:09:56.892
like, not so much, so it's
like a hard mozzarella.

01:09:56.892 --> 01:09:59.295
Let's see how it tastes in a burger.

01:09:59.295 --> 01:10:00.396
Nice.

01:10:01.230 --> 01:10:03.032
Not a fan of the onions.

01:10:03.032 --> 01:10:06.335
I think they overpower a little
bit the taste of the cheese.

01:10:06.335 --> 01:10:08.003
Without maybe the patty,

01:10:08.003 --> 01:10:11.340
it does seem like a
traditional Italian sandwich.

01:10:11.340 --> 01:10:14.243
And then we have the Parmesan burger.

01:10:14.243 --> 01:10:17.346
This one has bacon in it.

01:10:17.346 --> 01:10:19.882
Apparently when Burger
King launched this burger,

01:10:19.882 --> 01:10:21.584
they had to buy something like

01:10:21.584 --> 01:10:24.119
500 wheels of Parmigiano-Reggiano,

01:10:24.119 --> 01:10:28.691
which is like Parmesan. In
Italy they are the same thing.

01:10:28.691 --> 01:10:30.125
So quite a lot of wheels.

01:10:31.393 --> 01:10:33.462
I don't know. It feels like a dream

01:10:33.462 --> 01:10:37.633
to be in one of those rooms
with 500 wheels of Parmesan.

01:10:37.633 --> 01:10:38.767
It feels like, I don't know,

01:10:38.767 --> 01:10:40.836
next time you do it, please
call me, Burger King.

01:10:40.836 --> 01:10:42.538
I'm coming to collect the cheese.

01:10:43.806 --> 01:10:45.608
Better this one than the other one.

01:10:45.608 --> 01:10:48.177
This one is a little bit less messy.

01:10:48.177 --> 01:10:52.114
The flavors come out individually.
I can taste everything.

01:10:52.114 --> 01:10:54.984
Yeah, I like this one.
Always on the Parmesan team.

01:10:54.984 --> 01:10:56.619
And then we've got the big king.

01:10:56.619 --> 01:11:00.456
This is supposed to be Burger
King's version of the Big Mac.

01:11:00.456 --> 01:11:03.525
This one, it's slightly
different to the US

01:11:03.525 --> 01:11:07.062
because it has an extra bun in the middle,

01:11:07.062 --> 01:11:09.965
and apparently it has a special sauce

01:11:09.965 --> 01:11:13.869
that's supposed to taste
like Thousand Island sauce.

01:11:13.869 --> 01:11:14.970
Very yellowy.

01:11:14.970 --> 01:11:17.139
I never had Thousand Island sauce.

01:11:17.139 --> 01:11:20.209
I don't think I've ever seen
it, even in a supermarket.

01:11:20.209 --> 01:11:21.777
This is a bit vinegary,

01:11:21.777 --> 01:11:24.546
a bit like tartar sauce in a way,

01:11:24.546 --> 01:11:27.816
but, mm, I don't know.

01:11:27.816 --> 01:11:30.252
I'm not a fan, but I don't
know, maybe there's just, like,

01:11:30.252 --> 01:11:32.254
the aftertaste of pickles.

01:11:32.254 --> 01:11:34.156
That's also something I don't like.

01:11:34.156 --> 01:11:37.960
I know Joe doesn't like them,
so, yeah, there's two of us.

01:11:37.960 --> 01:11:40.129
Yes, Claudia dislikes pickles, too!

01:11:40.129 --> 01:11:41.597
I'm so happy to hear that.

01:11:41.597 --> 01:11:43.432
Claudia has impeccable taste.

01:11:43.432 --> 01:11:45.100
So for her to dislike pickles

01:11:45.100 --> 01:11:47.469
must mean that I also
have impeccable taste.

01:11:47.469 --> 01:11:50.406
So me and Claudia, no-pickle friends.

01:11:50.406 --> 01:11:53.942
And then we've got the
bacon burger king 3.0.

01:11:53.942 --> 01:11:55.477
It's got three of everything.

01:11:55.477 --> 01:11:59.615
It's got three patties, three cheeses,

01:11:59.615 --> 01:12:02.384
and actually eight strips of bacon.

01:12:02.384 --> 01:12:04.119
It's so heavy.

01:12:04.119 --> 01:12:05.654
I mean, I'm going to take this to the gym

01:12:05.654 --> 01:12:08.357
to use as a proper weight.

01:12:08.357 --> 01:12:10.125
It just looks gross.

01:12:10.125 --> 01:12:12.161
It looks like, I don't know, like cement.

01:12:12.161 --> 01:12:14.830
I don't know how this is
an exclusive to Italy.

01:12:14.830 --> 01:12:16.432
I feel like if I want to indulge,

01:12:16.432 --> 01:12:18.901
I'll just have two of something else

01:12:18.901 --> 01:12:20.536
that's a little bit less messy.

01:12:20.536 --> 01:12:22.538
There are eight strips of bacon, though,

01:12:22.538 --> 01:12:26.041
and apparently they are different
in Italy than in the US.

01:12:26.041 --> 01:12:27.910
So let's have a look.

01:12:27.910 --> 01:12:31.246
And then we've got the Bronx steakhouse.

01:12:31.246 --> 01:12:35.184
If you are from the Bronx,
does this look familiar to you?

01:12:35.184 --> 01:12:38.287
And then we have the

01:12:38.287 --> 01:12:40.923
veggie steakhouse.

01:12:40.923 --> 01:12:45.094
Same thing, just with a
veggie party. What is this?

01:12:45.094 --> 01:12:48.897
It's like veggie bacon. It's
the first time I see it.

01:12:48.897 --> 01:12:52.701
Why is it brown? It looks like a candy.

01:12:55.270 --> 01:12:58.307
Tastes like salt and like frying oil.

01:12:58.307 --> 01:13:00.876
Not so much like bacon.

01:13:02.711 --> 01:13:04.413
Yeah, does give you the feeling

01:13:04.413 --> 01:13:06.548
of just having a regular burger.

01:13:06.548 --> 01:13:08.717
This is not technically vegetarian

01:13:08.717 --> 01:13:12.554
because it's cooked on the
same grill as the meat patty.

01:13:12.554 --> 01:13:15.691
I guess this is a burger
for people that eat meat

01:13:15.691 --> 01:13:17.393
that want to try a veggie option.

01:13:17.393 --> 01:13:19.128
The veggie steakhouse?

01:13:19.128 --> 01:13:20.295
That might be a translation error.

01:13:20.295 --> 01:13:23.399
I don't know if it could be
a veggie and a steakhouse.

01:13:23.399 --> 01:13:26.001
Then we've got the big king XXL,

01:13:26.001 --> 01:13:28.971
so bigger size than this one.

01:13:28.971 --> 01:13:32.174
This one has got two
patties, four cheeses,

01:13:32.174 --> 01:13:36.078
and a special sauce.
Bigger onions as well.

01:13:36.078 --> 01:13:38.514
Then we have the plant-based Whopper,

01:13:38.514 --> 01:13:41.750
and then we've got the
crazy cheese Whopper.

01:13:41.750 --> 01:13:45.187
This one is a delivery exclusive,

01:13:45.187 --> 01:13:47.589
apparently for the cheese lovers.

01:13:47.589 --> 01:13:49.658
To be honest, as a cheese lover,

01:13:49.658 --> 01:13:50.959
what is this amount of cheese?

01:13:50.959 --> 01:13:52.394
Just, it's ridiculous.

01:13:52.394 --> 01:13:55.864
There was more in any other burger.

01:13:55.864 --> 01:13:57.633
It's just for the lovers of, like,

01:13:57.633 --> 01:14:01.570
weirdly hanging strips of bacon, maybe.

01:14:01.637 --> 01:14:03.705
All right, US burger exclusive options,

01:14:03.705 --> 01:14:04.907
starting right here.

01:14:04.907 --> 01:14:06.442
Got the bacon cheeseburger.

01:14:06.442 --> 01:14:07.943
Look how small this is, by the way.

01:14:07.943 --> 01:14:10.712
But as you can see, burger,

01:14:10.712 --> 01:14:12.981
got bacon and cheese. Believe it.

01:14:12.981 --> 01:14:14.883
Moving on to the Impossible Whopper.

01:14:14.883 --> 01:14:16.418
I think that's this one with lettuce. Yep.

01:14:16.418 --> 01:14:19.054
Impossible is a brand of plant-based meat

01:14:19.054 --> 01:14:21.356
here in the United
States that is just that,

01:14:21.356 --> 01:14:23.926
made from plants! No animals were harmed

01:14:23.926 --> 01:14:26.295
in the making of this burger, I think.

01:14:26.295 --> 01:14:27.763
Something that should be noted,

01:14:27.763 --> 01:14:30.199
there is a disclaimer on the
Burger King website that says,

01:14:30.199 --> 01:14:32.835
"Our Impossible meat is
cooked on the same broiler

01:14:32.835 --> 01:14:36.238
as the regular meat," and
also the mayo on these burgers

01:14:36.238 --> 01:14:41.210
does have eggs in it, so, good effort?

01:14:41.210 --> 01:14:43.579
Texas double Whopper. Come on, Texas.

01:14:43.579 --> 01:14:45.647
Texas is a state in the United States

01:14:45.647 --> 01:14:46.815
that does everything bigger,

01:14:46.815 --> 01:14:48.884
so of course they have their own Whopper.

01:14:48.884 --> 01:14:52.120
It's a double Whopper, double
the size of a regular Whopper.

01:14:52.120 --> 01:14:55.324
Look at this. It's got
double the meat. See that?

01:14:55.324 --> 01:14:57.860
And jalapeños on here,

01:14:57.860 --> 01:15:00.295
although they're kind of
nonexistent, but they're on there.

01:15:00.295 --> 01:15:02.431
In the US, we have the
single quarter-pound king.

01:15:02.431 --> 01:15:04.299
You saw that earlier. I
absolutely destroyed it.

01:15:04.299 --> 01:15:08.270
I threw it away. But also we
have a single Impossible king!

01:15:08.270 --> 01:15:10.172
Same thing as the Impossible Whopper!

01:15:10.172 --> 01:15:12.508
Why am I talking like this? Look at that.

01:15:12.508 --> 01:15:15.110
I mean, you could put this melted cheese

01:15:15.110 --> 01:15:17.012
on a piece of shoe leather,

01:15:17.012 --> 01:15:18.113
and I wouldn't know the difference.

01:15:18.113 --> 01:15:20.949
We also have a bacon Whopper Jr.,

01:15:20.949 --> 01:15:23.118
which they didn't give us,

01:15:23.118 --> 01:15:26.622
also a big king, which
they did not give us.

01:15:26.622 --> 01:15:27.656
I'm certain I ordered it.

01:15:27.656 --> 01:15:29.224
Anyway, what we do have is this,

01:15:29.224 --> 01:15:31.293
the Rodeo burger, pa-pow.

01:15:31.293 --> 01:15:33.562
It's a burger with barbecue
sauce and onion rings.

01:15:33.562 --> 01:15:35.664
Man, really generous with the onion rings.

01:15:35.664 --> 01:15:37.065
Fun fact about the Rodeo cheeseburger:

01:15:37.065 --> 01:15:38.834
It was created to
coincide with the release

01:15:38.834 --> 01:15:41.803
of the film "Small Soldiers" in 1998.

01:15:41.803 --> 01:15:45.474
Another fun fact: In 1998,
I worked at a movie theater

01:15:45.474 --> 01:15:48.677
in Schaumburg, Illinois,
that showed "Small Soldiers."

01:15:48.677 --> 01:15:51.747
This was for some reason brought out

01:15:51.747 --> 01:15:53.315
in time with that movie.

01:15:53.315 --> 01:15:55.651
It was on the dollar
menu, stayed on the menu.

01:15:55.651 --> 01:15:57.786
I guess you can see
why. Fun little burger.

01:15:57.786 --> 01:15:59.521
And the "Small Soldiers" Chip Hazard,

01:15:59.521 --> 01:16:00.355
which is the name of the character,

01:16:00.355 --> 01:16:01.290
I didn't even know what his name was,

01:16:01.290 --> 01:16:02.424
advertised it by saying,

01:16:02.424 --> 01:16:04.927
"You can't handle the Rodeo
burger," which is just like

01:16:04.927 --> 01:16:06.595
Jack Nicholson's line
from "A Few Good Men,"

01:16:06.595 --> 01:16:07.863
"You can't handle the truth!"

01:16:07.863 --> 01:16:09.431
Here are all the chicken items

01:16:09.431 --> 01:16:11.700
that you can get at Burger King in Italy,

01:16:11.700 --> 01:16:14.636
starting from the Crunchicken.

01:16:14.636 --> 01:16:19.141
Fried chicken, mayo, lettuce, and tomato.

01:16:19.141 --> 01:16:21.243
You can also get a chicken bacon king,

01:16:21.243 --> 01:16:26.114
same thing as the beef one,
with eight strips of bacon.

01:16:26.114 --> 01:16:29.651
Next up we have the chicken
royale, with bacon, cheese.

01:16:29.651 --> 01:16:34.256
Why is this this shape?
Does this look royal to you?

01:16:34.256 --> 01:16:35.691
Maybe it's just easier to eat.

01:16:35.691 --> 01:16:38.460
I don't know, but I'm not very intrigued.

01:16:38.460 --> 01:16:40.095
A lot of mayo here.

01:16:40.095 --> 01:16:43.565
And then we got the
crazy cheese chicken BBQ.

01:16:43.565 --> 01:16:46.301
Yeah, there's definitely
barbecue sauce here.

01:16:46.301 --> 01:16:49.838
And then we got a
plant-based nugget burger,

01:16:49.838 --> 01:16:52.841
which has mayo that is not vegan

01:16:52.841 --> 01:16:54.776
because obviously there's eggs in there,

01:16:54.776 --> 01:16:57.446
but there are three nuggets in there.

01:16:57.446 --> 01:17:00.749
Just quite funny, like a nugget burger.

01:17:00.749 --> 01:17:02.050
Here are most of the chicken options

01:17:02.050 --> 01:17:03.986
you can get at the US Burger King.

01:17:03.986 --> 01:17:08.590
Starting down here, we got
the BK royal crispy chicken.

01:17:08.590 --> 01:17:11.026
Every time we do a "Food Wars,"

01:17:11.026 --> 01:17:13.795
Burger King's got a bunch
of new chicken sandwiches

01:17:13.795 --> 01:17:16.131
because they're trying to
compete with Chick-fil-A,

01:17:16.131 --> 01:17:18.433
and if you ask me, they losing.

01:17:18.433 --> 01:17:22.671
All right. This looks like
the epitome of "just OK."

01:17:22.671 --> 01:17:25.841
We also have a spicy version
of the same sandwich,

01:17:25.841 --> 01:17:29.077
the spicy BK royal crispy sandwich.

01:17:29.077 --> 01:17:30.278
This one looks crispier.

01:17:31.113 --> 01:17:33.181
Much better. Not very spicy.

01:17:33.181 --> 01:17:35.517
Good flavor to it. Get that one.

01:17:35.517 --> 01:17:37.152
You also have a bacon and Swiss one,

01:17:37.152 --> 01:17:38.053
which I think is this one.

01:17:38.053 --> 01:17:39.154
All right. I'm going to
get a bite of the bacon

01:17:39.154 --> 01:17:40.288
and the Swiss.

01:17:41.523 --> 01:17:42.658
Tastes bacony.

01:17:42.658 --> 01:17:44.893
Typical to Burger King,
something's popular,

01:17:44.893 --> 01:17:47.963
so they make a somewhat inferior version.

01:17:47.963 --> 01:17:49.798
You can also get the honey mustard

01:17:49.798 --> 01:17:53.635
BK royal crisp chicken blabbity blah.

01:17:53.635 --> 01:17:55.470
[groans]

01:17:55.470 --> 01:17:57.539
This one also has bacon on it.

01:17:57.539 --> 01:17:59.341
The honey mustard's interesting.

01:17:59.341 --> 01:18:01.877
We also have a chicken
junior. It's a little guy.

01:18:01.877 --> 01:18:04.680
This is basically the
rip-off of the McChicken,

01:18:04.680 --> 01:18:08.617
a far more superior chicken sandwich.

01:18:09.951 --> 01:18:12.688
Another menu item that was
available over the summer

01:18:12.688 --> 01:18:14.623
but may be off the menu now,

01:18:14.623 --> 01:18:17.125
certainly wasn't at the BK
we went to here in Burbank,

01:18:17.125 --> 01:18:20.095
was the Italian BK royal crispy chicken.

01:18:20.095 --> 01:18:22.164
Let's get that picture up on the screen.

01:18:22.164 --> 01:18:25.100
This would've been perfect for
"Food Wars," US versus Italy.

01:18:25.100 --> 01:18:26.635
Couldn't get my hands on it.

01:18:26.635 --> 01:18:28.837
Claudia, what do you think of this?

01:18:28.837 --> 01:18:31.239
I don't know. That doesn't
look very Italian to me.

01:18:31.239 --> 01:18:32.908
I think if you put crispy chicken,

01:18:32.908 --> 01:18:35.577
that automatically makes it not Italian.

01:18:35.577 --> 01:18:38.647
Let's talk about wraps.
We thought there were two.

01:18:38.647 --> 01:18:42.784
Actually, the grilled
chicken is not there anymore,

01:18:42.784 --> 01:18:45.554
so we just got this crispy one.

01:18:45.554 --> 01:18:47.255
This wrap looks very sad.

01:18:47.255 --> 01:18:48.790
I don't know. I feel
like you could do better

01:18:48.790 --> 01:18:51.059
with the actual wrap itself.

01:18:51.059 --> 01:18:53.095
Here's what's inside.

01:18:53.095 --> 01:18:54.696
I don't know. The wrap is very pale.

01:18:54.696 --> 01:18:57.065
BK also has wraps. You can
get pretty much each one

01:18:57.065 --> 01:18:59.201
of these chicken sandwiches in wrap form.

01:18:59.201 --> 01:19:03.071
I went ahead and got the
spicy BK royal crispy wrap.

01:19:03.071 --> 01:19:04.206
I mean, all they're doing is taking --

01:19:04.206 --> 01:19:06.141
oh, so it's half a patty.
Not even a full patty.

01:19:06.141 --> 01:19:08.110
So you get half a patty and
all this stuff in wrap form.

01:19:08.110 --> 01:19:10.078
Like, what's the draw of this?

01:19:10.078 --> 01:19:12.280
If you want a wrap,
just go someplace else.

01:19:12.280 --> 01:19:14.983
Couple other exclusive
items that we got here.

01:19:14.983 --> 01:19:16.518
You can get a taco at Burger King.

01:19:16.518 --> 01:19:18.053
I love tacos just as much as the next guy,

01:19:18.053 --> 01:19:20.055
but, I mean, look how thin this is.

01:19:20.055 --> 01:19:22.824
It looks like the guy sat on
it before he gave it to us.

01:19:22.824 --> 01:19:24.025
I'm curious.

01:19:26.495 --> 01:19:27.562
I can't be sure, but I think they put

01:19:27.562 --> 01:19:28.764
the barbecue sauce in there.

01:19:28.764 --> 01:19:30.599
That can't be right. If
they did, that's terrible.

01:19:30.599 --> 01:19:32.701
Whatever it is, it's bad. Don't get it.

01:19:32.701 --> 01:19:34.569
This right here is the big fish.

01:19:34.569 --> 01:19:36.972
Look at this thing. What a nightmare.

01:19:36.972 --> 01:19:39.341
They put pickles on it? Guys, come on.

01:19:39.341 --> 01:19:41.943
Pickles on a fish sandwich.

01:19:41.943 --> 01:19:45.313
I really like the Filet-O-Fish.
I should say that right now.

01:19:45.313 --> 01:19:47.048
I think it's a tasty sandwich.

01:19:47.048 --> 01:19:47.883
I don't know what they're putting

01:19:47.883 --> 01:19:49.484
in the Filet-O-Fish at McDonald's,

01:19:49.484 --> 01:19:51.953
probably not a lot of fish,
but I think it's very good.

01:19:51.953 --> 01:19:53.221
My favorite thing about the Filet-O-Fish

01:19:53.221 --> 01:19:55.791
is their tartar sauce. It
makes and breaks the sandwich.

01:19:55.791 --> 01:19:59.694
For them, tartar sauce,
fantastic, so one would assume

01:19:59.694 --> 01:20:03.165
that this square fish patty,

01:20:03.165 --> 01:20:05.500
correct me I'm wrong, but
no fish is naturally square,

01:20:05.500 --> 01:20:08.770
so this highly processed fish patty

01:20:08.770 --> 01:20:10.739
is drowning in a white sauce

01:20:10.739 --> 01:20:12.507
that should be a tartar sauce,

01:20:12.507 --> 01:20:15.210
and we're going to find
out if it's any good.

01:20:17.779 --> 01:20:19.314
It's a thicker bun,

01:20:20.182 --> 01:20:22.317
so it feels like you're
getting more sandwich.

01:20:22.317 --> 01:20:23.618
Yeah, I actually kind of like that.

01:20:23.618 --> 01:20:24.586
I don't think it's better tasting

01:20:24.586 --> 01:20:26.454
than the Filet-O-Fish, but
it's still pretty good.

01:20:26.454 --> 01:20:29.591
Let's see what is in
Italy's king junior meal.

01:20:29.591 --> 01:20:32.727
As a main course, you can
either get a four-piece nugget,

01:20:32.727 --> 01:20:35.931
a chicken burger, a
hamburger, a cheeseburger,

01:20:35.931 --> 01:20:38.633
or a toast, which is what we got today.

01:20:38.633 --> 01:20:41.703
And then you also get
fries, a mini Kit Kat,

01:20:41.703 --> 01:20:43.405
a drink, and a toy.

01:20:43.405 --> 01:20:46.274
Let's see what's inside ours.

01:20:46.274 --> 01:20:47.409
Here's our toast.

01:20:49.878 --> 01:20:53.114
Tiny fries, cute,

01:20:54.115 --> 01:20:55.283
Kit Kat,

01:20:55.283 --> 01:20:56.518
the drink obviously,

01:20:56.518 --> 01:20:58.153
and a toy.

01:20:58.153 --> 01:21:01.857
What is this? It looks like a glass.

01:21:01.857 --> 01:21:03.024
It doesn't really look like something

01:21:03.024 --> 01:21:06.394
you would give to your child
if you were making their lunch.

01:21:06.394 --> 01:21:08.597
It is the plainest thing that you can get,

01:21:08.597 --> 01:21:11.166
and usually parents are a little bit wary

01:21:11.166 --> 01:21:14.703
of giving sauces and
things that are too rich.

01:21:14.703 --> 01:21:18.640
Kids-meal options in the
US, aka the king junior.

01:21:18.640 --> 01:21:21.042
You can get either a cheeseburger
or a four-piece nugget.

01:21:21.042 --> 01:21:22.210
I think we got the nuggets.

01:21:22.210 --> 01:21:23.845
And then your options are either fries,

01:21:23.845 --> 01:21:26.047
onion rings, or applesauce.

01:21:26.047 --> 01:21:29.584
They have a drink cup that is reusable.

01:21:30.485 --> 01:21:32.988
I think it's pretty nice.
And you can also get milk.

01:21:32.988 --> 01:21:34.456
See it says "Jr." right there?

01:21:34.456 --> 01:21:36.691
And for a toy,

01:21:39.561 --> 01:21:40.562
a spoon.

01:21:40.562 --> 01:21:43.131
No. The toy, they got nothing.

01:21:43.131 --> 01:21:44.933
I don't know if they
forgot to give us a toy,

01:21:44.933 --> 01:21:47.168
or maybe they don't have toys?

01:21:48.403 --> 01:21:49.304
What?

01:21:51.273 --> 01:21:52.841
Oh, you think because
I ordered as an adult,

01:21:52.841 --> 01:21:55.176
they're like, "He doesn't want a toy"?

01:21:55.176 --> 01:21:56.978
What, all work and no play for the J-man?

01:21:56.978 --> 01:21:58.213
Come on, I want a toy!

01:21:58.213 --> 01:22:00.382
I think maybe, though,

01:22:00.382 --> 01:22:02.484
you think the puzzle's the toy on the bag?

01:22:03.518 --> 01:22:04.686
I don't know.

01:22:05.720 --> 01:22:07.856
I don't think the spoon's the toy.

01:22:07.856 --> 01:22:11.192
So either they forgot the
toy or you don't get one.

01:22:11.192 --> 01:22:12.727
We didn't get one.

01:22:12.727 --> 01:22:15.597
Exclusive sides we have,
these are two of them.

01:22:15.597 --> 01:22:17.132
One thing I want to point
everyone's attention to

01:22:17.132 --> 01:22:19.901
are these chicken fries.

01:22:19.901 --> 01:22:23.471
That's right, chicken
strips shaped like fries.

01:22:23.471 --> 01:22:25.206
Interesting fact about this box,

01:22:25.206 --> 01:22:27.142
see how it kind of gets smaller here?

01:22:27.142 --> 01:22:29.044
This box was designed specifically

01:22:29.044 --> 01:22:32.981
to fit in a car cup holder,
because here in America,

01:22:32.981 --> 01:22:35.283
God forbid we stop and eat a meal.

01:22:35.283 --> 01:22:37.052
We have to eat and do something else.

01:22:37.052 --> 01:22:38.486
I think it's very funny
considering in Italy,

01:22:38.486 --> 01:22:40.622
it's like the meal is the event.

01:22:40.622 --> 01:22:42.223
Now, it's a chicken fry.

01:22:42.223 --> 01:22:45.627
It's more of a marketing
thing to call this a fry,

01:22:45.627 --> 01:22:48.063
because it's not a chicken tender,

01:22:48.063 --> 01:22:50.899
because tenders come from a
specific part of the chicken.

01:22:50.899 --> 01:22:53.368
The fry is more like a chicken finger,

01:22:53.368 --> 01:22:55.136
where it's made with whole muscle meat.

01:22:55.136 --> 01:22:57.038
They're really durable.
They're really elastic.

01:22:57.038 --> 01:22:58.106
Don't you think if you're waving

01:22:58.106 --> 01:22:59.107
a piece of chicken like this,

01:22:59.107 --> 01:23:01.009
it would've broken off by now?

01:23:01.009 --> 01:23:03.745
Look at this! Look at this!

01:23:03.745 --> 01:23:05.580
Why is this so like this?

01:23:05.580 --> 01:23:07.315
I think they taste fine.

01:23:07.315 --> 01:23:11.319
It's just a weird thing
to be on the menu still.

01:23:11.319 --> 01:23:12.687
I mean, I don't know
anyone who's getting these.

01:23:12.687 --> 01:23:14.489
Mozzarella sticks.

01:23:14.489 --> 01:23:16.691
We should've asked Claudia before.

01:23:16.691 --> 01:23:19.194
Do mozzarella sticks even exist in Italy?

01:23:19.194 --> 01:23:21.229
I want to know. Because here in the US,

01:23:21.229 --> 01:23:22.897
you can get these as a four-piece

01:23:22.897 --> 01:23:26.835
or an eight-piece with marinara sauce.

01:23:26.835 --> 01:23:28.203
These have been sitting for a while,

01:23:28.203 --> 01:23:30.005
but of course I'm wondering
what kind of cheese pull

01:23:30.005 --> 01:23:32.407
we can get from these mozzarella sticks.

01:23:34.209 --> 01:23:38.813
Eh, eh, oh, OK, OK.

01:23:39.748 --> 01:23:42.984
Oh, not a bad one. They're just OK.

01:23:42.984 --> 01:23:45.954
These are our exclusive
sides here in Italy,

01:23:45.954 --> 01:23:48.690
starting from these chili cheese bites.

01:23:48.690 --> 01:23:51.292
You can get them in a
six-piece and a nine-piece.

01:23:51.292 --> 01:23:54.562
Doesn't look like there's chili
in them. Let's try them out.

01:23:57.365 --> 01:23:59.034
They taste a bit too peppery, I think.

01:23:59.034 --> 01:24:01.002
I was expecting it just to taste spicy.

01:24:01.002 --> 01:24:04.372
Like, they taste like fresh
chilies, which is nice,

01:24:04.372 --> 01:24:06.141
but I'm not sure what cheese is this.

01:24:06.141 --> 01:24:10.345
Then we've got plant-based
nuggets as a six-piece.

01:24:10.345 --> 01:24:12.614
They look a bit green, like there's been,

01:24:12.614 --> 01:24:15.350
like there's some filter on them.

01:24:15.350 --> 01:24:16.918
They taste actually like nuggets.

01:24:16.918 --> 01:24:21.022
I don't know if this is fake chicken

01:24:21.022 --> 01:24:24.726
or it's just vegetables,
but they're quite good,

01:24:24.726 --> 01:24:27.662
and from the inside they
look like normal ones.

01:24:27.662 --> 01:24:31.766
You can then get bacon king
fries with cheddar sauce.

01:24:31.766 --> 01:24:34.502
You can also get them
without cheddar sauce.

01:24:34.502 --> 01:24:36.538
But here's the ones we've got.

01:24:36.538 --> 01:24:38.173
You can also get chicken wings

01:24:38.173 --> 01:24:40.875
in a four-piece and a eight-piece.

01:24:40.875 --> 01:24:44.579
Here's how they look like.
Just very tiny wings.

01:24:44.579 --> 01:24:48.817
When I was little, we used to
go and vacation in this town

01:24:48.817 --> 01:24:51.920
in the south of Italy
in a very small village,

01:24:51.920 --> 01:24:55.590
and the whole village
on the 15th of August

01:24:55.590 --> 01:24:59.127
was celebrating with something
that we call the Alata.

01:24:59.127 --> 01:25:01.529
Ala means wing in Italian.

01:25:01.529 --> 01:25:04.933
And it was just a big chicken-wings party.

01:25:04.933 --> 01:25:07.735
The ones I'm used to, they
were a little bit bigger

01:25:07.735 --> 01:25:11.573
and a bit more light colored.

01:25:11.573 --> 01:25:14.109
Let's see how this one tastes like.

01:25:16.811 --> 01:25:18.947
Ooh, spicy.

01:25:20.115 --> 01:25:24.385
It's a bit, yeah, a bit of a spicy sauce.

01:25:24.385 --> 01:25:26.488
Yeah, there's a lot of pepper in there.

01:25:26.488 --> 01:25:28.223
No, not a fan.

01:25:28.223 --> 01:25:30.325
Then you can get two types of toast,

01:25:30.325 --> 01:25:33.661
the king toast with Swiss cheese and ham.

01:25:33.661 --> 01:25:37.232
This is the same as in the kids menu.

01:25:37.232 --> 01:25:42.070
And then you can get it with
bacon and American cheese.

01:25:42.070 --> 01:25:45.206
And then we've got griller fries,

01:25:45.206 --> 01:25:48.576
or maybe you call these waffle fries.

01:25:48.576 --> 01:25:52.647
But we actually have some
packaged chips in Italy

01:25:52.647 --> 01:25:54.249
that are sold with this shape.

01:25:54.249 --> 01:25:56.151
Perhaps that's why they
went with the fries.

01:25:56.151 --> 01:25:58.987
There is a tiny bit of spice

01:25:58.987 --> 01:26:02.524
in the aftertaste. Quite nice.

01:26:02.524 --> 01:26:04.826
They're doing waffle fries in Italy.

01:26:04.826 --> 01:26:07.162
That's a direct rip-off
of the Chick-fil-A fries!

01:26:07.162 --> 01:26:09.564
Like, this company is shameless!

01:26:09.564 --> 01:26:12.100
If it's popular somewhere
else, Burger King has it.

01:26:12.100 --> 01:26:13.301
That's their new slogan.

01:26:13.301 --> 01:26:15.470
And then we also have
salads here in Italy.

01:26:15.470 --> 01:26:17.372
Technically there are four options,

01:26:17.372 --> 01:26:20.008
but we were only able to get two.

01:26:20.008 --> 01:26:23.144
So the four options
are just a mixed salad,

01:26:23.144 --> 01:26:26.915
crispy chicken, grilled chicken,

01:26:26.915 --> 01:26:28.216
and a tuna salad,

01:26:28.216 --> 01:26:29.851
which doesn't seem like something

01:26:29.851 --> 01:26:31.386
I would like to get at Burger King.

01:26:31.386 --> 01:26:33.955
Here we have a mixed salad.

01:26:33.955 --> 01:26:37.325
One thing I just, why
are you serving the salad

01:26:37.325 --> 01:26:39.027
with a whole tomato?

01:26:39.027 --> 01:26:41.196
Who eats this? Like, why?

01:26:41.196 --> 01:26:42.397
And we have another one here

01:26:42.397 --> 01:26:45.366
which was supposed to be the
grilled chicken, I think,

01:26:45.366 --> 01:26:50.138
but it's another one of those mixed salads

01:26:50.138 --> 01:26:51.539
with those huge tomatoes.

01:26:51.539 --> 01:26:54.175
The salads can also come
with some olive oil.

01:26:54.175 --> 01:26:56.644
It was actually given to
us in a little sachet,

01:26:56.644 --> 01:26:58.313
but we can't find it.

01:26:58.313 --> 01:26:59.147
Sauce talk.

01:26:59.147 --> 01:27:01.015
Discurso de la salsa.

01:27:01.015 --> 01:27:02.517
Sauce talk.

01:27:02.517 --> 01:27:04.886
Here are all the sauces
that are exclusive to Italy.

01:27:04.886 --> 01:27:08.957
Well, technically exclusive
because they're all from Heinz,

01:27:08.957 --> 01:27:11.292
so you won't find these in the US.

01:27:11.292 --> 01:27:13.061
Heinz makes all the sources here in Italy.

01:27:13.061 --> 01:27:15.163
We start from ketchup,

01:27:15.163 --> 01:27:18.032
then mayo, barbecue,

01:27:18.032 --> 01:27:21.502
sweet and sour sauce, curry mango sauce.

01:27:21.502 --> 01:27:24.305
Then we've got spicy tomato salsa,

01:27:24.305 --> 01:27:27.542
which, hm, sounds interesting.

01:27:27.542 --> 01:27:29.911
And then we've got cream honey mustard.

01:27:29.911 --> 01:27:34.782
The last one, which is not
made by Heinz, is Nocciolata.

01:27:34.782 --> 01:27:36.818
This is technically not a sauce.

01:27:36.818 --> 01:27:39.420
It's a hazelnuts and chocolate spread,

01:27:39.420 --> 01:27:40.488
a bit like Nutella.

01:27:40.488 --> 01:27:42.390
Yeah, this one, Rigoni di Asiago,

01:27:42.390 --> 01:27:46.060
is, some people will
say, the posh Nutella.

01:27:46.060 --> 01:27:49.097
It's a very nice and rich spread.

01:27:49.097 --> 01:27:50.965
Let's see, mango and curry.

01:27:50.965 --> 01:27:52.767
The color I was expecting.

01:27:52.767 --> 01:27:54.569
Nice. I'm surprised it's on the menu.

01:27:54.569 --> 01:27:58.106
Yeah, it does taste like
curry-inspired sauce

01:27:58.106 --> 01:28:00.675
and sweet, so maybe there is mango.

01:28:00.675 --> 01:28:01.976
I love the looks of the mango curry.

01:28:01.976 --> 01:28:03.111
I definitely want one of those.

01:28:03.111 --> 01:28:05.580
Can you please send it to me? Thank you.

01:28:05.580 --> 01:28:08.883
Here are pretty much all the
sauces you can get in the US,

01:28:08.883 --> 01:28:12.387
since they're not Heinz
products, at least not labeled.

01:28:12.387 --> 01:28:13.788
Do you think Burger King
makes their own sauces,

01:28:13.788 --> 01:28:15.690
or do you think they're
just going to the source

01:28:15.690 --> 01:28:16.758
and putting their own labels on it?

01:28:16.758 --> 01:28:19.961
I have no idea. Here we
got a barbecue sauce.

01:28:19.961 --> 01:28:22.163
I would love to try, when I go to Europe,

01:28:22.163 --> 01:28:23.631
like that's happening anytime soon,

01:28:23.631 --> 01:28:25.867
when I go to Europe, I want
to try their barbecue sauce.

01:28:25.867 --> 01:28:28.303
Because I feel like what
they think is barbecue

01:28:28.303 --> 01:28:30.872
and what we call barbecue
can't be the same.

01:28:32.140 --> 01:28:33.775
That's a sweet barbecue sauce.

01:28:33.775 --> 01:28:36.511
I'd liken it to a Kansas
City barbecue. Very good.

01:28:36.511 --> 01:28:38.179
This is the zesty sauce.

01:28:38.179 --> 01:28:41.382
This tastes like a strong
mustard, not honey mustard,

01:28:41.382 --> 01:28:43.017
but sweeter than a regular mustard.

01:28:43.017 --> 01:28:44.452
Actually, it's closer to a Dijon.

01:28:44.452 --> 01:28:47.155
It just says spices.
Doesn't say which ones.

01:28:47.155 --> 01:28:50.191
No. It's not bad, just, I don't want that.

01:28:50.191 --> 01:28:52.226
Sweet and sour sauce.

01:28:52.226 --> 01:28:54.962
Come on! Open like a normal --

01:28:54.962 --> 01:28:59.133
imagine if I was driving,
trying to eat my chicken, ah!

01:29:00.301 --> 01:29:02.804
I'd be on the opposite
side of the road by now,

01:29:02.804 --> 01:29:03.805
crashing into everyone.

01:29:03.805 --> 01:29:04.806
I'd be driving on the sidewalk

01:29:04.806 --> 01:29:06.407
trying to open this sauce.

01:29:06.407 --> 01:29:08.543
All right, sweet and sour, come on.

01:29:08.543 --> 01:29:10.845
Buffalo sauce. For those
of you not in America,

01:29:10.845 --> 01:29:13.915
Buffalo sauce is named
after Buffalo hot wings.

01:29:13.915 --> 01:29:15.883
It's a type of spicy sauce, mm,

01:29:15.883 --> 01:29:17.618
you get wings, and now it's on everything,

01:29:17.618 --> 01:29:19.087
and no, it does not taste like buffaloes.

01:29:19.087 --> 01:29:22.156
It's from Buffalo, New
York, where the sauce was,

01:29:22.156 --> 01:29:25.159
the recipe was made or
perfected, I don't know.

01:29:25.159 --> 01:29:26.761
It's basically hot wing sauce.

01:29:30.098 --> 01:29:31.132
I like Buffalo sauce.

01:29:31.132 --> 01:29:33.267
I don't think -- it's
only good on chicken.

01:29:33.267 --> 01:29:35.336
On burgers or fries or
dipping, doesn't work.

01:29:35.336 --> 01:29:36.838
Last we got ranch.

01:29:36.838 --> 01:29:38.606
This country is obsessed with ranch.

01:29:38.606 --> 01:29:42.176
I don't know why. It's kind of weird.

01:29:42.176 --> 01:29:44.145
But we got everyone in America,

01:29:44.145 --> 01:29:45.780
including Burger King, so,

01:29:45.780 --> 01:29:46.614
ee!

01:29:47.548 --> 01:29:48.649
Ranchy.

01:29:48.649 --> 01:29:50.918
And this is Heinz ketchup.

01:29:50.918 --> 01:29:53.287
Wait, we have Heinz ketchup,
and they have Heinz ketchup,

01:29:53.287 --> 01:29:54.522
so this isn't an exclusive.

01:29:55.923 --> 01:29:57.024
But these sauces are.

01:29:57.024 --> 01:30:00.294
Biscuits. Here in the US, we
have a specific type of biscuit

01:30:00.294 --> 01:30:03.798
that is not a cookie or a
scone, it's its own thing.

01:30:03.798 --> 01:30:06.601
Anyway, we can get just about
every breakfast sandwich

01:30:06.601 --> 01:30:08.736
at Burger King in biscuit form.

01:30:08.736 --> 01:30:10.471
There's the bacon, egg,
and cheese biscuit;

01:30:10.471 --> 01:30:11.939
sausage, egg, and cheese biscuit;

01:30:11.939 --> 01:30:13.708
smoky maple chicken biscuit;

01:30:13.708 --> 01:30:15.543
the ham, egg, and cheese biscuit;

01:30:15.543 --> 01:30:16.978
the egg and cheese biscuit;

01:30:16.978 --> 01:30:18.980
and the fully loaded biscuit.

01:30:18.980 --> 01:30:21.716
I'm not getting all of them.
It's a waste. Here's two.

01:30:21.716 --> 01:30:23.151
I got the bacon, egg, and cheese biscuit.

01:30:23.151 --> 01:30:25.319
Personally, I think when it
comes to breakfast sandwich,

01:30:25.319 --> 01:30:27.388
bacon, egg, and cheese
is the gold standard.

01:30:27.388 --> 01:30:28.623
You can maybe do it a different way,

01:30:28.623 --> 01:30:30.625
but I think bacon, egg, and cheese

01:30:30.625 --> 01:30:33.194
is pretty much the best
breakfast sandwich to get.

01:30:33.194 --> 01:30:34.128
Here it is. There's your egg.

01:30:34.128 --> 01:30:36.097
There's your bacon and
cheese. There's the biscuit.

01:30:36.097 --> 01:30:37.765
It's very dry. I don't
feel like trying it.

01:30:37.765 --> 01:30:40.635
And then also the fully
loaded one. This is hilarious.

01:30:40.635 --> 01:30:42.403
Want to get this? This has got
a little bit of everything.

01:30:42.403 --> 01:30:44.205
Got the egg, got the sausage, got the ham,

01:30:44.205 --> 01:30:46.441
got the cheese, and the bacon.

01:30:46.441 --> 01:30:49.377
How does this look, Italy? Huh?

01:30:49.377 --> 01:30:51.179
Breakfast is served. Let's go!

01:30:51.179 --> 01:30:53.080
Not only do we have that in biscuit form,

01:30:53.080 --> 01:30:56.250
we have the same exact type
of sandwiches in croissant,

01:30:56.250 --> 01:30:58.920
excuse me, Croissan'wich form.

01:30:58.920 --> 01:31:01.556
Once again, Italy, your
neighbors to the north,

01:31:01.556 --> 01:31:04.125
France, they invented the croissant.

01:31:04.125 --> 01:31:05.493
I'm sure all through Europe

01:31:05.493 --> 01:31:07.829
you have amazing pastries,
including croissants.

01:31:07.829 --> 01:31:11.132
Here in the US, we've
absolutely ruined them

01:31:11.132 --> 01:31:12.233
by cutting them in half

01:31:12.233 --> 01:31:14.469
and sticking meat and
cheese in the middle.

01:31:14.469 --> 01:31:16.838
So here we go. We got the
bacon, egg, and cheese.

01:31:16.838 --> 01:31:18.773
Again, the gold standard.

01:31:18.773 --> 01:31:20.374
You can also get a ham, egg, and cheese;

01:31:20.374 --> 01:31:23.478
egg and cheese; smoky maple
chicken Croissan'wich.

01:31:23.478 --> 01:31:25.079
God, that sounds horrible.

01:31:25.079 --> 01:31:27.415
Double sausage, egg, and
cheese, I forgot about that.

01:31:27.415 --> 01:31:30.151
That's two patties of
sausage, two slices of cheese,

01:31:30.151 --> 01:31:31.819
double the diarrhea in the morning.

01:31:31.819 --> 01:31:36.257
And of course, the fully
loaded Croissan'wich.

01:31:36.257 --> 01:31:37.525
Our cricket buddy is back.

01:31:38.960 --> 01:31:41.963
We will try to remove the
cricket audio in post,

01:31:41.963 --> 01:31:43.531
but sorry, everyone, we're filming this

01:31:43.531 --> 01:31:45.433
in the middle of the woods, apparently.

01:31:45.433 --> 01:31:50.104
We have sausage, egg, ham, bacon, cheese,

01:31:50.104 --> 01:31:52.039
oh, God.

01:31:52.039 --> 01:31:54.408
[cricket chirping]

01:31:54.408 --> 01:31:55.643
Cricket, do you want a bite of this?

01:31:55.643 --> 01:31:58.713
We also have breakfast burritos.

01:31:58.713 --> 01:32:01.649
This here is the Egg-Normous Burrito,

01:32:01.649 --> 01:32:04.652
which has bacon, egg, cheese,

01:32:04.652 --> 01:32:07.188
a hash brown, and a spicy sauce.

01:32:07.188 --> 01:32:09.891
This is for someone who
just wants your first hour

01:32:09.891 --> 01:32:11.692
once you punch in at
work to be on the toilet.

01:32:11.692 --> 01:32:13.861
So if you're looking to
poop on company time,

01:32:13.861 --> 01:32:15.596
maybe grab one of these
on the way to work.

01:32:15.596 --> 01:32:16.797
Look at this.

01:32:16.797 --> 01:32:18.599
Guys, this is like,

01:32:18.599 --> 01:32:21.736
oh, I don't even know what this is like.

01:32:21.736 --> 01:32:23.638
I've never seen anything like this.

01:32:23.638 --> 01:32:25.740
So of course I have to try it.

01:32:27.608 --> 01:32:29.143
Nope.

01:32:29.143 --> 01:32:29.977
Gross.

01:32:29.977 --> 01:32:34.982
And this next one is a
breakfast burrito junior.

01:32:34.982 --> 01:32:37.618
So this one's for kids. Want
to get them started young!

01:32:37.618 --> 01:32:38.452
Look what they did!

01:32:38.452 --> 01:32:40.555
They put a hash brown at
the beginning and the end.

01:32:40.555 --> 01:32:41.756
So you're going to be like,

01:32:43.858 --> 01:32:47.461
"Oh, it must be loaded with hash browns.

01:32:47.461 --> 01:32:52.400
Mm-mm, one at the entrance
and the exit. Nice try.

01:32:52.400 --> 01:32:56.203
Also in the US we're crazy about pancakes,

01:32:56.203 --> 01:32:57.538
and we have the pancake platter

01:32:57.538 --> 01:32:59.507
and the pancake and sausage platter,

01:32:59.507 --> 01:33:04.278
currently unavailable at
the Burbank Burger King.

01:33:04.278 --> 01:33:05.680
In Italy, we actually don't have

01:33:05.680 --> 01:33:08.115
a breakfast menu at Burger King.

01:33:08.115 --> 01:33:09.483
To be honest, I don't think Italians

01:33:09.483 --> 01:33:12.653
would like to have what
Joe has in his menu.

01:33:12.653 --> 01:33:15.523
Like, a croissant filled
with bacon and eggs

01:33:15.523 --> 01:33:18.225
doesn't seem quite right.

01:33:18.225 --> 01:33:21.629
I think most of us just
have a sweet breakfast

01:33:21.629 --> 01:33:24.498
that usually is just
a pastry and a coffee.

01:33:24.498 --> 01:33:26.367
It can be a very calorific pastry

01:33:26.367 --> 01:33:29.370
with a lot of Nutella or another filling,

01:33:29.370 --> 01:33:31.772
but usually it's always sweet.

01:33:31.772 --> 01:33:33.374
Sounds like Claudia is implying

01:33:33.374 --> 01:33:36.010
that Italians like something
a little more sweet,

01:33:36.010 --> 01:33:37.845
a baked good for breakfast.

01:33:37.845 --> 01:33:40.281
So, we do have some of those in the US,

01:33:40.281 --> 01:33:42.683
and we do have some of those
obviously at Burger King.

01:33:42.683 --> 01:33:44.318
Going on down here, starting off,

01:33:44.318 --> 01:33:47.722
we got French toast sticks.

01:33:47.722 --> 01:33:49.957
France, as you are aware, is a country

01:33:49.957 --> 01:33:52.593
that's right above Italy, and
they have their own toast,

01:33:52.593 --> 01:33:55.262
and we have that in stick
form, and this is them.

01:33:55.262 --> 01:33:57.465
And it also comes with a dipping syrup.

01:33:57.465 --> 01:33:59.300
What's more French than that?

01:33:59.300 --> 01:34:01.402
Look at this. Look at this.

01:34:01.402 --> 01:34:02.937
I know it's "Food Wars" Italy,

01:34:02.937 --> 01:34:06.307
but "Food Wars" France has gotta
be right around the corner.

01:34:06.307 --> 01:34:08.576
Any French person watching this right now

01:34:08.576 --> 01:34:10.344
is going to have a heart attack.

01:34:10.344 --> 01:34:11.979
But yeah, you know, I mean.

01:34:13.447 --> 01:34:15.249
You have no idea how sweet this is.

01:34:15.249 --> 01:34:18.886
Also, we have these hash brown
bites, these little guys.

01:34:20.321 --> 01:34:22.189
Desserts, sweets!

01:34:22.189 --> 01:34:24.725
Oh, how we have it in the
US at our Burger King.

01:34:24.725 --> 01:34:26.927
You can get a Hershey's sundae pie.

01:34:26.927 --> 01:34:28.295
Not Sunday day of the week.

01:34:28.295 --> 01:34:32.133
Sundae as in a

01:34:32.133 --> 01:34:34.068
ice cream sundae, right?

01:34:34.068 --> 01:34:36.037
And I mean, I mean, look at this.

01:34:36.037 --> 01:34:38.406
Look at this! Right?

01:34:38.406 --> 01:34:42.176
Look at this, how gooey
that is. Ooh! Come on.

01:34:44.145 --> 01:34:47.281
Also at Burger King, you can
get soft-serve ice cream.

01:34:47.281 --> 01:34:49.583
I didn't get it because
we've been in the studio

01:34:49.583 --> 01:34:51.085
for a couple hours and it's very hot,

01:34:51.085 --> 01:34:51.919
and it would've melt.

01:34:51.919 --> 01:34:54.889
Anyway, you can also get
chocolate chip cookies,

01:34:54.889 --> 01:34:56.257
hey!

01:34:56.257 --> 01:34:58.893
And a variety of shakes, a vanilla shake,

01:34:58.893 --> 01:35:01.328
a chocolate shake, a chocolate Oreo shake,

01:35:01.328 --> 01:35:03.731
and this, the Oreo shake.

01:35:03.731 --> 01:35:05.599
Every time we do a fast-food place

01:35:05.599 --> 01:35:08.369
that has a shake, the
Oreo shake, I get it.

01:35:08.369 --> 01:35:13.207
I think that Oreo, as far as
branded cookie snack shakes

01:35:13.207 --> 01:35:14.842
you get at a lot of
these fast-food places,

01:35:14.842 --> 01:35:16.877
the Oreo is the best one.

01:35:16.877 --> 01:35:18.012
Why, do you ask?

01:35:18.012 --> 01:35:20.781
Looks like a vanilla and
chocolate shake, right? Wrong.

01:35:20.781 --> 01:35:25.052
It isn't vanilla, it's the
Oreo-cream-flavored shake

01:35:25.052 --> 01:35:27.221
with Oreo chocolate cookies in it.

01:35:27.221 --> 01:35:30.925
Just, I'm telling you,
oh, my God, so good.

01:35:30.925 --> 01:35:33.227
Oreo is the best shake, hands down.

01:35:33.227 --> 01:35:34.662
Mm!

01:35:34.662 --> 01:35:37.565
So, on to the dessert
options here in Italy,

01:35:37.565 --> 01:35:39.967
these are the ones that
we were able to get,

01:35:39.967 --> 01:35:42.203
but actually there are a bunch of others,

01:35:42.203 --> 01:35:44.338
and we're going to put
them all on screen here.

01:35:44.338 --> 01:35:48.476
That includes a lot of
ice cream, like sundaes

01:35:48.476 --> 01:35:52.012
and milkshakes, but we
were not able to get them.

01:35:52.012 --> 01:35:53.414
So this is what we've got today.

01:35:53.414 --> 01:35:55.683
We've got Nocciolata pancakes,

01:35:55.683 --> 01:35:59.320
and then we've got nutty cheesecake,

01:35:59.320 --> 01:36:01.355
crown caramel soufflé.

01:36:01.355 --> 01:36:04.291
I think if you call something
lava cake, you will expect,

01:36:04.291 --> 01:36:06.594
I mean, I'm sure, like,
half of your customers

01:36:06.594 --> 01:36:08.863
will think that you
actually put lava in there.

01:36:08.863 --> 01:36:10.064
Yeah, and I was saying earlier,

01:36:10.064 --> 01:36:12.566
Nocciolata is actually a very
popular spread here in Italy.

01:36:12.566 --> 01:36:14.535
It's a hazelnut and chocolate spread.

01:36:14.535 --> 01:36:18.906
I was expecting it to be much thicker.

01:36:18.906 --> 01:36:20.207
Let's see.

01:36:24.812 --> 01:36:26.947
Quite nice.

01:36:26.947 --> 01:36:29.183
Yeah, the pancakes are OK.

01:36:29.183 --> 01:36:30.651
It's really delicious.

01:36:30.651 --> 01:36:32.019
It tastes much stronger,

01:36:32.019 --> 01:36:35.990
much more like hazelnuts
than Nutella does.

01:36:35.990 --> 01:36:38.592
Like, these two are competitors.

01:36:38.592 --> 01:36:40.094
Approved.

01:36:40.094 --> 01:36:42.363
We can also get some milkshakes.

01:36:42.363 --> 01:36:46.634
The exclusive ones are
Nesquik, Nescafé, and Oreo.

01:36:46.634 --> 01:36:49.003
Drinks in the US Burger
King, we have a lot.

01:36:49.003 --> 01:36:50.638
Fountain drinks, for instance.

01:36:50.638 --> 01:36:51.739
It's a fountain-drink cup.

01:36:51.739 --> 01:36:54.175
I wasn't going to get all these
because it's just super hot,

01:36:54.175 --> 01:36:55.676
and it's a pain in the
butt to get the stuff here.

01:36:55.676 --> 01:36:57.077
All the other drinks have melted.

01:36:57.077 --> 01:36:59.113
I told you I'm wearing this
shirt. It's hot in here!

01:36:59.113 --> 01:37:01.215
We have something called frozen drinks.

01:37:01.215 --> 01:37:04.018
You can get a frozen Coke
and a frozen wild cherry

01:37:04.018 --> 01:37:07.054
and also a frozen blue raspberry,
which is not available.

01:37:07.054 --> 01:37:10.724
This was more of a slush consistency

01:37:10.724 --> 01:37:14.295
before it melted in this
80-degree studio. What?

01:37:14.295 --> 01:37:16.831
Oh, we also got milk. OK.

01:37:16.831 --> 01:37:20.901
Anyway, I mean, not bad.

01:37:20.901 --> 01:37:21.802
I mean, it's still pretty cold.

01:37:21.802 --> 01:37:26.006
But, yeah, usually this is
a lot more icelike, icy.

01:37:26.006 --> 01:37:28.342
There's a wild cherry, oh, yeah.

01:37:28.342 --> 01:37:30.377
We have coffee drinks. You
can get an iced coffee,

01:37:30.377 --> 01:37:33.147
this used to have ice
in it, and a hot coffee.

01:37:33.147 --> 01:37:36.183
And, of course, who doesn't like to relax

01:37:36.183 --> 01:37:39.753
with a room-temperature fat-free milk?

01:37:39.753 --> 01:37:41.355
That'll wash down your burger.

01:37:41.355 --> 01:37:42.556
Here are all the drinks

01:37:42.556 --> 01:37:45.626
that are exclusive to Italy Burger King,

01:37:45.626 --> 01:37:49.797
starting from this very
cute Pago orange juice.

01:37:49.797 --> 01:37:52.166
Then we got some tea.

01:37:52.166 --> 01:37:56.070
We've got peach and rose, fancy,

01:37:56.070 --> 01:37:58.806
and lemon and lemongrass.

01:37:58.806 --> 01:38:01.075
We've got Monster Energy,

01:38:01.075 --> 01:38:05.112
which has been delivered
in a bit of a funny shape.

01:38:05.112 --> 01:38:06.513
And then we've got beer.

01:38:06.513 --> 01:38:09.216
You can either get Heineken or Ichnusa,

01:38:09.216 --> 01:38:11.385
which is a Sardinian beer.

01:38:11.385 --> 01:38:15.723
Some Burger Kings will also
serve a full range of coffees,

01:38:15.723 --> 01:38:18.993
espresso coffees, because
that's what coffee means to us.

01:38:18.993 --> 01:38:21.762
But because we got our
food and drinks delivered,

01:38:21.762 --> 01:38:24.064
we actually were not
able to select coffee,

01:38:24.064 --> 01:38:25.933
so we couldn't get any today.

01:38:29.036 --> 01:38:31.839
Burger King, in my point of view,

01:38:31.839 --> 01:38:34.508
is like fast food's little brother.

01:38:34.508 --> 01:38:38.612
It's always trying to
be like the big dogs.

01:38:38.612 --> 01:38:40.214
It's always trying to be like McDonald's.

01:38:40.214 --> 01:38:42.650
It's always like whatever is good,

01:38:42.650 --> 01:38:47.521
Burger King has kind of a
later, crummier version of it.

01:38:47.521 --> 01:38:50.758
Now, I will say, the Whopper
is a fantastic sandwich.

01:38:50.758 --> 01:38:53.427
I love the Whopper. I get it occasionally.

01:38:53.427 --> 01:38:56.063
But everything else on Burger
King's menu, thumbs down,

01:38:56.063 --> 01:38:57.364
or at least there's something else

01:38:57.364 --> 01:38:59.967
that's better than
whatever they're offering.

01:38:59.967 --> 01:39:01.635
You know, Burger King, I only eat there

01:39:01.635 --> 01:39:05.773
when it's the ultimate
convenience, which is rare,

01:39:05.773 --> 01:39:07.341
because I don't know if a lot of people

01:39:07.341 --> 01:39:10.778
outside of the US knew this,
but Burger King's strategy

01:39:10.778 --> 01:39:15.115
is to build a location
close to a McDonald's.

01:39:15.115 --> 01:39:18.085
Did you know that? So McDonald's
does all this research

01:39:18.085 --> 01:39:21.355
about where to position their
restaurants strategically,

01:39:21.355 --> 01:39:24.591
you know, traffic patterns,

01:39:24.591 --> 01:39:26.660
rent and locations, all that stuff.

01:39:26.660 --> 01:39:27.995
McDonald's has a whole
department of people

01:39:27.995 --> 01:39:29.663
to figure that out, and
then Burger King's like,

01:39:29.663 --> 01:39:30.798
"All right, we'll build
one across the street

01:39:30.798 --> 01:39:32.633
from that McDonald's." That's for real!

01:39:32.633 --> 01:39:34.268
Like, that's their vibe on everything.

01:39:34.268 --> 01:39:35.936
So I don't know what it's
like in other countries,

01:39:35.936 --> 01:39:39.173
but in Burger King, you're
just like, "Oh, Burger King."

01:39:39.173 --> 01:39:41.075
In Italy, I think Burger King

01:39:41.075 --> 01:39:44.845
goes pretty much hand
in hand with McDonald's.

01:39:44.845 --> 01:39:47.715
Obviously it's been there
for a little bit less time.

01:39:47.715 --> 01:39:49.583
Burger King is quite popular in Italy.

01:39:49.583 --> 01:39:53.287
They currently have 232 outlets.

01:39:53.287 --> 01:39:57.057
KFC has only got 50
branches here in Italy.

01:39:57.057 --> 01:39:59.159
Although they are still behind McDonald's.

01:39:59.159 --> 01:40:02.296
That has 630 branches.

01:40:02.296 --> 01:40:04.298
Like, some of us have, most of us

01:40:04.298 --> 01:40:06.200
have celebrated birthdays at McDonald's.

01:40:06.200 --> 01:40:08.936
So obviously we do have some memories

01:40:08.936 --> 01:40:11.739
and something that brings us back to it.

01:40:11.739 --> 01:40:14.041
I think it's also a
little bit more expensive

01:40:14.041 --> 01:40:17.578
compared to McDonald's, and
maybe that's one of the reasons

01:40:17.578 --> 01:40:21.415
why people would choose
one instead of the other.

01:40:21.415 --> 01:40:24.785
Even though there are some
Italian ingredients in the menu,

01:40:24.785 --> 01:40:28.222
Burger King is still
pretty much considered

01:40:28.222 --> 01:40:31.091
the American option or, like,

01:40:31.091 --> 01:40:33.827
the American fast-food chain,

01:40:33.827 --> 01:40:35.929
whereas McDonald's has sort of

01:40:35.929 --> 01:40:38.265
got rid of the "American" fast-food chain.

01:40:38.265 --> 01:40:41.402
It's just the fast-food
chain, if that makes sense.

01:40:41.402 --> 01:40:43.203
They are the first chain that has removed

01:40:43.203 --> 01:40:46.106
preservatives and colorants from food,

01:40:46.106 --> 01:40:48.776
but there are quite a few
items that we've seen today

01:40:48.776 --> 01:40:51.745
that look very shiny and very colorful,

01:40:51.745 --> 01:40:53.313
and I would really like to know,

01:40:53.313 --> 01:40:56.250
how do you make your cheese
so yellow without colorants?

01:40:56.250 --> 01:40:59.953
Like, why? Like, how is that
even possible naturally?

01:40:59.953 --> 01:41:04.191
Rivals, I don't know, would you
consider McDonald's a rival?

01:41:04.191 --> 01:41:06.827
That's like me saying The Rock's my rival.

01:41:06.827 --> 01:41:10.164
Like, yeah, rivals, but, like, come on.

01:41:10.164 --> 01:41:11.365
I don't think he's sweating

01:41:11.365 --> 01:41:13.734
that I'm out there doing videos as well.

01:41:15.502 --> 01:41:18.205
There's no, no one's, I
mean, Wendy's, I guess.

01:41:21.141 --> 01:41:22.676
Let's talk about prices.

01:41:22.676 --> 01:41:26.346
In Italy, a Whopper is 6 euros, 50 cents,

01:41:26.346 --> 01:41:29.716
which is about $7.27.

01:41:29.716 --> 01:41:32.453
If you want to make that a
meal with a medium-sized drink

01:41:32.453 --> 01:41:35.689
and medium fries, that's
going to cost you 11 euros,

01:41:35.689 --> 01:41:39.059
and that's about $12.30.

01:41:39.059 --> 01:41:42.729
And in the US, a Whopper
will cost you $6.89,

01:41:42.729 --> 01:41:47.267
or 6 euros and 16 eurobytes.

01:41:47.267 --> 01:41:49.636
I don't know what the, what? Is it cents?

01:41:49.636 --> 01:41:51.338
All right, everyone, relax. It's cents.

01:41:51.338 --> 01:41:52.339
There you go, all right.

01:41:52.339 --> 01:41:53.173
[beep]

01:41:53.173 --> 01:41:55.309
So 6 euros and 16 cents.

01:41:55.309 --> 01:41:59.947
Now, that's a 6% decrease in
price. How do you like that?

01:41:59.947 --> 01:42:01.748
If you're making a meal
with a medium fries

01:42:01.748 --> 01:42:05.319
and medium drink, it'll cost you $12.18,

01:42:05.319 --> 01:42:09.289
or 10 euros and 95 eurocents.

01:42:09.289 --> 01:42:12.326
So, it actually works out
cheaper to get a Whopper meal

01:42:12.326 --> 01:42:16.497
in the US rather than in
Italy, but just by a few cents.

01:42:16.497 --> 01:42:18.432
12 bucks? Uh,

01:42:18.432 --> 01:42:20.834
I guess I'm used to it,
but come to think of it,

01:42:20.834 --> 01:42:25.739
it's a lot more expensive
than what I initially thought.

01:42:25.739 --> 01:42:27.174
Yeah, I mean, I don't even
think it's that good of a deal.

01:42:27.174 --> 01:42:28.175
It's not, like, too expensive,

01:42:28.175 --> 01:42:31.044
but I think almost 13 bucks or whatever,

01:42:31.044 --> 01:42:32.346
12-something plus tax for all this

01:42:32.346 --> 01:42:36.884
is like, ugh, might as
well get something better.

01:42:36.884 --> 01:42:38.485
The prices seem fair.

01:42:38.485 --> 01:42:40.721
It is a little bit more
expensive than McDonald's,

01:42:40.721 --> 01:42:43.023
but also the burgers
are a little bit bigger,

01:42:43.023 --> 01:42:45.092
and it's definitely almost half the price

01:42:45.092 --> 01:42:46.527
as, like, a Five Guys.

01:42:46.527 --> 01:42:48.128
I think 11 euros is fair,

01:42:48.128 --> 01:42:52.166
but if you start getting
close to, like, 15,

01:42:52.166 --> 01:42:53.100
that's where I think

01:42:53.100 --> 01:42:55.836
I would like to sit down at a restaurant,

01:42:55.836 --> 01:42:58.805
and that's probably the
price of a main course,

01:42:58.805 --> 01:43:00.574
like a restaurant here in Milan.

01:43:00.574 --> 01:43:03.977
So 11 euros was just below,

01:43:03.977 --> 01:43:06.346
just below the restaurant line, let's say.

01:43:08.849 --> 01:43:12.386
As the Whopper is Burger
King's No. 1 bestselling item,

01:43:12.386 --> 01:43:14.788
we thought we would
compare them nutritionally.

01:43:14.788 --> 01:43:18.859
In Italy, a Whopper contains 683 calories.

01:43:18.859 --> 01:43:21.795
Our US Whopper contains all this.

01:43:21.795 --> 01:43:24.131
If you make that a meal
by adding medium fries

01:43:24.131 --> 01:43:27.000
and a medium Coke, the total is this.

01:43:27.000 --> 01:43:30.437
Making the grand total this.

01:43:30.437 --> 01:43:33.073
The most calorific item on the menu here

01:43:33.073 --> 01:43:35.976
is the bacon king 3.0,

01:43:35.976 --> 01:43:39.580
at 1,342 calories.

01:43:39.580 --> 01:43:43.050
That is a lot for a burger.

01:43:43.050 --> 01:43:45.719
Our bacon king is also the
most calorific single item

01:43:45.719 --> 01:43:49.890
on the menu, at 1,200 calories. Oof.

01:43:49.890 --> 01:43:51.892
Claudia: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:43:51.892 --> 01:43:53.927
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:43:53.927 --> 01:43:56.863
between Five Guys in Italy and the US.

01:43:56.863 --> 01:43:58.532
This is "Food Wars."

01:44:00.901 --> 01:44:05.005
Burgers in Italy come in two
sizes, little and regular.

01:44:05.005 --> 01:44:07.941
Little has one patty, and regular has two.

01:44:07.941 --> 01:44:11.545
Our burgers also come in two
sizes, little and regular.

01:44:11.545 --> 01:44:13.981
Let's weigh a regular plain
hamburger in both countries

01:44:13.981 --> 01:44:16.283
to see who has the bigger burgers.

01:44:16.283 --> 01:44:20.954
That's 136 grams.

01:44:20.954 --> 01:44:23.523
Nico: 138 grams.

01:44:23.523 --> 01:44:27.527
The burger mark is really off-putting.

01:44:27.527 --> 01:44:29.796
Any difference might
be down to the patties.

01:44:29.796 --> 01:44:32.165
Five Guys actually tells
us that the US patties

01:44:32.165 --> 01:44:35.469
should weigh about 94
grams each, or 3.3 ounces,

01:44:35.469 --> 01:44:37.771
although this will be the
weight before cooking.

01:44:37.771 --> 01:44:39.773
The Five Guys Italy website says

01:44:39.773 --> 01:44:43.610
that the patties when uncooked
should weigh 67 grams,

01:44:43.610 --> 01:44:45.579
so we're going to see if that's true.

01:44:45.579 --> 01:44:46.947
Obviously this has been cooked,

01:44:46.947 --> 01:44:49.416
so the meat should have released some fat,

01:44:49.416 --> 01:44:51.685
but we're going to find out soon.

01:44:51.685 --> 01:44:53.720
This is a Five Guys hot dog.

01:44:53.720 --> 01:44:54.988
It looks a little weird

01:44:54.988 --> 01:44:56.990
because they slice them down
the middle to cook them.

01:44:56.990 --> 01:45:00.327
I really love how these
cook when they're sliced.

01:45:00.327 --> 01:45:02.062
Let's measure the length first.

01:45:02.062 --> 01:45:05.065
That's about 16.2 centimeters.

01:45:05.065 --> 01:45:09.102
I think that's about 15 centimeters.

01:45:09.102 --> 01:45:10.637
Yeah, 6 inches.

01:45:10.637 --> 01:45:13.006
We don't use inches in Italy.

01:45:13.006 --> 01:45:15.509
Now let's weigh the plain hot dog.

01:45:15.509 --> 01:45:18.345
That is 144 grams.

01:45:18.345 --> 01:45:20.080
We're now going to weigh it.

01:45:20.080 --> 01:45:21.682
So, just for reference,

01:45:21.682 --> 01:45:25.252
we put mustard, ketchup,
and onions in this hot dog,

01:45:25.252 --> 01:45:27.020
so obviously it's going
to be a bit heavier

01:45:27.020 --> 01:45:29.289
than the regular one. Let's see.

01:45:29.289 --> 01:45:32.159
195 grams.

01:45:32.159 --> 01:45:33.860
Our fries come in three sizes

01:45:33.860 --> 01:45:35.729
in either plain or Cajun spice.

01:45:35.729 --> 01:45:38.899
You can get little, regular, or large.

01:45:38.899 --> 01:45:41.735
Our Five Guys fries come in three sizes,

01:45:41.735 --> 01:45:44.204
either plain or with Cajun spice.

01:45:44.204 --> 01:45:46.640
Little, regular, and large.

01:45:46.640 --> 01:45:50.310
According to Five Guys, the
little should weigh 227 grams.

01:45:50.310 --> 01:45:51.912
Let's see if that's true.

01:45:51.912 --> 01:45:55.015
It's not. It's 82 grams.

01:45:55.015 --> 01:45:56.750
This is 82, oh, wait,

01:45:57.517 --> 01:45:59.319
yeah, it's 82 grams.

01:45:59.319 --> 01:46:02.989
Our little fries should weigh 256 grams.

01:46:02.989 --> 01:46:04.358
103 grams.

01:46:04.358 --> 01:46:07.060
So, we did ask a Five Guys employee

01:46:07.060 --> 01:46:09.663
about how they package their fries.

01:46:09.663 --> 01:46:11.865
They scoop the fries
into one of these cups,

01:46:11.865 --> 01:46:14.601
put that in the bag, and
then they do another scoop

01:46:14.601 --> 01:46:16.837
of fries on top, I think.

01:46:16.837 --> 01:46:18.171
So that could be the reason why

01:46:18.171 --> 01:46:19.506
some of these weights are off.

01:46:19.506 --> 01:46:21.475
There's just, like, fries everywhere.

01:46:21.475 --> 01:46:24.211
Don't really know which
fry came from which cup.

01:46:24.211 --> 01:46:25.545
It's a mess.

01:46:25.545 --> 01:46:29.316
We're supposed to have
1,225 grams altogether,

01:46:29.316 --> 01:46:32.452
but right now we're sitting at 870 grams,

01:46:32.452 --> 01:46:35.522
including the "extra fries,"
which aren't really extra.

01:46:35.522 --> 01:46:38.792
So, our total should
have been 1,220 grams,

01:46:38.792 --> 01:46:41.161
but we got 580 grams.

01:46:41.161 --> 01:46:43.196
So that's less than half.

01:46:43.196 --> 01:46:45.732
Milkshakes in Italy come in one size,

01:46:45.732 --> 01:46:48.668
and this is supposed
to be 400 milliliters.

01:46:48.668 --> 01:46:50.137
So, this is the vanilla milkshake.

01:46:50.137 --> 01:46:53.006
In the US, I believe we only
have one size of milkshake.

01:46:53.006 --> 01:46:55.142
So let's see how much we get.

01:46:55.142 --> 01:46:57.210
It's actually almost 500.

01:46:57.210 --> 01:46:58.712
I'll say it's, like,

01:46:58.712 --> 01:47:02.349
480 millimeters.

01:47:02.349 --> 01:47:03.884
Something around that.

01:47:06.086 --> 01:47:08.288
Here's everything you'll
find at Five Guys in the US

01:47:08.288 --> 01:47:09.956
that you won't find in Italy.

01:47:09.956 --> 01:47:12.426
Here's everything you'll
find at Five Guys Italy

01:47:12.426 --> 01:47:14.394
that you won't find in the US.

01:47:14.394 --> 01:47:15.829
The owners of Five Guys like to keep

01:47:15.829 --> 01:47:17.831
the restaurants and
the menus all the same,

01:47:17.831 --> 01:47:21.034
so there aren't any exclusive
burger options in the US.

01:47:21.034 --> 01:47:23.570
This is the Five Guys burger menu.

01:47:23.570 --> 01:47:26.440
So, our burger menus are
almost exactly the same.

01:47:26.440 --> 01:47:27.974
The only difference is that here

01:47:27.974 --> 01:47:31.845
you can order two additional
patties, not just one.

01:47:31.845 --> 01:47:36.116
So you end up with a burger
with four patties in it.

01:47:36.116 --> 01:47:37.684
I'm not sure you can do that in the US.

01:47:37.684 --> 01:47:39.219
Maybe if you ask nicely.

01:47:39.219 --> 01:47:41.888
But it's an official feature here.

01:47:41.888 --> 01:47:44.524
Since Five Guys is known for
its customizable options,

01:47:44.524 --> 01:47:47.861
you probably could order two
extra patties for your burger,

01:47:47.861 --> 01:47:50.096
but we'll let you have this one, Claudia.

01:47:50.096 --> 01:47:51.631
But seeing as America doesn't have

01:47:51.631 --> 01:47:53.433
official exclusive menu items,

01:47:53.433 --> 01:47:55.602
Five Guys enthusiasts had to get creative

01:47:55.602 --> 01:47:59.072
and make their own in the form
of an unofficial secret menu.

01:47:59.072 --> 01:48:00.240
So, this is the patty melt.

01:48:00.240 --> 01:48:03.677
It's a grilled cheese sandwich
with an extra patty inside.

01:48:03.677 --> 01:48:05.512
It looks kind of good to me.

01:48:05.512 --> 01:48:08.515
I love when restaurants do grilled cheeses

01:48:08.515 --> 01:48:10.217
with the buns of the burgers.

01:48:10.217 --> 01:48:11.651
I think it tastes so good.

01:48:13.820 --> 01:48:16.923
I feel like I like this better
than the Five Guys burgers.

01:48:16.923 --> 01:48:19.526
It's something about the way
the bread gets all toasty.

01:48:19.526 --> 01:48:21.728
It just makes it so much more delicious!

01:48:21.728 --> 01:48:24.631
So, next is the artery annihilator.

01:48:24.631 --> 01:48:26.900
That's a little ridiculous.

01:48:26.900 --> 01:48:29.236
So, we have to put a bacon hot dog

01:48:29.236 --> 01:48:32.305
inside of a bacon cheeseburger.

01:48:32.305 --> 01:48:34.741
How I'm going to do that, I don't know.

01:48:34.741 --> 01:48:38.678
What I think is right is
making it edible in some form,

01:48:38.678 --> 01:48:40.881
so I'm just going to break it up a little.

01:48:43.783 --> 01:48:45.519
I'm trying to squish it
down because it's not

01:48:45.519 --> 01:48:48.388
going to fit into my mouth. OK.

01:48:51.858 --> 01:48:53.193
This literally sucks.

01:48:53.193 --> 01:48:54.828
Like, don't order this.

01:48:54.828 --> 01:48:56.129
There's no reason for you to --

01:48:56.129 --> 01:48:58.031
if you want a hot dog and a burger ...

01:49:00.033 --> 01:49:01.968
let me swallow this stupid bite of food.

01:49:01.968 --> 01:49:02.802
Hold on.

01:49:02.802 --> 01:49:05.238
I feel like putting the
hot dog into the burger

01:49:05.238 --> 01:49:07.474
doesn't make it taste any better.

01:49:07.474 --> 01:49:09.242
It just makes it a lot harder to eat

01:49:09.242 --> 01:49:11.611
and a lot less enjoyable of an experience,

01:49:11.611 --> 01:49:15.048
so I think this is really not fun or good.

01:49:15.048 --> 01:49:16.750
To me, I think this should be at the top.

01:49:16.750 --> 01:49:18.451
So let's try.

01:49:18.451 --> 01:49:19.586
Double bread?

01:49:19.586 --> 01:49:21.288
Yeah, there's a bit of sauce.

01:49:21.288 --> 01:49:23.123
All right.

01:49:23.123 --> 01:49:26.126
So, here's your Italian version.

01:49:26.126 --> 01:49:28.061
Artery annihilator, right?

01:49:28.061 --> 01:49:30.196
I don't know. I feel like this is

01:49:30.196 --> 01:49:32.399
annihilating my eyesight as well

01:49:32.399 --> 01:49:35.535
on top of my arteries if I were to try it.

01:49:41.575 --> 01:49:42.776
Too much stuff.

01:49:42.776 --> 01:49:44.244
Five Guys is of course famous

01:49:44.244 --> 01:49:46.680
for its wide selection of free toppings.

01:49:46.680 --> 01:49:50.083
According to Five Guys,
there are over 250,000 ways

01:49:50.083 --> 01:49:51.384
to customize your burger.

01:49:51.384 --> 01:49:53.086
Now, these aren't exclusive toppings,

01:49:53.086 --> 01:49:54.788
but here's what you can get.

01:49:54.788 --> 01:49:56.957
The only exclusive
topping we have in America

01:49:56.957 --> 01:49:58.191
is A.1. sauce.

01:49:58.191 --> 01:50:00.794
In Italy, the toppings are
almost exactly the same

01:50:00.794 --> 01:50:04.030
as in the US, but we do
have one exclusive sauce,

01:50:04.030 --> 01:50:05.799
which is the HP sauce.

01:50:05.799 --> 01:50:07.367
According to chefs at Five Guys,

01:50:07.367 --> 01:50:08.702
when customizing your burger,

01:50:08.702 --> 01:50:11.304
there's a specific way
it has to be stacked

01:50:11.304 --> 01:50:12.439
within their rules.

01:50:12.439 --> 01:50:14.307
It should be the bottom bun;

01:50:14.307 --> 01:50:17.744
then any wet items, like
grilled onions or mushrooms;

01:50:17.744 --> 01:50:20.113
then the first patty;
two slices of cheese;

01:50:20.113 --> 01:50:21.681
then another patty;

01:50:21.681 --> 01:50:23.650
then dry items like lettuce, tomatoes,

01:50:23.650 --> 01:50:24.985
and jalapeños go on top;

01:50:24.985 --> 01:50:27.787
and then there's the top
bun to finish it all off.

01:50:27.787 --> 01:50:29.255
Let's see if it came in the order

01:50:29.255 --> 01:50:30.890
that it's supposed to come in.

01:50:30.890 --> 01:50:34.294
So, at the bottom I
see the grilled onions,

01:50:34.294 --> 01:50:35.528
I see grilled mushrooms,

01:50:35.528 --> 01:50:38.965
and I also see peppers, green peppers.

01:50:38.965 --> 01:50:40.467
So it's already out of order

01:50:40.467 --> 01:50:43.269
because the jalapeños are on
the bottom for some reason.

01:50:43.269 --> 01:50:45.805
I feel like, I don't
know, I feel like this,

01:50:45.805 --> 01:50:48.775
if it doesn't affect the taste,
I personally do not care.

01:50:48.775 --> 01:50:51.244
But if it's their law in the Five Guys,

01:50:51.244 --> 01:50:53.647
then I guess you should
be doing it. I don't know.

01:50:53.647 --> 01:50:55.715
All right, so we got the first patty,

01:50:55.715 --> 01:50:57.984
the two slices of cheese, another patty,

01:50:57.984 --> 01:51:00.687
and then on top we have
the lettuce and tomatoes.

01:51:00.687 --> 01:51:03.890
Let's check if the order
is the same here in Italy.

01:51:03.890 --> 01:51:07.794
So, yes, we got bottom
bun, onions and mushrooms.

01:51:07.794 --> 01:51:11.064
We got a patty, cheese,

01:51:11.064 --> 01:51:13.767
we got another patty,

01:51:13.767 --> 01:51:16.803
tomatoes, and lettuce at the top.

01:51:16.803 --> 01:51:18.271
Good job, Five Guys.

01:51:18.271 --> 01:51:20.373
Five Guys also offers sandwich options.

01:51:20.373 --> 01:51:22.642
There aren't any exclusive
sandwiches in the US,

01:51:22.642 --> 01:51:23.777
but here's what you can get.

01:51:23.777 --> 01:51:27.280
So, we have a grilled cheese,
a BLT, and a veggie sandwich.

01:51:27.280 --> 01:51:28.982
Veggie sandwich.

01:51:30.884 --> 01:51:31.951
Mm-mm.

01:51:33.219 --> 01:51:34.320
It's not bad,

01:51:34.320 --> 01:51:36.956
it's just a little too
vegetable-heavy for me.

01:51:36.956 --> 01:51:37.757
No.

01:51:38.858 --> 01:51:42.495
Next is the BLT, which,
if you mess this up ...

01:51:46.633 --> 01:51:48.368
Yeah, it tastes like an OK BLT.

01:51:48.368 --> 01:51:50.303
It just mostly tastes like bacon.

01:51:50.303 --> 01:51:51.871
And then we have the grilled cheese,

01:51:51.871 --> 01:51:53.006
which I think will be good

01:51:53.006 --> 01:51:54.774
because I already liked the patty melt,

01:51:54.774 --> 01:51:56.276
and they're like sisters.

01:51:58.912 --> 01:52:00.280
That's a really good grilled cheese.

01:52:00.280 --> 01:52:02.048
We do have one exclusive in Italy,

01:52:02.048 --> 01:52:04.517
which is a BLT sandwich with cheese,

01:52:04.517 --> 01:52:07.520
which is supposed to be this one,

01:52:07.520 --> 01:52:11.291
but there's been a bit
of a mix-up in the order,

01:52:11.291 --> 01:52:14.894
and the one we got has just
cheese and a lot of bacon.

01:52:14.894 --> 01:52:17.630
There aren't any exclusive
Five Guys hot-dog options

01:52:17.630 --> 01:52:20.033
in either country, but
here's what you can get.

01:52:20.033 --> 01:52:21.701
A hot dog, a bacon dog,

01:52:21.701 --> 01:52:24.370
a cheese dog, or a bacon cheese dog.

01:52:24.370 --> 01:52:26.873
I've never had a hot
dog with cheese on it,

01:52:26.873 --> 01:52:28.675
so I am kind of intrigued.

01:52:28.675 --> 01:52:32.545
I will say, though, I am a
fan of the slicing the hot dog

01:52:32.545 --> 01:52:34.948
and putting this side on the griddle,

01:52:34.948 --> 01:52:36.816
just so everything gets nice and crispy.

01:52:36.816 --> 01:52:38.785
I think they do taste better that way.

01:52:41.354 --> 01:52:43.523
It's not for me.
Something about the cheese

01:52:43.523 --> 01:52:45.959
and the hot dog mixing
together feels wrong,

01:52:45.959 --> 01:52:48.762
because I've never had it. It feels weird.

01:52:48.762 --> 01:52:53.333
So, this is the bacon and cheese hot dog.

01:52:53.333 --> 01:52:54.334
Looks pretty good to me,

01:52:54.334 --> 01:52:57.604
but I'm not really familiar with hot dogs.

01:52:57.604 --> 01:53:00.573
I think in general in Italy we
don't really have that many.

01:53:00.573 --> 01:53:03.143
Definitely burgers are more popular.

01:53:06.179 --> 01:53:08.081
Yeah, maybe with some sauce
it would be a bit better.

01:53:08.081 --> 01:53:11.351
In the US, we have two
exclusive milkshake options,

01:53:11.351 --> 01:53:13.887
the Oreo creme and the Double Stuf,

01:53:13.887 --> 01:53:15.655
which I am very excited about.

01:53:15.655 --> 01:53:17.657
I love Oreos, and Oreo milkshakes

01:53:17.657 --> 01:53:19.325
are objectively the best milkshake.

01:53:19.325 --> 01:53:21.261
Let's try the Oreo creme first.

01:53:21.261 --> 01:53:24.831
So, this is just the filling
of the Oreos, essentially.

01:53:24.831 --> 01:53:26.766
OK, give it a good swirl.

01:53:26.766 --> 01:53:29.135
And it is creme and not cream.

01:53:31.671 --> 01:53:33.039
That is literally so good.

01:53:33.039 --> 01:53:37.210
You're actually drinking
the creme inside of an Oreo.

01:53:37.210 --> 01:53:38.578
Next is Double Stuf.

01:53:38.578 --> 01:53:41.815
So I assume this has the creme

01:53:41.815 --> 01:53:44.517
and also a bunch of Oreo pieces in it.

01:53:45.451 --> 01:53:46.953
Oh, my God, this is the best one.

01:53:46.953 --> 01:53:48.788
At Five Guys, you can actually add bacon

01:53:48.788 --> 01:53:50.557
to any of their milkshake flavors.

01:53:50.557 --> 01:53:51.958
This is a vanilla bacon.

01:53:51.958 --> 01:53:54.327
I just feel like vanilla seemed like

01:53:54.327 --> 01:53:56.396
the easiest thing to pair with the bacon.

01:53:56.396 --> 01:53:59.866
I've never tried this
before, but let's see.

01:54:00.733 --> 01:54:02.669
It tastes like vanilla and bacon.

01:54:02.669 --> 01:54:04.404
I'm just trying to decide mentally

01:54:04.404 --> 01:54:07.640
if that's, like, something
I should have eaten.

01:54:07.640 --> 01:54:10.243
We thought we had one exclusive

01:54:10.243 --> 01:54:12.679
in the milkshake department in Italy.

01:54:12.679 --> 01:54:14.547
On their website, it still states

01:54:14.547 --> 01:54:17.250
that there is a coffee
milkshake that you can order.

01:54:17.250 --> 01:54:20.820
We did order it, but then
when we got to the store

01:54:20.820 --> 01:54:23.156
to collect it, turns out
it's been discontinued.

01:54:23.156 --> 01:54:25.058
And it's been years they haven't done it.

01:54:25.058 --> 01:54:28.561
So please update your website, Five Guys.

01:54:28.561 --> 01:54:31.464
We still got a bacon milkshake,

01:54:31.464 --> 01:54:34.601
and then weirdly on the website also,

01:54:34.601 --> 01:54:37.470
it lets you add every single flavor,

01:54:37.470 --> 01:54:38.972
so we got a milkshake

01:54:38.972 --> 01:54:42.141
with absolutely everything
that was available.

01:54:42.141 --> 01:54:45.645
What's in here? There is
Oreos, bananas, strawberry.

01:54:45.645 --> 01:54:49.883
There's so many different
things that just,

01:54:49.883 --> 01:54:52.018
in my mind, they don't
really work together.

01:54:53.786 --> 01:54:54.854
I think there's just too many things

01:54:54.854 --> 01:54:57.523
to even make out what stuff is.

01:54:57.523 --> 01:54:58.892
To be honest, it's not too bad.

01:54:58.892 --> 01:55:01.527
Now we've got the bacon milkshake.

01:55:01.527 --> 01:55:04.464
Mixed in bacon with milk.

01:55:04.464 --> 01:55:06.366
It does sound a bit ridiculous.

01:55:07.567 --> 01:55:08.568
I'm a bit disappointed, though,

01:55:08.568 --> 01:55:10.169
because I don't really
taste the bacon much.

01:55:10.169 --> 01:55:11.571
We also have some drink options

01:55:11.571 --> 01:55:13.206
you can only get in the US,

01:55:13.206 --> 01:55:15.942
Simply lemonade, root beer, and Dr Pepper.

01:55:15.942 --> 01:55:17.610
Do Italians like root beer?

01:55:17.610 --> 01:55:19.012
That's what I would love to know.

01:55:19.012 --> 01:55:21.381
You know what that is. I'm sure they do.

01:55:21.381 --> 01:55:24.183
If you're Italian, from
Italy, comment down below

01:55:24.183 --> 01:55:26.586
and tell me if you know
what root beer is, one,

01:55:26.586 --> 01:55:28.554
and two, do you actually think it's good?

01:55:28.554 --> 01:55:30.056
Because here, people love it.

01:55:30.056 --> 01:55:31.557
And here are all the drinks

01:55:31.557 --> 01:55:33.626
that you can only find in Italy.

01:55:33.626 --> 01:55:36.462
We've got Fanta orange, sparkling water,

01:55:36.462 --> 01:55:37.864
and then four beers.

01:55:40.566 --> 01:55:42.302
So, let's talk about prices now.

01:55:42.302 --> 01:55:44.737
In Italy at Five Guys, a cheeseburger

01:55:44.737 --> 01:55:47.874
will cost you 13 euros and 45 cents.

01:55:47.874 --> 01:55:52.312
Translated to dollars, that is $14.82.

01:55:52.312 --> 01:55:54.681
So, for comparison, at
McDonald's you can get

01:55:54.681 --> 01:55:57.116
a cheeseburger for 2 euros.

01:55:57.116 --> 01:56:00.620
So yeah, for the same price,
13-point-something euros,

01:56:00.620 --> 01:56:04.424
you could get six of
these at the other chain.

01:56:04.424 --> 01:56:05.425
That's maybe too cheap,

01:56:05.425 --> 01:56:08.895
but 13 euros for a burger in tinfoil

01:56:08.895 --> 01:56:11.097
just sort of all squished together

01:56:11.097 --> 01:56:12.865
still at a fast-food chain,

01:56:12.865 --> 01:56:17.136
that's way, way over what I would pay.

01:56:17.136 --> 01:56:21.407
In the US, a cheeseburger
will cost you $11.79,

01:56:21.407 --> 01:56:23.443
or 10 euros and 70 cents.

01:56:23.443 --> 01:56:26.612
That is a 26% decrease in price.

01:56:26.612 --> 01:56:28.781
So, Five Guys is doing this thing

01:56:28.781 --> 01:56:32.151
where all of their food is
fresh and made to order.

01:56:32.151 --> 01:56:34.821
They're trying to kind
of raise the standard

01:56:34.821 --> 01:56:37.390
of what fast food could be.

01:56:37.390 --> 01:56:40.526
I think that's why their
prices are on the higher end,

01:56:40.526 --> 01:56:43.463
although I don't know if
that's fully justified,

01:56:43.463 --> 01:56:44.897
because I can say

01:56:44.897 --> 01:56:47.700
that I've had better, cheaper burgers.

01:56:47.700 --> 01:56:48.868
I think that's allowed.

01:56:48.868 --> 01:56:50.103
And to make that a meal,

01:56:50.103 --> 01:56:53.673
so with a regular fries and a drink,

01:56:53.673 --> 01:56:57.310
that will cost you 23 euros and 20 cents,

01:56:57.310 --> 01:57:01.180
which in dollars is $25.57.

01:57:01.180 --> 01:57:03.649
Again, so overpriced.

01:57:03.649 --> 01:57:05.785
Like, 23 euros for all this,

01:57:06.886 --> 01:57:10.189
and I still don't even have a plate.

01:57:10.189 --> 01:57:12.325
It's just a lot. A lot.

01:57:12.325 --> 01:57:15.828
To make it a meal with regular
fries and a regular drink,

01:57:15.828 --> 01:57:20.166
it will cost you $21.47,

01:57:20.166 --> 01:57:23.236
or 19 euros and 48 cents.

01:57:23.236 --> 01:57:26.906
I ... it's just not making sense to me.

01:57:26.906 --> 01:57:31.477
$21 for a fast-food
burger, fries, and drink,

01:57:31.477 --> 01:57:33.079
no. Absolutely not.

01:57:35.348 --> 01:57:37.817
Let's take a look at some
of the basic ingredients

01:57:37.817 --> 01:57:39.919
at a Five Guys Italy.

01:57:39.919 --> 01:57:44.390
In Italy, the burger itself,
it's 100% ground beef.

01:57:44.390 --> 01:57:46.592
And in the US, a burger actually contains

01:57:46.592 --> 01:57:48.795
80/20 USDA ground chuck.

01:57:48.795 --> 01:57:50.797
If you want to add cheese
to your burger, though,

01:57:50.797 --> 01:57:53.266
here's everything that's in the cheese.

01:57:53.266 --> 01:57:55.134
Five Guys cheese in the US contains

01:57:55.134 --> 01:57:57.303
all of these ingredients.

01:57:57.303 --> 01:57:58.337
Let's look at the bun.

01:57:58.337 --> 01:58:01.908
It contains water, salt,
sugar, vegetable shortening,

01:58:01.908 --> 01:58:04.077
milk, eggs, bleached bread flour,

01:58:04.077 --> 01:58:05.912
yeast, and sesame seeds.

01:58:05.912 --> 01:58:09.148
So, in Italy the bun has
a total of 11 ingredients.

01:58:09.148 --> 01:58:11.484
That's two more than the US.

01:58:11.484 --> 01:58:14.654
The additional ingredients
are calcium carbonate

01:58:14.654 --> 01:58:16.722
and spirit vinegar.

01:58:16.722 --> 01:58:18.091
The only difference in the hot dogs

01:58:18.091 --> 01:58:20.426
is some of the ingredients
to make the pink coloring.

01:58:20.426 --> 01:58:22.795
We love dyeing our food here.

01:58:22.795 --> 01:58:24.730
The ingredients for the
fries are really simple.

01:58:24.730 --> 01:58:27.733
It's just potatoes, refined
peanut oil, and salt.

01:58:27.733 --> 01:58:30.503
If you go to a Five Guys,
they have this little board

01:58:30.503 --> 01:58:33.639
that tells you where your
potatoes are coming from that day,

01:58:33.639 --> 01:58:36.109
and ours came from St. Anthony, Idaho.

01:58:36.109 --> 01:58:38.778
And the fries at Five
Guys are very simple.

01:58:38.778 --> 01:58:42.048
They are potatoes, peanut oil, and salt.

01:58:42.048 --> 01:58:44.283
It's the first thing that
I see something cooked

01:58:44.283 --> 01:58:45.418
with peanut oil.

01:58:45.418 --> 01:58:48.921
Let's see. Do they taste
like peanuts at all, or?

01:58:49.822 --> 01:58:52.225
Actually, they taste quite potatoey.

01:58:52.225 --> 01:58:54.393
Like, they taste quite nice.

01:58:54.393 --> 01:58:56.329
Yeah, maybe it's the peanut oil after all.

01:58:58.731 --> 01:59:01.934
In the US, a cheeseburger
that has a bun, two patties,

01:59:01.934 --> 01:59:03.769
two pieces of cheese, and no toppings

01:59:03.769 --> 01:59:06.606
comes out to about 984 calories.

01:59:06.606 --> 01:59:09.242
The total fat comes out to about 55 grams,

01:59:09.242 --> 01:59:10.910
carbs 39 grams,

01:59:10.910 --> 01:59:12.145
sugar 8 grams,

01:59:12.145 --> 01:59:16.015
and sodium 1,050 milligrams.

01:59:16.015 --> 01:59:18.584
In Italy, a regular cheeseburger contains

01:59:18.584 --> 01:59:21.354
756 calories,

01:59:21.354 --> 01:59:25.458
of which 45 grams are total fat,

01:59:25.458 --> 01:59:27.393
40 grams are carbs,

01:59:27.393 --> 01:59:29.695
8 grams are sugar,

01:59:29.695 --> 01:59:33.499
and 908 milligrams are sodium.

01:59:33.499 --> 01:59:35.835
And if you make that a
meal, you can add fries,

01:59:35.835 --> 01:59:40.540
and they contain 1,122 calories,

01:59:40.540 --> 01:59:43.342
then 66 grams of fat,

01:59:43.342 --> 01:59:46.012
120 grams of carbs,

01:59:46.012 --> 01:59:48.314
1.7 grams of sugar,

01:59:48.314 --> 01:59:52.585
and 716 milligrams of sodium.

01:59:52.585 --> 01:59:55.788
Our regular fries are 953 calories,

01:59:55.788 --> 01:59:57.223
41 grams of fat,

01:59:57.223 --> 01:59:59.559
131 grams of carbs,

01:59:59.559 --> 02:00:00.760
4 grams of sugar,

02:00:00.760 --> 02:00:03.963
and 962 milligrams of sodium.

02:00:03.963 --> 02:00:06.165
And a chocolate milkshake contains

02:00:06.165 --> 02:00:09.068
874 calories,

02:00:09.068 --> 02:00:12.171
then 39 grams of fat,

02:00:12.171 --> 02:00:15.141
121 grams of carbs,

02:00:15.141 --> 02:00:17.777
108 grams of sugar,

02:00:17.777 --> 02:00:21.614
and 408 milligrams of sodium.

02:00:21.614 --> 02:00:24.584
And a chocolate milkshake is 830 calories,

02:00:24.584 --> 02:00:26.018
36 grams of fat,

02:00:26.018 --> 02:00:27.954
116 grams of carbs,

02:00:27.954 --> 02:00:29.555
107 grams of sugar,

02:00:29.555 --> 02:00:31.791
and 400 milligrams of sodium.

02:00:31.791 --> 02:00:35.361
So, the total for a meal
that includes a cheeseburger,

02:00:35.361 --> 02:00:37.563
regular fries, and the milkshake

02:00:37.563 --> 02:00:40.800
is 2,752 calories,

02:00:40.800 --> 02:00:43.903
of which 150 grams are total fat,

02:00:43.903 --> 02:00:46.839
then 281 grams carbs,

02:00:46.839 --> 02:00:49.542
118 grams of sugar,

02:00:49.542 --> 02:00:54.146
and 2,032 milligrams of sodium.

02:00:54.146 --> 02:00:58.217
Bringing the total to 2,767 calories,

02:00:58.217 --> 02:01:00.620
132 grams of total fat,

02:01:00.620 --> 02:01:02.455
286 grams of carbs,

02:01:02.455 --> 02:01:04.190
119 grams of sugar,

02:01:04.190 --> 02:01:08.027
and 2,412 milligrams of sodium.

02:01:08.027 --> 02:01:10.796
Well, the numbers for the
fries are actually based on

02:01:10.796 --> 02:01:13.299
what is stated on the website,

02:01:13.299 --> 02:01:17.336
and we got basically half
of what is stated there.

02:01:17.336 --> 02:01:20.539
So if you want to make this
a little bit more accurate,

02:01:20.539 --> 02:01:24.977
you should halve the
nutrition numbers as well.

02:01:27.246 --> 02:01:30.850
Five Guys first opened
in Italy in 2018 in Milan

02:01:30.850 --> 02:01:34.320
just behind the Duomo, so
a very touristic location.

02:01:34.320 --> 02:01:38.124
And then in 2021 after
a bit of a COVID break,

02:01:38.124 --> 02:01:40.626
it opened in Rome, and there are now

02:01:40.626 --> 02:01:43.162
another four locations in Milan.

02:01:43.162 --> 02:01:44.864
I think, well, starting with Milan,

02:01:44.864 --> 02:01:46.265
it's a very smart choice.

02:01:46.265 --> 02:01:51.237
Obviously it's the most
international city.

02:01:51.237 --> 02:01:52.905
There's a lot of tourists,

02:01:52.905 --> 02:01:55.641
like, fashion capital of Italy,

02:01:55.641 --> 02:02:00.112
a lot of offices, a lot of
foreigners as well here,

02:02:00.112 --> 02:02:03.082
which is maybe the reason
why they opened here.

02:02:03.082 --> 02:02:05.451
I know Five Guys is
available in a lot of places,

02:02:05.451 --> 02:02:07.186
but something about the branding

02:02:07.186 --> 02:02:08.621
and the way the food is presented

02:02:08.621 --> 02:02:11.324
feels very East Coast to me.

02:02:11.324 --> 02:02:14.126
I think it's because the fries
remind me of boardwalk fries

02:02:14.126 --> 02:02:16.362
that you'd get down at the Jersey shore.

02:02:16.362 --> 02:02:18.364
It's a little weird because some stuff

02:02:18.364 --> 02:02:20.366
has the Five Guys logo on it

02:02:20.366 --> 02:02:21.667
and you can tell where it's from.

02:02:21.667 --> 02:02:23.436
Other stuff, like the
fries and the burgers,

02:02:23.436 --> 02:02:26.806
just come in regular foil,
a regular unmarked cup.

02:02:26.806 --> 02:02:30.443
So it's like, it's not a
lot of brand recognition,

02:02:30.443 --> 02:02:31.277
at least for me.

02:02:31.277 --> 02:02:33.813
I've never even seen a
Five Guys advertisement.

02:02:33.813 --> 02:02:36.115
I've never seen a commercial.
I've never gotten an ad.

02:02:36.115 --> 02:02:39.085
Once you take this cup away,
you probably wouldn't know

02:02:39.085 --> 02:02:40.486
where I got this food from.

02:02:40.486 --> 02:02:42.221
Because their burgers are made to order,

02:02:42.221 --> 02:02:44.757
it does take longer for
you to get your order.

02:02:44.757 --> 02:02:47.993
I've waited, like, at least 10 minutes

02:02:47.993 --> 02:02:49.995
for my order at a Five Guys before,

02:02:49.995 --> 02:02:52.798
so it's not the fastest fast-food option.

02:02:52.798 --> 02:02:55.668
But the food is as fresh as it can be.

02:02:55.668 --> 02:02:57.370
It kind of gives me the feeling

02:02:57.370 --> 02:02:59.872
of food you'd get at a concession stand

02:02:59.872 --> 02:03:03.109
at a local baseball game
at a school or something.

02:03:03.109 --> 02:03:06.812
It's definitely got
its own thing going on.

02:03:07.113 --> 02:03:09.215
Claudia: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:03:09.215 --> 02:03:11.083
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:03:11.083 --> 02:03:13.619
between Pringles in Italy and the US.

02:03:13.619 --> 02:03:15.287
This is "Food Wars."

02:03:18.357 --> 02:03:20.292
Here are all the exclusive flavors

02:03:20.292 --> 02:03:23.329
that you will find in Italy
that you won't get in the US.

02:03:23.329 --> 02:03:24.830
Here are all the US Pringles

02:03:24.830 --> 02:03:26.098
you're not going to find in Italy.

02:03:26.098 --> 02:03:28.334
Starting from paprika.

02:03:28.334 --> 02:03:30.069
I've got to say paprika
is something that's

02:03:30.069 --> 02:03:32.304
very popular in Spain.

02:03:33.939 --> 02:03:35.441
Yeah, it's quite nice, actually.

02:03:35.441 --> 02:03:37.810
For those who may not
know what paprika is,

02:03:37.810 --> 02:03:41.113
it's actually dried, crushed red pepper.

02:03:41.113 --> 02:03:43.249
Very fruity and fresh, in a way.

02:03:43.249 --> 02:03:46.218
I know you guys in the US
have a barbecue flavor.

02:03:46.218 --> 02:03:49.655
We actually have Texas barbecue.

02:03:49.655 --> 02:03:51.891
I don't know, is there
maybe any difference,

02:03:51.891 --> 02:03:54.727
or maybe this is just marketing
to appeal to the Italians

02:03:54.727 --> 02:03:58.030
because when you say "Texas barbecue" it

02:03:58.030 --> 02:04:00.766
feels cooler and we
already know what it is?

02:04:02.001 --> 02:04:03.636
I don't know. It's barbecue sauce again.

02:04:03.636 --> 02:04:06.372
Is barbecue sauce in Texas
supposed to taste different?

02:04:06.372 --> 02:04:09.308
The US actually has dozens
of regional barbecue styles,

02:04:09.308 --> 02:04:11.744
including Texas, which has at least four.

02:04:11.744 --> 02:04:13.045
So it depends on who you ask,

02:04:13.045 --> 02:04:15.114
and I don't know where barbecue started.

02:04:15.114 --> 02:04:17.082
Yeah, we also have just barbecue.

02:04:18.050 --> 02:04:20.186
How do I describe the flavor? Tangy?

02:04:20.186 --> 02:04:22.021
Good, though. I love barbecue.

02:04:22.021 --> 02:04:25.925
And then on to the exclusive
train, we've got ketchup.

02:04:27.059 --> 02:04:28.994
Hm. I think it's a bit too strong.

02:04:28.994 --> 02:04:30.596
I prefer the other ones.

02:04:30.596 --> 02:04:33.632
The queen of them all, the pizza flavored.

02:04:33.632 --> 02:04:36.635
As I should be, I'm a little
bit worried about those

02:04:36.635 --> 02:04:40.940
because as an Italian I'm very
vocal about what pizza is.

02:04:40.940 --> 02:04:43.642
I have pretty low expectations for these,

02:04:43.642 --> 02:04:46.111
just because everything
pizza flavor to me,

02:04:46.111 --> 02:04:47.613
it's, like, a bit of a gimmick.

02:04:49.615 --> 02:04:50.983
No.

02:04:50.983 --> 02:04:53.018
They just taste like oregano.

02:04:53.018 --> 02:04:54.653
I don't know why you guys have this idea

02:04:54.653 --> 02:04:56.889
that Italians love oregano so much.

02:04:56.889 --> 02:05:00.226
Like, I have so many spices
and herbs in my kitchen,

02:05:00.226 --> 02:05:01.927
and guess what's missing.

02:05:01.927 --> 02:05:03.128
Oregano.

02:05:03.128 --> 02:05:06.532
Weirdly, and maybe I'm going
to be canceled for this,

02:05:06.532 --> 02:05:10.202
but the ketchup ones
taste more like pizza,

02:05:10.202 --> 02:05:12.238
because they taste more like tomatoes.

02:05:12.238 --> 02:05:14.640
Then we've got smoky bacon.

02:05:16.008 --> 02:05:19.078
They taste more like the
oil you cook the bacon in.

02:05:19.078 --> 02:05:19.979
Not a fan.

02:05:19.979 --> 02:05:22.715
You may also be able to
find Emmental Pringles,

02:05:22.715 --> 02:05:25.284
but we were not able to track them down.

02:05:25.284 --> 02:05:28.153
So, Emmental is a Swiss cheese

02:05:28.153 --> 02:05:31.790
made in the German part of Switzerland.

02:05:31.790 --> 02:05:34.126
Oh, cheddar cheese. Let's go!

02:05:34.126 --> 02:05:35.294
Bursting with flavor.

02:05:36.495 --> 02:05:37.863
Get that on screen.

02:05:37.863 --> 02:05:38.697
Good.

02:05:38.697 --> 02:05:41.500
Ooh, I've never had this
one before, hot honey.

02:05:41.500 --> 02:05:42.334
Nope.

02:05:42.334 --> 02:05:45.070
Ah, cheddar and sour cream.
Dude, these are always good.

02:05:46.238 --> 02:05:47.973
Mm! The chive!

02:05:47.973 --> 02:05:49.041
Salt and vinegar.

02:05:49.041 --> 02:05:50.276
Got ranch.

02:05:50.276 --> 02:05:53.245
Not the best ranch-flavored
chip out there, but not bad.

02:05:53.245 --> 02:05:54.713
I think Claudia should try these.

02:05:54.713 --> 02:05:56.115
Yo, Claudia, catch!

02:05:56.115 --> 02:05:57.082
Gah!

02:06:01.186 --> 02:06:02.655
Thanks, Joe.

02:06:02.655 --> 02:06:06.792
I've actually never had ranch
sauce or, like, dressing.

02:06:07.993 --> 02:06:10.729
I can already see people
sort of walking away from me

02:06:10.729 --> 02:06:12.197
the moment I start talking to them

02:06:12.197 --> 02:06:14.633
because of the onion.

02:06:14.633 --> 02:06:16.569
It's very potent.

02:06:16.569 --> 02:06:17.803
No.

02:06:17.803 --> 02:06:20.439
I'm seeing flames on both of
these. I'm seeing a grill.

02:06:20.439 --> 02:06:22.841
So assumption is these are spicy.

02:06:22.841 --> 02:06:25.611
Enchilada adobada.

02:06:25.611 --> 02:06:28.547
And the las meras meras habaneras.

02:06:29.782 --> 02:06:31.116
Not a lot of heat to
them, but pretty good.

02:06:31.116 --> 02:06:32.985
I don't know if that tastes
like an enchilada, but.

02:06:34.353 --> 02:06:35.988
Mm!

02:06:35.988 --> 02:06:38.023
These are good. They're not like Takis,

02:06:38.023 --> 02:06:39.692
but they're in the Taki
space. They're spicy.

02:06:39.692 --> 02:06:42.127
They have a Flamin' Hot
Cheeto kind of vibe to it.

02:06:42.127 --> 02:06:43.996
Minecraft suspicious stew.

02:06:45.764 --> 02:06:47.266
Limited time only. Thank God.

02:06:47.266 --> 02:06:49.435
Look, he's got a little
gamer headset on there.

02:06:49.435 --> 02:06:52.905
Shameless, Julius Pringle.
Shameless, going after the kids.

02:06:54.139 --> 02:06:55.341
I'm surprised. For
something that's clearly

02:06:55.341 --> 02:06:56.175
marketed as kids,

02:06:56.175 --> 02:06:59.011
this does not have a
very strong flavor to it.

02:06:59.011 --> 02:07:00.779
Tastes like a weak sour cream and onion.

02:07:00.779 --> 02:07:01.814
Philly cheesesteak.

02:07:01.814 --> 02:07:04.249
Check out the best
cheesesteak in Philadelphia

02:07:04.249 --> 02:07:07.086
"Food Tours" episode,
staring myself and Harry.

02:07:07.086 --> 02:07:10.823
And this is that sandwich in chip form.

02:07:10.823 --> 02:07:13.425
I can't imagine one
human being wanting this.

02:07:16.362 --> 02:07:17.563
Avoid this.

02:07:17.563 --> 02:07:18.697
Oh, smells terrible.

02:07:18.697 --> 02:07:20.566
There's also a French fries and ketchup

02:07:20.566 --> 02:07:22.368
and everything bagel flavor

02:07:22.368 --> 02:07:24.036
we were not able to get for this shoot.

02:07:24.036 --> 02:07:25.771
Let's get scorched.

02:07:25.771 --> 02:07:27.840
We also have a line of scorchin',

02:07:27.840 --> 02:07:30.242
I-N-apostrophe, Pringles.

02:07:30.242 --> 02:07:33.579
You can see the steam
coming out of Julius' ears.

02:07:33.579 --> 02:07:35.214
This one, he's crying.

02:07:35.214 --> 02:07:36.749
He's crying on the Buffalo one.

02:07:36.749 --> 02:07:38.851
He's not crying on the other ones. OK.

02:07:38.851 --> 02:07:39.818
Something to look forward to.

02:07:39.818 --> 02:07:41.420
Start down here with the barbecue.

02:07:42.988 --> 02:07:44.490
Come on!

02:07:44.490 --> 02:07:45.424
Get hot!

02:07:46.291 --> 02:07:47.726
Nope, not scorchin'.

02:07:47.726 --> 02:07:49.395
Let's try the cheddar.

02:07:49.395 --> 02:07:51.930
I mean, they even have the
temperature thing in the logo.

02:07:51.930 --> 02:07:53.832
The thermometer going up.

02:07:55.000 --> 02:07:56.235
Not only are they not scorchin',

02:07:56.235 --> 02:07:58.804
but also I'm not really
getting any flavor. Cheddar?

02:07:58.804 --> 02:07:59.872
Sour cream and onion.

02:07:59.872 --> 02:08:03.375
I mean, I love sour cream
and onion chips. [coughs]

02:08:04.643 --> 02:08:05.477
Mm.

02:08:05.477 --> 02:08:06.945
They taste like sour cream
and onion chips, but,

02:08:06.945 --> 02:08:09.415
I mean, I'm getting a little,
like, low-level spice.

02:08:09.415 --> 02:08:12.251
This one, as you can see,
Julius Pringle is crying.

02:08:12.251 --> 02:08:13.986
Look at this. The chip, the pepper,

02:08:13.986 --> 02:08:16.455
and the bottle of hot
sauce are all on fire.

02:08:17.790 --> 02:08:19.958
Little bit of heat. Yeah, there it is!

02:08:19.958 --> 02:08:22.261
There it is! OK.

02:08:22.261 --> 02:08:25.030
I guess look for the tears
if you want spicy Pringles.

02:08:25.030 --> 02:08:26.131
Chili and lime.

02:08:27.199 --> 02:08:28.033
No.

02:08:28.033 --> 02:08:29.668
Instead of scorchin', in Italy,

02:08:29.668 --> 02:08:32.171
spicy Pringles are called flame,

02:08:32.171 --> 02:08:35.474
and you can find them
as a spicy BBQ flavor

02:08:35.474 --> 02:08:37.543
and cheese and chili flavor.

02:08:38.944 --> 02:08:40.879
I think I'll be able to have a few

02:08:40.879 --> 02:08:42.915
without having to go and drink,

02:08:42.915 --> 02:08:44.216
but I think it's manageable.

02:08:44.216 --> 02:08:45.818
It's a very manageable spice.

02:08:45.818 --> 02:08:47.953
Let's try the cheese and chili now.

02:08:47.953 --> 02:08:50.089
This one have two chilies on them,

02:08:50.089 --> 02:08:54.093
so they're supposed to
be the mild-ish ones,

02:08:54.093 --> 02:08:56.095
whereas these have three.

02:08:58.063 --> 02:08:59.364
Ooh!

02:08:59.364 --> 02:09:02.835
You're attacked by this cheese
taste, cheese flavoring,

02:09:02.835 --> 02:09:04.403
fake-cheese taste.

02:09:04.403 --> 02:09:05.571
Not nice.

02:09:05.571 --> 02:09:07.439
Also in the US you can
get something called

02:09:07.439 --> 02:09:10.008
the Pringles harvest blend.

02:09:10.008 --> 02:09:11.877
Four varieties to choose from.

02:09:11.877 --> 02:09:13.979
According to the ad copy,

02:09:13.979 --> 02:09:16.782
"A deliciously complex tasting experience

02:09:16.782 --> 02:09:18.817
unlike one you've ever had."

02:09:18.817 --> 02:09:20.319
Barf!

02:09:20.319 --> 02:09:21.353
They're potato chips.

02:09:21.353 --> 02:09:25.257
Let's embark on this taste
journey unlike any other.

02:09:26.692 --> 02:09:27.526
Hang on.

02:09:29.461 --> 02:09:31.063
The taste difference between these two

02:09:31.063 --> 02:09:32.898
are hardly noticeable.

02:09:32.898 --> 02:09:34.800
They definitely look different.

02:09:34.800 --> 02:09:36.001
Homestyle ranch.

02:09:36.001 --> 02:09:37.302
Also multigrain.

02:09:37.302 --> 02:09:40.038
Amazon. This guy drop-kicked
this to my front door.

02:09:40.038 --> 02:09:41.340
This is ridiculous!

02:09:42.407 --> 02:09:44.009
These are different than
their regular ranch,

02:09:44.009 --> 02:09:45.244
and I do like these.

02:09:45.244 --> 02:09:48.947
Flavor's not as strong, not
as insane, which I like.

02:09:48.947 --> 02:09:51.083
Sweet potatoes, next are sweet potato,

02:09:51.083 --> 02:09:52.384
and this is sea salt.

02:09:52.384 --> 02:09:54.153
I like that. I like sweet potatoes,

02:09:55.354 --> 02:09:57.322
I like maracas, so.

02:09:57.322 --> 02:09:59.591
OK, again, the sweet
potato smoky barbecue.

02:10:00.692 --> 02:10:02.928
I've definitely experienced this before,

02:10:02.928 --> 02:10:04.797
so I want to update that ad copy.

02:10:04.797 --> 02:10:07.566
The last exclusives we have
is the lighter side range,

02:10:07.566 --> 02:10:09.168
where you can get the lightly salted

02:10:09.168 --> 02:10:11.003
and the reduced-fat original.

02:10:11.003 --> 02:10:12.871
Could not get them for
the time of filming,

02:10:12.871 --> 02:10:14.373
and honestly, I'm glad.

02:10:14.373 --> 02:10:16.875
I'm not interested in less
salt or less fat. Forget it.

02:10:16.875 --> 02:10:19.878
So, if I were to rank them all, let's see.

02:10:19.878 --> 02:10:21.213
OK, worst, pizza.

02:10:22.181 --> 02:10:23.482
Didn't like the bacon.

02:10:24.483 --> 02:10:26.752
Didn't like this one with the cheese.

02:10:26.752 --> 02:10:28.220
Let's put the other spicy one,

02:10:28.220 --> 02:10:30.989
just because I'm not so big on spices.

02:10:30.989 --> 02:10:32.658
Now I'm going to put the ketchup.

02:10:32.658 --> 02:10:34.459
I'm going to put this one here,

02:10:34.459 --> 02:10:36.361
and probably the paprika

02:10:36.361 --> 02:10:39.264
is the one that I will reach out for.

02:10:39.264 --> 02:10:40.566
OK, in no particular order,

02:10:40.566 --> 02:10:42.334
my favorites of the day were

02:10:42.334 --> 02:10:44.603
the las meras meras habaneras.

02:10:44.603 --> 02:10:46.104
Very good. Taking these home.

02:10:46.104 --> 02:10:47.773
Cheddar and sour cream.

02:10:47.773 --> 02:10:48.941
Always good.

02:10:48.941 --> 02:10:50.409
Scorchin' series, a little disappointed

02:10:50.409 --> 02:10:52.644
except for the Buffalo.
My guy's crying on there,

02:10:52.644 --> 02:10:54.513
so you know that they're scorching.

02:10:54.513 --> 02:10:56.081
And I did like the harvest blend ones,

02:10:56.081 --> 02:10:57.249
the sweet potato ones.

02:10:57.249 --> 02:10:58.550
I sign off on them.

02:10:58.550 --> 02:10:59.451
Here's what sucked.

02:10:59.451 --> 02:11:01.854
Hot honey. Not hot, very little honey.

02:11:01.854 --> 02:11:03.789
The Philly cheesesteak
thing. Yeah, you can't.

02:11:03.789 --> 02:11:05.757
And this Minecraft suspicious stew.

02:11:05.757 --> 02:11:07.559
I don't, I'm not eating
anything called "suspicious,"

02:11:07.559 --> 02:11:08.560
that's just weird.

02:11:10.429 --> 02:11:13.232
In Italy, our Pringles come in four sizes.

02:11:13.232 --> 02:11:16.001
We've got a 40-gram small size.

02:11:16.001 --> 02:11:20.372
You may also be able to find
a pop-and-go 70-grams tube,

02:11:20.372 --> 02:11:22.708
but we were not able to track it down.

02:11:22.708 --> 02:11:24.276
And then you can also get them

02:11:24.276 --> 02:11:27.746
in the 175-grams standard tube.

02:11:27.746 --> 02:11:31.350
But if you get the flame
spicy Pringle range,

02:11:31.350 --> 02:11:35.220
you only get for the
standard tube 160 grams,

02:11:35.220 --> 02:11:37.756
even though the tubes
look exactly the same.

02:11:37.756 --> 02:11:39.391
Maybe it's done to protect you.

02:11:39.391 --> 02:11:42.561
Sometimes Pringles releases a 3-foot tube,

02:11:42.561 --> 02:11:46.265
which always breaks the internet
when it actually comes out.

02:11:46.265 --> 02:11:48.800
Sadly, it was not in stores right now,

02:11:48.800 --> 02:11:51.136
but it looks like it's just three tubes

02:11:51.136 --> 02:11:52.771
stacked on top of one another.

02:11:52.771 --> 02:11:55.707
So visually, this is what you will get.

02:11:57.442 --> 02:12:00.312
Here in the US, our
Pringles come in five sizes.

02:12:00.312 --> 02:12:02.781
Snack stack, then another little one,

02:12:02.781 --> 02:12:05.417
the grab-and-go, the original tube,

02:12:05.417 --> 02:12:07.352
and the party stack.

02:12:07.352 --> 02:12:11.089
That means that the biggest
American size is 10% larger

02:12:11.089 --> 02:12:13.492
than the biggest Italian one.

02:12:13.492 --> 02:12:16.261
We wanted to find out how
many Pringles are in a tube,

02:12:16.261 --> 02:12:18.897
but we didn't really want
to count them one by one.

02:12:18.897 --> 02:12:21.800
So we're going to weigh
them and do some maths.

02:12:21.800 --> 02:12:26.071
We should be getting 87.5
Pringles in each tube.

02:12:26.071 --> 02:12:28.240
Well, the 0.5 is maybe
some, like, crumbles.

02:12:28.240 --> 02:12:30.409
The numbers, as we have crunched here

02:12:30.409 --> 02:12:32.444
at the "Food Wars" math lab,

02:12:32.444 --> 02:12:34.513
is 149 grams total.

02:12:34.513 --> 02:12:37.182
And if one chip is 1.9 grams,

02:12:37.182 --> 02:12:38.617
that equals

02:12:38.617 --> 02:12:42.788
78.4 chips on average per tube.

02:12:44.856 --> 02:12:48.293
In Italy, the original
Pringles contain the following.

02:12:48.293 --> 02:12:51.730
The original Pringles in
the US contain all of this.

02:12:51.730 --> 02:12:54.032
There aren't any major differences,

02:12:54.032 --> 02:12:55.667
except for actually coloring

02:12:55.667 --> 02:12:58.170
that we do add to our
Pringles here in Italy.

02:12:58.170 --> 02:13:01.306
It's annatto. It's made from plants,

02:13:01.306 --> 02:13:02.941
and it's totally natural.

02:13:02.941 --> 02:13:05.877
I mean, annatto is very dark.

02:13:05.877 --> 02:13:07.913
It's a flashy orangey brown.

02:13:07.913 --> 02:13:10.682
So it's still very far from this coloring,

02:13:10.682 --> 02:13:13.352
but there is a difference with the US.

02:13:13.352 --> 02:13:15.420
The longest ingredient list for Pringles

02:13:15.420 --> 02:13:16.621
in the US are these,

02:13:16.621 --> 02:13:18.824
the scorchin' sour cream and onion,

02:13:18.824 --> 02:13:21.927
with 47 ingredients. Good God!

02:13:21.927 --> 02:13:23.362
Eleven of these are main ingredients,

02:13:23.362 --> 02:13:25.497
and 36 are subingredients.

02:13:25.497 --> 02:13:27.799
Now, many of these are flavoring spices

02:13:27.799 --> 02:13:31.003
and different dairy products
to create the cream flavor

02:13:31.003 --> 02:13:31.870
as well as some colorings

02:13:31.870 --> 02:13:33.438
which you may not have heard of before.

02:13:33.438 --> 02:13:36.108
Red 40, yellow 5, and yellow 6.

02:13:36.108 --> 02:13:37.809
There's new evidence that red 40

02:13:37.809 --> 02:13:41.079
is triggering inflammatory bowel disease

02:13:41.079 --> 02:13:44.816
because it is disrupting the
way the gut barrier works,

02:13:44.816 --> 02:13:48.086
which is harmful and
encourages inflammation.

02:13:48.086 --> 02:13:49.621
First it scorches your tongue,

02:13:49.621 --> 02:13:51.523
and then it scorches your bowels.

02:13:51.523 --> 02:13:53.158
UK manufacturers

02:13:53.158 --> 02:13:55.093
were made to remove this
from their products.

02:13:55.093 --> 02:13:58.230
However, it can be
legally sold by EU imports

02:13:58.230 --> 02:14:00.632
providing it is properly labeled,

02:14:00.632 --> 02:14:03.101
"May have an adverse effect on activity

02:14:03.101 --> 02:14:04.436
and attention in children."

02:14:04.436 --> 02:14:06.872
Yellow No. 5, also called tartrazine,

02:14:06.872 --> 02:14:08.273
is a type of sodium salt

02:14:08.273 --> 02:14:12.210
that, when eaten, it
becomes "sulfanic" acid?

02:14:12.210 --> 02:14:14.546
It is this acid that can
cause allergic reactions,

02:14:14.546 --> 02:14:17.949
especially in asthmatic
people, and can produce eczema,

02:14:17.949 --> 02:14:20.385
hives, and also hyperactivity in children.

02:14:20.385 --> 02:14:22.587
Many Nordic countries have banned its use,

02:14:22.587 --> 02:14:24.556
but it is approved in the US and UK.

02:14:24.556 --> 02:14:25.590
Heads up, Harry.

02:14:25.590 --> 02:14:30.095
Yellow No. 6, also called
sunset yellow or E110,

02:14:30.095 --> 02:14:31.396
is similar to tartrazine.

02:14:31.396 --> 02:14:33.832
And these colors have appeared
in a bunch of flavors,

02:14:33.832 --> 02:14:35.133
these specifically.

02:14:37.202 --> 02:14:40.172
Obviously Pringles is a very
well-known brand in Italy,

02:14:40.172 --> 02:14:44.109
but I think the idea of chips as a thing,

02:14:44.109 --> 02:14:46.845
for us, chips are not
really a thing of their own.

02:14:46.845 --> 02:14:49.381
They're, like, part of a family of snacks.

02:14:49.381 --> 02:14:51.950
In Italy, we tend to have chips

02:14:51.950 --> 02:14:54.719
on a snack board with other things,

02:14:54.719 --> 02:14:56.321
other items like olives

02:14:56.321 --> 02:14:58.890
or tiny pieces of focaccia.

02:14:58.890 --> 02:15:02.694
Pringles is not the first brand
that I would reach out to.

02:15:02.694 --> 02:15:06.631
It's funny because to me all
these seem quite a big number.

02:15:06.631 --> 02:15:08.266
Having to decide between, like,

02:15:08.266 --> 02:15:09.601
three, four, five, six, seven,

02:15:09.601 --> 02:15:11.736
seven flavors,

02:15:11.736 --> 02:15:14.973
and then you got the original, it's a lot.

02:15:14.973 --> 02:15:18.410
We just saw the 500
different flavors they have.

02:15:18.410 --> 02:15:21.346
Pringles, they're doing
every flavor. Good for them.

02:15:21.346 --> 02:15:22.881
But as far as the classics,

02:15:22.881 --> 02:15:25.050
the salt and vinegar, the
barbecue, the cheddar,

02:15:25.050 --> 02:15:26.284
sour cream and onion,

02:15:26.284 --> 02:15:28.153
I feel like Pringles is pretty good at

02:15:28.153 --> 02:15:29.287
doing most flavors.

02:15:29.287 --> 02:15:30.856
But they also had that
stupid Minecraft flavor,

02:15:30.856 --> 02:15:32.090
so I don't know.

02:15:32.090 --> 02:15:34.292
I don't know. They are
exclusive to the Italian market,

02:15:34.292 --> 02:15:38.497
but they still do seem
adapted to the Italian market,

02:15:38.497 --> 02:15:41.166
versus created for the Italian market.

02:15:41.166 --> 02:15:43.435
If you wanted something very Italian,

02:15:43.435 --> 02:15:45.570
you should have put an olive oil one.

02:15:45.570 --> 02:15:47.639
You're really missing an opportunity here.

02:15:47.639 --> 02:15:50.275
Just put an olive-oil-flavored chip.

02:15:50.275 --> 02:15:52.043
We've talked about this
on "Food Wars" before.

02:15:52.043 --> 02:15:54.846
In America, chips and snacks
are all going after each other.

02:15:54.846 --> 02:15:56.748
They might be owned by the same company,

02:15:56.748 --> 02:15:58.350
and they're just, like, cross-pollinating,

02:15:58.350 --> 02:16:00.652
but the chip aisle is just all filled with

02:16:00.652 --> 02:16:02.988
these different iterations
of the same kind of idea, so,

02:16:02.988 --> 02:16:04.456
I see tube snacks all the time.

02:16:04.456 --> 02:16:07.325
I've got actually here some
of the most popular ones.

02:16:07.325 --> 02:16:10.362
We've got Fonzies, which are like,

02:16:10.362 --> 02:16:11.897
pretty much like chips.

02:16:11.897 --> 02:16:15.467
You know, in a way, this is a
very traditional Italian chip.

02:16:15.467 --> 02:16:17.002
You also find these.

02:16:17.002 --> 02:16:18.870
These are called crostini.

02:16:18.870 --> 02:16:20.438
This is like dried bread, you know?

02:16:20.438 --> 02:16:23.508
It's a bit like crumbs.
As you say, like crouton.

02:16:23.508 --> 02:16:26.578
Especially in the south of
Italy where I'm from, Bari,

02:16:26.578 --> 02:16:28.246
we make these all the time.

02:16:28.246 --> 02:16:29.481
They're called taralli.

02:16:29.481 --> 02:16:30.482
Shape is always the same,

02:16:30.482 --> 02:16:32.517
but you always get them
in different flavors.

02:16:32.517 --> 02:16:34.186
Actually, my grandma makes them,

02:16:34.186 --> 02:16:36.354
and it's, like, the best thing ever.

02:16:36.354 --> 02:16:39.491
And they're made with
flour, olive oil, and wine.

02:16:39.491 --> 02:16:43.895
So this is the absolute OG Italian snack.

02:16:45.931 --> 02:16:46.765
The best.

02:16:46.765 --> 02:16:49.534
My grandma's are better, but this is good.

02:16:51.503 --> 02:16:53.638
In the US, our original regular tube,

02:16:53.638 --> 02:16:56.741
the 5.2-ounce, or the 149-gram,

02:16:56.741 --> 02:16:58.777
is currently $2 at Walmart.

02:16:58.777 --> 02:17:01.112
In Italy, our original Pringles

02:17:01.112 --> 02:17:03.949
in the 175-grams tube

02:17:03.949 --> 02:17:06.318
will cost you 2 euros 30.

02:17:06.318 --> 02:17:09.321
That's about $2.47.

02:17:09.321 --> 02:17:13.491
That means that in Italy we
get a 23% price increase,

02:17:13.491 --> 02:17:16.661
although we do get a few more grams.

02:17:16.661 --> 02:17:18.129
We wanted to see how much

02:17:18.129 --> 02:17:20.498
our biggest portion of Pringles will cost.

02:17:20.498 --> 02:17:24.436
For a 48-snack-stack-cup variety pack,

02:17:24.436 --> 02:17:27.305
it costs $29.72.

02:17:27.305 --> 02:17:31.710
Divide that by 48, and
each snack stack costs

02:17:31.710 --> 02:17:33.078
62 cents.

02:17:33.078 --> 02:17:35.046
Hey, Claudia, just out of curiosity,

02:17:35.046 --> 02:17:37.082
for common Italian snack foods,

02:17:37.082 --> 02:17:39.050
how do Pringles compare in price?

02:17:39.050 --> 02:17:41.486
Compared to other snacks
that you can get in Italy,

02:17:41.486 --> 02:17:42.821
for example, the taralli,

02:17:42.821 --> 02:17:44.356
they're actually quite expensive.

02:17:44.356 --> 02:17:47.892
And you do get only 175 grams.

02:17:47.892 --> 02:17:50.395
Things like these, they're
usually sold at bakeries

02:17:50.395 --> 02:17:52.731
for, like, 2, 3 euros per kilo.

02:17:52.731 --> 02:17:55.166
So that's quite a lot of difference.

02:17:56.968 --> 02:17:59.638
In the US, 100 grams of
original Pringle chips

02:17:59.638 --> 02:18:01.439
contain all this.

02:18:01.439 --> 02:18:03.074
That's almost half of your recommended

02:18:03.074 --> 02:18:04.542
fat intake for the day.

02:18:04.542 --> 02:18:08.046
In Italy, a 100-gram
portion of original Pringles

02:18:08.046 --> 02:18:09.814
contains the following.

02:18:09.814 --> 02:18:13.952
Our version actually contains
more sugar than the US one,

02:18:13.952 --> 02:18:17.022
but slightly less fat and sodium.

02:18:17.022 --> 02:18:19.624
Across all Pringles flavors for calories,

02:18:19.624 --> 02:18:20.892
they're all pretty much the same.

02:18:20.892 --> 02:18:23.895
Now, some have 1 gram extra of carbs,

02:18:23.895 --> 02:18:25.263
and the sodium is the only thing

02:18:25.263 --> 02:18:26.765
that fluctuates between flavors.

02:18:26.765 --> 02:18:30.001
In Italy, the flavor with
the most sodium is ketchup.

02:18:30.001 --> 02:18:32.270
A 100-gram serving contains

02:18:32.270 --> 02:18:35.206
750 milligrams of sodium.

02:18:35.206 --> 02:18:36.741
In the US, our saltiest flavor

02:18:36.741 --> 02:18:38.410
is the las meras meras habaneras,

02:18:38.410 --> 02:18:41.746
with 1,107 milligrams.

02:18:41.746 --> 02:18:43.882
That's nearly half of
your daily allowance.

02:18:43.882 --> 02:18:45.850
Nico: From exclusive
items to portion sizes,

02:18:45.850 --> 02:18:48.353
we wanted to find out all the
differences between Starbucks

02:18:48.353 --> 02:18:49.854
in Italy and the US.

02:18:49.854 --> 02:18:51.323
This is "Food Wars."

02:18:53.892 --> 02:18:56.728
Our hot drinks in Italy
come in four sizes:

02:18:56.728 --> 02:19:00.332
short, tall, grande, and venti.

02:19:00.332 --> 02:19:02.367
Our hot drinks come in five sizes,

02:19:02.367 --> 02:19:06.604
short, tall, grande, venti, and

02:19:06.604 --> 02:19:08.073
the coffee traveler.

02:19:10.308 --> 02:19:13.445
Two of these, like grande
and venti, are Italian words.

02:19:13.445 --> 02:19:15.680
Venti means 20 in Italian,

02:19:15.680 --> 02:19:17.382
and grande just means big.

02:19:17.382 --> 02:19:18.983
Let's measure them out to see.

02:19:20.852 --> 02:19:23.722
The name translates to 20, but it is not.

02:19:23.722 --> 02:19:26.257
In the US, iced coffees
come in four sizes,

02:19:26.257 --> 02:19:29.127
tall, grande, venti, and trenta.

02:19:29.127 --> 02:19:31.696
Trenta is not available as an option

02:19:31.696 --> 02:19:33.465
for their espresso drinks,

02:19:33.465 --> 02:19:35.500
but you can get it in stuff like cold brew

02:19:35.500 --> 02:19:36.801
or their iced teas.

02:19:36.801 --> 02:19:39.371
Our iced coffees come in three sizes,

02:19:39.371 --> 02:19:42.006
a tall, grande, and venti.

02:19:42.006 --> 02:19:44.642
Let's measure the venti to see

02:19:44.642 --> 02:19:48.947
if it actually is 20 ounces.

02:19:48.947 --> 02:19:50.281
Eighteen ounces.

02:19:50.281 --> 02:19:53.318
So, again, not a true venti.

02:19:53.318 --> 02:19:55.086
It's more like a diciotto,

02:19:55.086 --> 02:19:56.554
which is 18.

02:19:56.554 --> 02:19:57.389
We're also going to weigh

02:19:57.389 --> 02:19:59.257
some popular food items from Starbucks.

02:19:59.257 --> 02:20:00.859
Let's start with the butter croissant.

02:20:03.928 --> 02:20:05.363
So, it's a pretty big difference

02:20:05.363 --> 02:20:07.098
to how much Italy's weighs.

02:20:07.098 --> 02:20:08.700
It's a lot smaller.

02:20:08.700 --> 02:20:11.536
Another popular bakery item
is the blueberry muffin.

02:20:11.536 --> 02:20:13.238
Let's see what it weighs.

02:20:20.278 --> 02:20:23.181
Here's everything that you'll
find at Starbucks in Italy

02:20:23.181 --> 02:20:24.949
that you won't find in the US.

02:20:24.949 --> 02:20:27.619
Here's everything that you'll
find at a Starbucks in the US

02:20:27.619 --> 02:20:29.320
that you won't find in Italy.

02:20:29.320 --> 02:20:30.855
We know that Starbucks is popular

02:20:30.855 --> 02:20:32.891
because of its customization options.

02:20:32.891 --> 02:20:34.692
So because of that, we're
only going to look at

02:20:34.692 --> 02:20:37.162
the official menus in the US and Italy.

02:20:37.162 --> 02:20:38.730
These are the exclusive hot drinks

02:20:38.730 --> 02:20:40.732
that you can find at
Starbucks here in Italy,

02:20:40.732 --> 02:20:43.535
starting from this tiny cup.

02:20:43.535 --> 02:20:45.703
This one is barley coffee.

02:20:45.703 --> 02:20:47.772
In Italian we call it caffè d'orzo.

02:20:47.772 --> 02:20:50.742
And it's basically an
alternative to espresso

02:20:50.742 --> 02:20:54.279
for those people that
cannot really drink coffee.

02:20:54.279 --> 02:20:56.381
It has the look of coffee.

02:20:56.381 --> 02:20:57.382
I'm not a fan of this.

02:20:57.382 --> 02:21:00.785
I think, you know, because I
can drink normal coffee, so,

02:21:00.785 --> 02:21:02.787
but if I were not able to,

02:21:02.787 --> 02:21:04.756
I think I'll just force myself to like it

02:21:04.756 --> 02:21:07.826
just for the pleasure of
still having my espresso.

02:21:07.826 --> 02:21:10.094
And then we have a vanilla latte.

02:21:10.094 --> 02:21:13.865
It does smell just like a
cappuccino, really, but.

02:21:13.865 --> 02:21:17.635
Obviously it's past 11 or so,

02:21:17.635 --> 02:21:19.938
so it's past breakfast time anyway,

02:21:19.938 --> 02:21:23.274
so cappuccinos are a no-no drink for me.

02:21:23.274 --> 02:21:26.211
I'm not so much into drinking milk

02:21:26.211 --> 02:21:28.079
after a certain time of the day.

02:21:28.079 --> 02:21:30.315
And then we have latte macchiato.

02:21:30.315 --> 02:21:31.549
And then we have this one.

02:21:31.549 --> 02:21:34.619
This one is a salted
maple and caramel latte.

02:21:36.554 --> 02:21:38.590
It just smells like sugar.

02:21:38.590 --> 02:21:42.794
It's nice. Yeah, it does taste
like fake, artificial syrup.

02:21:42.794 --> 02:21:44.863
And then we've got some teas.

02:21:44.863 --> 02:21:49.601
We got Teavana English
breakfast, jasmine pearl,

02:21:49.601 --> 02:21:52.904
high-biscus, or ih-biscus, as we say here,

02:21:52.904 --> 02:21:54.606
and chamomile.

02:21:54.606 --> 02:21:57.442
And you may also be able
to find the Moroccan,

02:21:57.442 --> 02:22:00.979
which in Italian just translates
into literally Marocchino.

02:22:00.979 --> 02:22:02.780
It's like a tiny cappuccino, in a way.

02:22:02.780 --> 02:22:05.850
There's a bit of coffee and
a bit of milk, obviously,

02:22:05.850 --> 02:22:08.486
with its own proper ratio.

02:22:08.486 --> 02:22:11.890
And it's named weirdly
after a Moroccan leather

02:22:11.890 --> 02:22:15.627
that has the same color
that this coffee has.

02:22:15.627 --> 02:22:18.396
It's a brown-ish, light brown leather.

02:22:18.396 --> 02:22:20.231
That's actually very popular here

02:22:20.231 --> 02:22:22.400
in the northern region
in Milan, where we are.

02:22:22.400 --> 02:22:26.004
So, here are the hot exclusive
beverages we bought today.

02:22:26.004 --> 02:22:29.240
This is the caramel apple spice juice.

02:22:29.240 --> 02:22:31.843
The apple crisp oat milk macchiato.

02:22:31.843 --> 02:22:33.878
We have a blond vanilla latte,

02:22:33.878 --> 02:22:36.948
and this is a royal English breakfast tea.

02:22:36.948 --> 02:22:39.651
We also have these exclusive hot drinks.

02:22:39.651 --> 02:22:43.288
I feel like I have to try
this caramel apple spice juice

02:22:43.288 --> 02:22:46.991
because it looks nothing like juice.

02:22:46.991 --> 02:22:48.092
So I'm interested.

02:22:52.564 --> 02:22:54.299
I think it's just hot apple cider.

02:22:54.299 --> 02:22:56.601
It doesn't taste bad, actually.
That tastes pretty good.

02:22:56.601 --> 02:22:58.870
I'm going to try the royal
English breakfast tea

02:22:58.870 --> 02:23:00.071
in honor of Harry.

02:23:03.508 --> 02:23:05.543
It's not my favorite.

02:23:05.543 --> 02:23:07.445
But my preference is iced tea,

02:23:07.445 --> 02:23:09.380
not hot tea, so maybe that's why.

02:23:09.380 --> 02:23:11.082
And I also like them a lot sweeter.

02:23:11.082 --> 02:23:14.319
We have lots of exclusive
cold drinks here in Italy.

02:23:14.319 --> 02:23:17.455
We didn't get everything,
but here's what we've got,

02:23:17.455 --> 02:23:21.793
starting from a cookies
and cream Frappuccino.

02:23:21.793 --> 02:23:24.262
I'm quite surprised this
is exclusive to Italy

02:23:24.262 --> 02:23:28.533
because I always associate
cookies and cream with the US.

02:23:28.533 --> 02:23:32.103
It has held its shape in the delivery.

02:23:32.103 --> 02:23:34.639
To me, this is a bit of a foreign idea

02:23:34.639 --> 02:23:38.476
because we just have the
boring chocolate flavor.

02:23:40.845 --> 02:23:43.781
Yeah, like chocolate cookies. Nice.

02:23:43.781 --> 02:23:45.483
It's like a childhood memory.

02:23:45.483 --> 02:23:46.851
Here are all the Fraps that we got.

02:23:46.851 --> 02:23:49.187
So, we have the chai cream.

02:23:49.187 --> 02:23:51.556
This is the mocha cookie Frap.

02:23:51.556 --> 02:23:55.927
This is the apple crisp
Frap, the pumpkin spice Frap,

02:23:55.927 --> 02:23:58.129
and the white mocha cream Frap.

02:23:58.129 --> 02:24:01.332
I feel very compelled to
try this mocha cookie Frap

02:24:01.332 --> 02:24:03.334
because it just looks like a milkshake.

02:24:03.334 --> 02:24:04.435
It looks like dessert.

02:24:04.435 --> 02:24:07.672
There's literally cookie crumbles in it.

02:24:09.941 --> 02:24:11.876
Yeah, it tastes like cold chocolate milk,

02:24:11.876 --> 02:24:15.346
specifically Nestlé syrup chocolate milk.

02:24:15.346 --> 02:24:18.783
An apple crisp Frappuccino
sounds kind of special to me,

02:24:18.783 --> 02:24:20.251
so I really want to taste it.

02:24:20.251 --> 02:24:21.919
Kind of tastes like a candle.

02:24:21.919 --> 02:24:24.422
I don't like that. Not at all.

02:24:24.422 --> 02:24:25.690
But I tried it.

02:24:25.690 --> 02:24:28.126
The pumpkin spice Frap
and the apple crisp Frap

02:24:28.126 --> 02:24:29.360
are seasonal items,

02:24:29.360 --> 02:24:31.763
so you're not going to be
able to find them year-round.

02:24:31.763 --> 02:24:35.033
And then we have iced
cold foam cappuccino.

02:24:36.467 --> 02:24:38.803
We don't really have a lot of foam here.

02:24:38.803 --> 02:24:41.606
It also looks quite dark for a cappuccino,

02:24:41.606 --> 02:24:43.808
but maybe that's just
because the foam is gone,

02:24:43.808 --> 02:24:47.078
but I don't know. They
keep putting hearts here,

02:24:47.078 --> 02:24:48.980
but I'm not really tempted to try this.

02:24:48.980 --> 02:24:53.951
And then we have an iced
salted maple and caramel latte.

02:24:53.951 --> 02:24:58.923
Does smell a lot like sugar, actually.

02:24:58.923 --> 02:25:01.826
Not even like maple. It
actually just smells like sugar.

02:25:01.826 --> 02:25:04.462
And you can see the sugar at the top.

02:25:04.462 --> 02:25:06.431
I did live in Canada for one year.

02:25:06.431 --> 02:25:08.232
Let's see if it does
actually taste like maple.

02:25:08.232 --> 02:25:11.369
I don't know if I can advocate
for Canadians out there,

02:25:11.369 --> 02:25:14.539
but for what it's worth,
I'm going to try it.

02:25:14.539 --> 02:25:17.241
There's no maple in there, definitely no.

02:25:17.241 --> 02:25:19.711
It's like sugar.

02:25:19.711 --> 02:25:22.246
Not even caramel. Just a lot of sugar.

02:25:22.246 --> 02:25:24.482
I feel like a Canadian
would never order this.

02:25:24.482 --> 02:25:26.751
But that will be another
episode of "Food Wars."

02:25:26.751 --> 02:25:30.922
And then we have iced chai tea oat latte.

02:25:30.922 --> 02:25:34.025
Again, quite surprised that
this is exclusive to Italy,

02:25:34.025 --> 02:25:36.427
because we're not so big on chai.

02:25:36.427 --> 02:25:38.629
I don't know. For some
reason I really like chai

02:25:38.629 --> 02:25:40.431
as, like, the tea version,

02:25:40.431 --> 02:25:43.334
but I've never really
quite liked it with milk.

02:25:43.334 --> 02:25:44.569
So, we have cold brews,

02:25:44.569 --> 02:25:46.738
but we also have nitro cold brews,

02:25:46.738 --> 02:25:48.206
which are a little bit frothier

02:25:48.206 --> 02:25:50.241
and thicker than the regular cold brew.

02:25:50.241 --> 02:25:52.443
This is the pumpkin cream cold brew.

02:25:52.443 --> 02:25:55.680
This is the cinnamon caramel
cream nitro cold brew.

02:25:55.680 --> 02:25:59.350
And here we have the vanilla
sweet cream nitro cold brew.

02:25:59.350 --> 02:26:01.819
I already know that I love
the pumpkin cream cold brew.

02:26:01.819 --> 02:26:04.889
I kind of want to try
this cinnamon caramel one.

02:26:07.792 --> 02:26:09.427
No, not for me.

02:26:09.427 --> 02:26:12.029
It's a little weirdly sweet

02:26:12.029 --> 02:26:14.265
for something that doesn't
have any milk in it,

02:26:14.265 --> 02:26:15.366
I don't think.

02:26:15.366 --> 02:26:17.135
Let me try this one.

02:26:17.135 --> 02:26:18.069
This one's really good.

02:26:18.069 --> 02:26:19.871
I really like the vanilla
sweet cream cold brew.

02:26:19.871 --> 02:26:23.374
That just tastes like a
really good foamy coffee.

02:26:23.374 --> 02:26:25.009
We then have this one,

02:26:25.009 --> 02:26:28.079
the very berry hibiscus Refresher.

02:26:28.079 --> 02:26:30.414
And then we have a matcha frappé.

02:26:30.414 --> 02:26:32.617
Again, I don't know how
this is specific to Italy

02:26:32.617 --> 02:26:35.086
because I think the whole matcha craze

02:26:35.086 --> 02:26:38.089
has kind of maybe spared us, in a way.

02:26:38.089 --> 02:26:39.257
But there's no other place

02:26:39.257 --> 02:26:41.626
where you will find any matcha flavoring,

02:26:41.626 --> 02:26:43.928
because I think our
green thing is pistachio.

02:26:43.928 --> 02:26:45.763
Like, we just don't have space

02:26:45.763 --> 02:26:47.932
for two green things to compete.

02:26:47.932 --> 02:26:48.766
Let's give it a try.

02:26:48.766 --> 02:26:53.037
I've never actually had
it in a Frappuccino.

02:26:53.037 --> 02:26:54.839
Yeah, tastes like matcha.

02:26:54.839 --> 02:26:56.741
Just very artificial matcha.

02:26:56.741 --> 02:26:59.510
We have a bunch of other iced
coffees that you can get.

02:26:59.510 --> 02:27:01.546
Here they all are.

02:27:01.546 --> 02:27:04.916
And today we actually
bought the iced flat white.

02:27:04.916 --> 02:27:06.951
I've had this before, and
I think I really like it,

02:27:06.951 --> 02:27:08.920
but I just want to take a sip again.

02:27:08.920 --> 02:27:10.621
Still good, still delicious.

02:27:10.621 --> 02:27:13.157
It's a little milky,
but it's really tasty.

02:27:13.157 --> 02:27:15.726
We also have several iced teas.

02:27:15.726 --> 02:27:19.430
Here we have the pumpkin cream
chai, the matcha lemonade,

02:27:19.430 --> 02:27:23.000
a peach green tea, the
London fog iced latte,

02:27:23.000 --> 02:27:27.004
an iced passion tea, the frozen
strawberry acai lemonade,

02:27:27.004 --> 02:27:29.173
and the frozen mango
dragon fruit lemonade.

02:27:29.173 --> 02:27:31.876
Starbucks sells these
Evolution Fresh juices.

02:27:31.876 --> 02:27:35.179
This one is orange, apple,
mango, pineapple, and acerola.

02:27:35.179 --> 02:27:36.747
That sounds really good.

02:27:36.747 --> 02:27:39.150
I've never had matcha
and lemonade together,

02:27:39.150 --> 02:27:40.318
so let's taste it.

02:27:41.652 --> 02:27:43.187
That's actually not bad.

02:27:43.187 --> 02:27:44.355
I thought I was going to hate it.

02:27:44.355 --> 02:27:45.423
It's actually pretty good.

02:27:45.423 --> 02:27:47.992
Let's try the London fog tea latte.

02:27:50.027 --> 02:27:52.063
No! So candle-y!

02:27:52.063 --> 02:27:53.798
I feel like I'm going to keep saying that.

02:27:53.798 --> 02:27:56.300
Why does everything taste
a little weird today?

02:27:56.300 --> 02:27:59.770
I do want to try one of
these frozen Refreshers.

02:27:59.770 --> 02:28:02.506
Let's see what this
strawberry acai tastes like.

02:28:02.506 --> 02:28:05.009
It's really good. It tastes
like strawberry lemonade.

02:28:05.009 --> 02:28:07.311
It's not frozen anymore, but it's tasty.

02:28:07.311 --> 02:28:08.880
We then have a bunch of smoothies.

02:28:08.880 --> 02:28:12.316
We have this Innocent blue juice,

02:28:12.316 --> 02:28:14.151
and the names are actually funny

02:28:14.151 --> 02:28:16.888
because they are a play on words here.

02:28:16.888 --> 02:28:19.490
This one is called Fa-Blu-Loso.

02:28:19.490 --> 02:28:22.426
Then we have a pink juice from Innocent.

02:28:22.426 --> 02:28:24.896
This one has another play on words,

02:28:24.896 --> 02:28:27.598
it's Rosa A Iosa.

02:28:27.598 --> 02:28:29.300
And if you're Italian watching this,

02:28:29.300 --> 02:28:30.801
yes, I'm from the south,

02:28:30.801 --> 02:28:33.871
because you can tell by the
way we pronounce our O's.

02:28:33.871 --> 02:28:35.907
We then have these tiny ones.

02:28:35.907 --> 02:28:39.543
This juice is mango,
passion fruit, and apple,

02:28:39.543 --> 02:28:43.047
and another one with
strawberry and banana.

02:28:43.047 --> 02:28:45.283
Yeah, they look very nice and natural.

02:28:45.283 --> 02:28:47.551
We have other cold drinks.

02:28:47.551 --> 02:28:48.953
This one is a chinotto,

02:28:48.953 --> 02:28:51.956
and they're all from this brand Tomarchio.

02:28:51.956 --> 02:28:53.824
I've actually never heard of it,

02:28:53.824 --> 02:28:57.161
but it looks like a fancy chinotto to me.

02:28:57.161 --> 02:29:00.264
So, chinotto is an Italian
drink made with bergamot.

02:29:00.264 --> 02:29:02.233
We normally just have
it from San Pellegrino,

02:29:02.233 --> 02:29:04.735
which is a more commercial
brand. Does tastes good.

02:29:04.735 --> 02:29:07.138
It's a bit like the Italian
version of Coca-Cola.

02:29:07.138 --> 02:29:10.474
My parents' generation, they
were having these, not Coke.

02:29:10.474 --> 02:29:13.177
We then have a red orange.

02:29:13.177 --> 02:29:16.213
We have sparkling soda
from the same brand,

02:29:16.213 --> 02:29:20.584
and we have lemonade,
which looks very nice.

02:29:20.584 --> 02:29:23.487
And then we picked up also this.

02:29:23.487 --> 02:29:25.823
It's just cold infused water.

02:29:25.823 --> 02:29:28.159
In Italian it's called Infuso A Freddo.

02:29:28.159 --> 02:29:29.427
And actually we've got more.

02:29:29.427 --> 02:29:31.462
Here are the rest of the cold drinks.

02:29:31.462 --> 02:29:36.233
Here is the US Only customizable
drink that we created.

02:29:36.233 --> 02:29:38.269
This is a caffè vanilla coffee Frap

02:29:38.269 --> 02:29:39.303
with half-and-half.

02:29:39.303 --> 02:29:41.572
The cup is lined with caramel sauce.

02:29:41.572 --> 02:29:44.041
It's got brown sugar syrup, mocha sauce,

02:29:44.041 --> 02:29:46.177
and cinnamon dolce sprinkles.

02:29:46.177 --> 02:29:48.713
And also I think some cookie crumbles.

02:29:48.713 --> 02:29:50.948
There are some mysterious crumbles on top

02:29:50.948 --> 02:29:52.984
that I have no idea where they came from

02:29:52.984 --> 02:29:56.153
because I didn't ask for
them, but it looks fun.

02:29:56.153 --> 02:29:57.955
This is going to give
me the worst tummy ache,

02:29:57.955 --> 02:29:59.290
I already know.

02:30:02.727 --> 02:30:04.462
That is the sweetest drink

02:30:04.462 --> 02:30:05.896
I think I've ever tasted in my life.

02:30:05.896 --> 02:30:09.033
It's too much. Absolutely too much.

02:30:09.033 --> 02:30:12.470
It is really fun that Starbucks
lets you customize anything,

02:30:12.470 --> 02:30:13.671
pretty much anything,

02:30:13.671 --> 02:30:16.307
because this would never
have been made otherwise.

02:30:16.307 --> 02:30:19.477
There is a lot of food at
Starbucks here in Italy.

02:30:19.477 --> 02:30:22.146
Let's start from the savory options.

02:30:22.146 --> 02:30:26.517
We've got your dear salmon bagel.

02:30:27.918 --> 02:30:30.988
I don't know, does that
have cream cheese in it?

02:30:30.988 --> 02:30:34.725
No, it does look like just salmon

02:30:34.725 --> 02:30:36.694
and some herbs.

02:30:36.694 --> 02:30:39.063
Some sad salad.

02:30:39.063 --> 02:30:40.564
Yeah, this is also cooked salmon.

02:30:40.564 --> 02:30:43.434
And aren't you big on, like,
smoked salmon over there?

02:30:43.434 --> 02:30:45.269
I don't know. Nico, you are in New York.

02:30:45.269 --> 02:30:47.405
What do you think from a
New Yorker point of view?

02:30:47.405 --> 02:30:49.206
Does that look like a good bagel?

02:30:49.206 --> 02:30:50.441
No, it does not.

02:30:50.441 --> 02:30:52.309
But maybe it tastes better than it looks.

02:30:52.309 --> 02:30:53.878
Now, we have some toasts.

02:30:53.878 --> 02:30:56.347
We have ham and cheese.

02:30:56.347 --> 02:30:58.716
Looks like an honest toast.

02:30:58.716 --> 02:31:00.584
And then we've got the same version,

02:31:00.584 --> 02:31:02.119
just with three cheeses.

02:31:02.119 --> 02:31:04.121
I'll be curious to know
which cheeses they are,

02:31:04.121 --> 02:31:06.791
because they just say three cheeses.

02:31:06.791 --> 02:31:09.994
And then we've got
baked focaccia with ham.

02:31:09.994 --> 02:31:12.830
Well, OK, first of all,
this is not focaccia.

02:31:12.830 --> 02:31:14.832
I mean, I don't know what this is.

02:31:14.832 --> 02:31:16.700
It looks great, actually.

02:31:16.700 --> 02:31:18.469
Looks very nice and fluffy.

02:31:18.469 --> 02:31:20.204
But this is not focaccia,

02:31:20.204 --> 02:31:23.040
because it just doesn't have the shape

02:31:23.040 --> 02:31:24.608
and it's too fluffy.

02:31:24.608 --> 02:31:26.477
It just looks like bread to me.

02:31:26.477 --> 02:31:28.913
Yeah, it just looks quite nice, actually.

02:31:28.913 --> 02:31:30.881
Like a normal sandwich you would find.

02:31:30.881 --> 02:31:32.149
It's quite refreshing

02:31:32.149 --> 02:31:33.751
because I don't know
when this is going out,

02:31:33.751 --> 02:31:35.119
but, like, the amount of burgers

02:31:35.119 --> 02:31:37.354
and things filled with weird sauces

02:31:37.354 --> 02:31:40.691
I had to try for this
show is just unbelievable.

02:31:40.691 --> 02:31:42.193
And Starbucks, I don't know,

02:31:42.193 --> 02:31:44.228
but, like, it looks like
you really made it in Italy.

02:31:44.228 --> 02:31:45.963
You're, like, serving actual Italian food.

02:31:45.963 --> 02:31:47.031
So thank you.

02:31:47.031 --> 02:31:50.201
And here we have some of our
exclusive breakfast items.

02:31:50.201 --> 02:31:52.803
This is the Impossible sandwich;

02:31:52.803 --> 02:31:54.939
the bacon and Gruyère egg bites;

02:31:54.939 --> 02:31:56.674
the bacon sausage egg wrap;

02:31:56.674 --> 02:31:59.009
the bacon, Gouda, and egg sandwich;

02:31:59.009 --> 02:32:01.779
and here's the berry trio parfait.

02:32:01.779 --> 02:32:04.548
Let's take a bite of
the Impossible sandwich.

02:32:04.548 --> 02:32:07.551
I've had this before, and I
feel like I mostly like it.

02:32:07.551 --> 02:32:09.487
It's just a little bit weird

02:32:09.487 --> 02:32:11.021
if you let it sit for too long.

02:32:12.857 --> 02:32:15.259
I feel like for a not-real sausage patty,

02:32:15.259 --> 02:32:16.827
this actually tastes pretty good.

02:32:16.827 --> 02:32:18.262
I've always thought that the egg bites

02:32:18.262 --> 02:32:20.297
were some sort of genius move,

02:32:20.297 --> 02:32:22.633
even though Starbucks
definitely didn't invent them.

02:32:22.633 --> 02:32:24.802
My favorite are the egg white bites.

02:32:24.802 --> 02:32:28.572
These don't look edible
anymore, but I'll take a bite.

02:32:30.007 --> 02:32:31.308
That's really good, actually.

02:32:31.308 --> 02:32:33.711
I think it's just because
I got a mouthful of bacon,

02:32:33.711 --> 02:32:35.346
but it tastes really good.

02:32:35.346 --> 02:32:38.315
And then we have a bunch of sandwiches.

02:32:38.315 --> 02:32:40.684
Here we call sandwiches tramezzini,

02:32:40.684 --> 02:32:43.287
but it's just kind of translation.

02:32:43.287 --> 02:32:46.624
We have this one with salmon and avocado.

02:32:46.624 --> 02:32:50.661
Looks nice, even though the
options outside of the box

02:32:50.661 --> 02:32:52.229
look very, like, look delicious.

02:32:52.229 --> 02:32:54.498
So I wouldn't go for the boxed one.

02:32:54.498 --> 02:32:57.201
We have this one with porchetta,

02:32:57.201 --> 02:33:01.005
which is roasted pork from
Rome and the Roman region.

02:33:01.005 --> 02:33:02.306
Very, very good.

02:33:02.306 --> 02:33:04.108
And, yeah, if you're ever around there,

02:33:04.108 --> 02:33:07.778
they also do a lot of nice
festivals, so check it out.

02:33:07.778 --> 02:33:10.514
This one has porchetta and mushrooms,

02:33:10.514 --> 02:33:14.118
and the last one is this one
with zucchini and eggplants.

02:33:14.118 --> 02:33:15.653
We also got salads.

02:33:15.653 --> 02:33:19.490
We have chicken and cheese,

02:33:19.490 --> 02:33:21.625
what looks like grated Parmesan,

02:33:21.625 --> 02:33:24.395
and then we got tuna and feta

02:33:24.395 --> 02:33:26.864
with croutons and olives again.

02:33:26.864 --> 02:33:29.400
This is all you need for a salad.

02:33:29.400 --> 02:33:32.203
The only Caesar we know
here is Julius Caesar.

02:33:32.203 --> 02:33:34.605
I know that's bad, but actually it's true.

02:33:34.605 --> 02:33:36.574
It's just very, very
cliché, but it's true.

02:33:36.574 --> 02:33:37.808
We don't like Caesar salad.

02:33:37.808 --> 02:33:40.511
And then we've got this
one, it's called pincho,

02:33:40.511 --> 02:33:44.748
with cured ham, artichoke
sauce, and mozzarella.

02:33:44.748 --> 02:33:46.884
OK, interesting shape. It looks funny.

02:33:46.884 --> 02:33:48.852
I don't really know what a pincho is.

02:33:48.852 --> 02:33:51.155
It may be something from
another Italian region.

02:33:51.155 --> 02:33:53.157
I'm not so familiar with it actually.

02:33:53.157 --> 02:33:55.392
To be honest, this
artichoke is a bit of a joke

02:33:55.392 --> 02:33:57.661
because there is not a lot of it.

02:33:58.729 --> 02:34:00.097
Let's try it out and see.

02:34:03.634 --> 02:34:07.037
That artichoke actually
tastes quite natural,

02:34:07.037 --> 02:34:08.038
so very nice.

02:34:08.038 --> 02:34:09.406
Yeah, it's not flavoring.

02:34:09.406 --> 02:34:10.341
Yeah, I like this one.

02:34:10.341 --> 02:34:13.043
We then have some stuffed croissants

02:34:13.043 --> 02:34:15.879
because here we're not French,

02:34:15.879 --> 02:34:18.649
so we're not scared of
putting things in croissants,

02:34:18.649 --> 02:34:20.985
like our friends across the border.

02:34:20.985 --> 02:34:22.253
So this, they're quite similar.

02:34:22.253 --> 02:34:25.889
This one has cured ham and
scamorza, it looks like.

02:34:25.889 --> 02:34:27.458
A little salad thing.

02:34:27.458 --> 02:34:28.993
I honestly, I don't really like it.

02:34:28.993 --> 02:34:30.194
Doesn't taste like much,

02:34:30.194 --> 02:34:33.297
and it just ruins everything visually.

02:34:33.297 --> 02:34:36.200
Next croissant we have, I
think it's the same cheese

02:34:36.200 --> 02:34:38.535
just with cooked ham instead.

02:34:38.535 --> 02:34:41.605
In Italy we actually do eat
a lot of savory croissants.

02:34:41.605 --> 02:34:43.941
Sorry, French people.

02:34:43.941 --> 02:34:47.344
We usually eat them as
tiny bites in an aperitif.

02:34:47.344 --> 02:34:49.580
They serve them. They're
really, really this size.

02:34:49.580 --> 02:34:50.581
They're very tiny.

02:34:50.581 --> 02:34:51.849
We also have this one,

02:34:51.849 --> 02:34:53.584
which is supposed to be a focaccia

02:34:53.584 --> 02:34:56.220
with a plant-based schnitzel.

02:34:56.220 --> 02:34:58.522
I mean, honestly, this is not focaccia.

02:34:58.522 --> 02:35:02.459
I mean, quite clearly there's
been some mistake in the menu

02:35:02.459 --> 02:35:05.129
because it's just a sandwich,

02:35:05.129 --> 02:35:06.930
and I don't know, why
do plant-based things

02:35:06.930 --> 02:35:09.466
always have very sad buns like this?

02:35:09.466 --> 02:35:10.968
Why don't you use this one?

02:35:10.968 --> 02:35:12.202
This looks much nicer.

02:35:12.202 --> 02:35:15.039
This is just very sad and plain.

02:35:15.039 --> 02:35:17.474
We do have some snacks as well.

02:35:18.442 --> 02:35:20.678
We have some mixed fruits and nuts,

02:35:20.678 --> 02:35:24.481
we have roasted and salted mixed nuts,

02:35:24.481 --> 02:35:26.483
and then we have cheese snacks.

02:35:26.483 --> 02:35:29.987
OK, this looks like it's a thing,

02:35:29.987 --> 02:35:34.658
because McDonald's also
has those tiny Parmesans,

02:35:34.658 --> 02:35:36.327
those tiny Parmesan snacks,

02:35:36.327 --> 02:35:38.228
and Starbucks seems to be following suit

02:35:38.228 --> 02:35:40.631
and just giving you some cheese snacks.

02:35:40.631 --> 02:35:43.400
It just says it's a semi-hard cheese.

02:35:43.400 --> 02:35:45.636
And it's only made with
three ingredients. Nice.

02:35:45.636 --> 02:35:48.806
You know, milk, salt, and rennet.

02:35:48.806 --> 02:35:51.842
OK, no, I'm a bit disappointed.

02:35:51.842 --> 02:35:55.546
I was expecting actual cheese,
like tiny bits of cheese.

02:35:55.546 --> 02:35:57.881
This is like, it's like a chip.

02:36:00.951 --> 02:36:04.488
Yeah, they're cheesy. They're
not too bad, actually.

02:36:04.488 --> 02:36:07.157
Moving on to our more lunchy options.

02:36:07.157 --> 02:36:10.194
This is the grilled cheese on sourdough.

02:36:10.194 --> 02:36:12.963
The tomato mozzarella
sandwich on focaccia.

02:36:12.963 --> 02:36:15.299
They also offer a ham
and Swiss on a baguette

02:36:15.299 --> 02:36:17.735
and a Turkey provolone pesto on ciabatta

02:36:17.735 --> 02:36:19.103
that we did not get.

02:36:19.103 --> 02:36:21.405
I want to take a bite
of this grilled cheese.

02:36:21.405 --> 02:36:23.207
The bread actually looks pretty good.

02:36:23.207 --> 02:36:24.742
There's not going to be a cheese pull.

02:36:24.742 --> 02:36:27.077
It's going to crack in half if I do that.

02:36:27.077 --> 02:36:30.714
It's literally so solid
from sitting here all day.

02:36:34.685 --> 02:36:39.356
[crew laughing]

02:36:39.356 --> 02:36:41.925
OK, wait, it looks like
there's no cheese even in this.

02:36:41.925 --> 02:36:44.061
That's so weird.

02:36:44.061 --> 02:36:45.929
It must be a lighter cheese.

02:36:45.929 --> 02:36:47.731
I've had way better grilled cheese,

02:36:47.731 --> 02:36:50.300
but this bread's actually pretty tasty.

02:36:50.300 --> 02:36:53.370
This sandwich seems
inspired by Italian flavors,

02:36:53.370 --> 02:36:56.740
so I'm very shocked that
it's not on the Italian menu.

02:36:56.740 --> 02:36:59.109
That is one sad-looking sandwich.

02:36:59.109 --> 02:37:00.677
I'm going to take a bite from the middle.

02:37:00.677 --> 02:37:02.679
Don't be mad. It's just
that all the filling

02:37:02.679 --> 02:37:06.183
has moved to the center of the bread.

02:37:07.718 --> 02:37:11.422
It's not bad. It's not great,
but it's not a bad sandwich.

02:37:11.422 --> 02:37:13.490
It mostly tastes like pesto.

02:37:13.490 --> 02:37:15.859
We also have a variety of protein boxes.

02:37:15.859 --> 02:37:18.562
Here we have the PB&amp;J protein box.

02:37:18.562 --> 02:37:20.631
This used to be my lunch every single day

02:37:20.631 --> 02:37:21.832
when I was in college.

02:37:21.832 --> 02:37:26.003
Starbucks in Italy has
a lot of bakery options.

02:37:26.003 --> 02:37:27.471
This I'm very excited about

02:37:27.471 --> 02:37:31.241
because I think we do actually
associate Starbucks with

02:37:31.241 --> 02:37:33.644
a breakfast café, in a way.

02:37:33.644 --> 02:37:37.648
Starting from a maple and pecan braid.

02:37:37.648 --> 02:37:40.818
Then we have a cinnamon swirl.

02:37:40.818 --> 02:37:42.653
Yeah, it looks nice and fluffy.

02:37:42.653 --> 02:37:44.721
And then we've got the saddest,

02:37:44.721 --> 02:37:47.391
saddest-looking croissant ever.

02:37:47.391 --> 02:37:49.726
This is the vegan one.

02:37:49.726 --> 02:37:52.563
It's just a very unpleasant brown.

02:37:52.563 --> 02:37:54.798
Is this what the lack of butter makes?

02:37:54.798 --> 02:37:57.601
Like, just something very brown?

02:37:57.601 --> 02:38:00.838
It doesn't feel that great, and inside,

02:38:00.838 --> 02:38:03.040
it just actually ...

02:38:03.040 --> 02:38:05.542
it cuts a little bit like a bread,

02:38:05.542 --> 02:38:06.910
in a way.

02:38:09.580 --> 02:38:11.281
Right, bread's vegan, yeah.

02:38:11.281 --> 02:38:14.084
So here's some bread in
the shape of a croissant.

02:38:14.084 --> 02:38:15.719
And then we've got another croissant.

02:38:15.719 --> 02:38:19.156
This one is multigrain and honey.

02:38:19.156 --> 02:38:20.757
And then we've got a plain one.

02:38:20.757 --> 02:38:23.594
Very good lamination, actually, Starbucks.

02:38:23.594 --> 02:38:25.896
Look, there's a lot, a lot of layers.

02:38:25.896 --> 02:38:28.098
Actually, Starbucks
called these croissants

02:38:28.098 --> 02:38:31.668
"French croissants" in Italian as well.

02:38:31.668 --> 02:38:34.905
And they actually do look quite different

02:38:34.905 --> 02:38:38.041
compared to the Italian
croissants that I'm used to.

02:38:38.041 --> 02:38:39.109
Italian croissants,

02:38:39.109 --> 02:38:42.246
they're not made of layers
of dough and butter.

02:38:42.246 --> 02:38:43.080
Let's see.

02:38:49.520 --> 02:38:51.088
A plain one, I will have it

02:38:51.088 --> 02:38:53.557
only if it's laminated this way.

02:38:53.557 --> 02:38:55.959
I think the Italian one is
just really meant to be filled,

02:38:55.959 --> 02:39:00.297
so I'm curious to see how the
others actually look and feel,

02:39:00.297 --> 02:39:02.132
just because they are
still the French ones,

02:39:02.132 --> 02:39:03.367
but they are filled.

02:39:03.367 --> 02:39:06.837
So, we've got this one
here with apricot jam.

02:39:06.837 --> 02:39:08.071
Let's check it out.

02:39:09.373 --> 02:39:11.174
Yeah, lots of jam.

02:39:11.174 --> 02:39:12.609
Looks quite nice.

02:39:12.609 --> 02:39:17.214
And then we have the
green thing here in Italy

02:39:17.214 --> 02:39:18.782
that is not matcha.

02:39:18.782 --> 02:39:20.584
It's pistachio.

02:39:24.087 --> 02:39:26.223
Tastes like a nutty spread.

02:39:26.223 --> 02:39:28.926
Quite a nice spread.

02:39:28.926 --> 02:39:30.527
There's not a lot of it, though.

02:39:30.527 --> 02:39:32.429
And final one, we've got the custard.

02:39:32.429 --> 02:39:34.064
This also looks quite nice.

02:39:34.064 --> 02:39:37.267
Just want to see how much
custard there is in here.

02:39:37.267 --> 02:39:39.703
There's a lot. It's a bit eggy as well,

02:39:39.703 --> 02:39:42.105
which is what I would
look for in a custard.

02:39:43.140 --> 02:39:45.142
Not too lemony, just a hint.

02:39:45.142 --> 02:39:46.810
And a bit of vanilla.

02:39:46.810 --> 02:39:49.346
And apparently you can also
get a hazelnut croissant,

02:39:49.346 --> 02:39:51.582
but we were not able to get it.

02:39:51.582 --> 02:39:55.085
And then we have a double-chocolate cookie

02:39:55.085 --> 02:39:57.254
and a hazelnut doughnut.

02:39:58.422 --> 02:40:02.492
Yeah, we're starting to
enter foreign territory here.

02:40:02.492 --> 02:40:05.729
Maybe a bit sad compared
to what's coming after,

02:40:05.729 --> 02:40:07.431
which are these mini doughnuts.

02:40:07.431 --> 02:40:09.333
Quite cute and colorful.

02:40:09.333 --> 02:40:10.667
And then we have some brownies.

02:40:10.667 --> 02:40:13.737
We have a caramel crumble brownie,

02:40:13.737 --> 02:40:16.940
and then we have a
triple-chocolate brownie.

02:40:16.940 --> 02:40:18.609
I actually quite like brownies.

02:40:18.609 --> 02:40:23.280
It's one of those sort
of foreign cakes that

02:40:23.280 --> 02:40:25.549
I'm kind of very used to,

02:40:25.549 --> 02:40:27.517
and I don't mind having it.

02:40:27.517 --> 02:40:30.721
Let's see if we do it well here in Italy.

02:40:32.990 --> 02:40:35.559
This is like the ones I'm
used to that I've had.

02:40:35.559 --> 02:40:36.994
And then we have this one.

02:40:36.994 --> 02:40:40.330
It's a raspberry and coconut loaf cake.

02:40:40.330 --> 02:40:44.468
It does look a bit like
a typical Italian cake.

02:40:44.468 --> 02:40:46.670
I had no idea that this type of cakes

02:40:46.670 --> 02:40:50.073
were called loaf cakes,
but seems quite accurate.

02:40:50.073 --> 02:40:52.676
Not quite convinced about
the stuff at the top.

02:40:52.676 --> 02:40:55.445
It just doesn't seem necessary.

02:40:55.445 --> 02:40:58.348
I would've put it inside
just to flavor the dough

02:40:58.348 --> 02:41:00.050
rather than just put it at the top.

02:41:00.050 --> 02:41:02.953
And then we have a strawberry cheesecake.

02:41:02.953 --> 02:41:06.256
Then you may also be
able to find apple pie;

02:41:06.256 --> 02:41:10.360
apricot-filled rings;
custard and raisin swirl;

02:41:10.360 --> 02:41:12.663
then a vanilla and chocolate muffin

02:41:12.663 --> 02:41:14.931
that's also available in triple chocolate,

02:41:14.931 --> 02:41:16.967
brownie, and orange;

02:41:16.967 --> 02:41:18.735
mini chocolate muffins;

02:41:18.735 --> 02:41:23.273
carrot cake, that can also be
red velvet and chocolate cake;

02:41:23.273 --> 02:41:25.709
and a milk chocolate gold coin.

02:41:25.709 --> 02:41:28.278
The US also has a lot of baked goods.

02:41:28.278 --> 02:41:31.581
We have a couple of the
iconic Starbucks cake pops.

02:41:31.581 --> 02:41:34.184
I want to take a bite of
this cookies and cream one.

02:41:37.888 --> 02:41:39.022
That's so good.

02:41:39.022 --> 02:41:41.124
This is the blueberry scone,

02:41:41.124 --> 02:41:42.926
the everything bagel,

02:41:42.926 --> 02:41:45.829
the petite vanilla scone, the coffee cake,

02:41:45.829 --> 02:41:48.265
even though it looks
like someone sat on it.

02:41:49.099 --> 02:41:51.935
It looks a little smooshed,
but it's very good.

02:41:51.935 --> 02:41:56.006
The incredible, incomparable lemon loaf.

02:41:56.006 --> 02:41:57.374
It's delicious.

02:41:57.374 --> 02:41:59.276
The glazed doughnut.

02:41:59.276 --> 02:42:01.845
I did say that Italy's
bagel didn't look that good,

02:42:01.845 --> 02:42:03.847
not that ours looks any better,

02:42:03.847 --> 02:42:06.216
but I just want to taste
the everything bagel

02:42:06.216 --> 02:42:08.852
to see what the flavor is giving.

02:42:10.787 --> 02:42:12.289
It's, like, mediocre.

02:42:12.289 --> 02:42:15.892
It's not that good on flavor,
and it's not a great texture.

02:42:15.892 --> 02:42:19.996
I would only reach for a
Starbucks bagel if I was, like,

02:42:19.996 --> 02:42:21.798
going on a flight or something

02:42:21.798 --> 02:42:23.767
and this was just my only option.

02:42:23.767 --> 02:42:25.469
I don't think that I
would ever purchase it

02:42:25.469 --> 02:42:28.538
with a million other good
bagel options around me.

02:42:28.538 --> 02:42:29.573
So, the pumpkin loaf

02:42:29.573 --> 02:42:32.876
and the pumpkin cream cheese
muffin are seasonal exclusives

02:42:32.876 --> 02:42:34.945
along with the baked apple croissant,

02:42:34.945 --> 02:42:36.446
which was not available today.

02:42:36.446 --> 02:42:38.148
I feel like people are
buying them like crazy.

02:42:38.148 --> 02:42:39.049
They're really good.

02:42:39.049 --> 02:42:40.450
And if you want the little snacks,

02:42:40.450 --> 02:42:41.785
there are also these options.

02:42:41.785 --> 02:42:45.055
We've got yogurt with wildflower honey

02:42:45.055 --> 02:42:47.991
and yogurt with berries and jam.

02:42:47.991 --> 02:42:48.959
Then we've got some fruits.

02:42:48.959 --> 02:42:50.660
You can also get pineapple,

02:42:50.660 --> 02:42:53.063
and then we've got just a fruit salad.

02:42:53.063 --> 02:42:56.800
And finally we've got this
thing, the cookie straw.

02:42:56.800 --> 02:42:58.969
So, is this how you're
supposed to have it?

02:42:58.969 --> 02:43:01.204
This feels like something
a child would have.

02:43:01.204 --> 02:43:04.341
It's like I'm alone at
home and I'm, like, 12.

02:43:04.341 --> 02:43:07.477
I'm having a very calorific
drink with a weird straw.

02:43:09.513 --> 02:43:11.047
Yeah, weird.

02:43:13.083 --> 02:43:15.552
I actually don't mind the straw per se,

02:43:15.552 --> 02:43:19.990
but just the idea seems so ridiculous.

02:43:19.990 --> 02:43:23.794
We also got a few iconic
Starbucks checkout snacks.

02:43:23.794 --> 02:43:26.129
So, this is the marshmallow dream bar,

02:43:26.129 --> 02:43:27.330
we have the madeleines,

02:43:27.330 --> 02:43:29.699
and we also have the
vanilla almond biscotti.

02:43:29.699 --> 02:43:32.068
I see these at every
single Starbucks I go to,

02:43:32.068 --> 02:43:33.870
and I'm always tempted to buy one.

02:43:33.870 --> 02:43:35.806
I kind of want to try these madeleines.

02:43:35.806 --> 02:43:38.141
I don't think I've ever
had a madeleine before.

02:43:42.546 --> 02:43:43.547
That's pretty good!

02:43:43.547 --> 02:43:46.349
It kind of tastes like
a cakey sugar cookie.

02:43:46.349 --> 02:43:47.884
I don't know if it's
supposed to taste like that,

02:43:47.884 --> 02:43:49.586
but it does taste like that.

02:43:49.586 --> 02:43:50.987
You may also know Starbucks

02:43:50.987 --> 02:43:53.156
for the Starbucks Reserve roasteries

02:43:53.156 --> 02:43:55.759
that are very much present in the US.

02:43:55.759 --> 02:43:57.994
You can also find them in other countries,

02:43:57.994 --> 02:44:00.530
and actually there's one
here in Italy too in Milan

02:44:00.530 --> 02:44:02.699
that opened in 2018.

02:44:02.699 --> 02:44:06.169
And the roasteries are famous for having

02:44:06.169 --> 02:44:09.573
different types of coffee
that have the rarest coffee

02:44:09.573 --> 02:44:11.107
that you can find at Starbucks.

02:44:11.107 --> 02:44:13.343
They offer experiences at these roasteries

02:44:13.343 --> 02:44:15.645
where they demonstrate different
ways to make the coffee

02:44:15.645 --> 02:44:18.481
through blending, brewing, and infusions,

02:44:18.481 --> 02:44:21.117
and they also have wine, beers, cocktails,

02:44:21.117 --> 02:44:22.819
some of which include coffee.

02:44:22.819 --> 02:44:24.521
They have a lot of food options too.

02:44:24.521 --> 02:44:27.057
Each roastery is a little
different in its architecture,

02:44:27.057 --> 02:44:29.492
so it's really interesting
just to have a look around.

02:44:29.492 --> 02:44:31.461
Unfortunately we were not able

02:44:31.461 --> 02:44:33.663
to visit the roastery in this trip,

02:44:33.663 --> 02:44:35.999
but we actually went in 2018,

02:44:35.999 --> 02:44:38.835
so we're going to play
some footage of our visit.

02:44:38.835 --> 02:44:39.903
I was there.

02:44:39.903 --> 02:44:41.671
We took a visit to one of the roasteries

02:44:41.671 --> 02:44:44.241
here in New York City.
It was really cool to see

02:44:44.241 --> 02:44:45.709
how they make these different drinks,

02:44:45.709 --> 02:44:48.345
and everything in there is so fancy

02:44:48.345 --> 02:44:50.213
compared to a regular Starbucks.

02:44:50.213 --> 02:44:52.749
These are the drinks exclusive
to the New York roastery

02:44:52.749 --> 02:44:54.150
that we wanted to try.

02:44:54.150 --> 02:44:56.453
Let's start with the
hazelnut bianco latte.

02:44:56.453 --> 02:44:57.787
I love hazelnut, so.

02:44:59.356 --> 02:45:00.257
It's really good.

02:45:00.257 --> 02:45:02.359
It's really, really, really good!

02:45:02.359 --> 02:45:03.660
I feel like it tastes better

02:45:03.660 --> 02:45:06.529
than any other Starbucks coffee I've had.

02:45:06.529 --> 02:45:09.599
Let's try the
whiskey-barrel-aged cold brew.

02:45:09.599 --> 02:45:11.234
This is intriguing to me.

02:45:11.234 --> 02:45:12.469
I hate whiskey,

02:45:12.469 --> 02:45:14.504
but there's no real whiskey in this.

02:45:18.742 --> 02:45:22.312
OK, wait, it tastes like
there is whiskey in it,

02:45:22.312 --> 02:45:23.713
but there isn't!

02:45:23.713 --> 02:45:25.782
I made sure to say alcohol-free.

02:45:25.782 --> 02:45:28.318
I think from what I'm understanding is

02:45:28.318 --> 02:45:31.988
that they might age this
in the whiskey barrels

02:45:31.988 --> 02:45:34.357
once the whiskey is
removed from those barrels,

02:45:34.357 --> 02:45:37.027
but it still tastes very strong.

02:45:39.930 --> 02:45:42.999
It's spirit-free, but
the spirits are lurking.

02:45:42.999 --> 02:45:44.567
You can still taste it.

02:45:44.567 --> 02:45:47.437
This was actually invented in Italy

02:45:47.437 --> 02:45:51.541
and then, yeah, launched again,
recreated at the roastery.

02:45:51.541 --> 02:45:53.810
This is the oleato caffè latte,

02:45:53.810 --> 02:45:56.680
and oleato just literally means oiled,

02:45:56.680 --> 02:46:00.850
and it's just a caffè latte
with a shot of olive oil.

02:46:00.850 --> 02:46:03.954
Apparently this is the CEO of Starbucks

02:46:03.954 --> 02:46:05.689
that traveled to Italy, to Sicily,

02:46:05.689 --> 02:46:10.660
and just saw some people having
shots of olive oil in coffee

02:46:10.694 --> 02:46:13.096
and thought it would be a good idea

02:46:13.096 --> 02:46:15.498
to roll this out internationally.

02:46:15.498 --> 02:46:17.167
And for some reason thought that

02:46:17.167 --> 02:46:19.970
all Italians were actually doing it.

02:46:19.970 --> 02:46:21.738
I don't know, it's the
first time I hear it.

02:46:21.738 --> 02:46:24.607
Like, I would be quite happy
to have a shot of olive oil

02:46:24.607 --> 02:46:26.810
for just energy,

02:46:26.810 --> 02:46:28.678
but I don't know if I
would like it in my coffee.

02:46:28.678 --> 02:46:30.880
That seems like a bit too much.

02:46:30.880 --> 02:46:33.116
It's like, "Oh, what are two things

02:46:33.116 --> 02:46:34.918
Italians are associated with?

02:46:34.918 --> 02:46:35.952
Olive oil and coffee.

02:46:35.952 --> 02:46:39.022
Let's just put them all
together and make it a drink."

02:46:39.022 --> 02:46:40.557
It's green!

02:46:42.292 --> 02:46:43.493
It's green!

02:46:43.493 --> 02:46:47.263
And obviously the oil is
floating on the coffee.

02:46:47.263 --> 02:46:50.000
Well, so the idea is that
they should emulsify,

02:46:50.000 --> 02:46:52.335
but it's been sitting here for a bit

02:46:52.335 --> 02:46:53.870
because we've been doing all the filming,

02:46:53.870 --> 02:46:55.939
so perhaps that's why they separated.

02:46:55.939 --> 02:46:57.974
It just smells like coffee.

02:46:57.974 --> 02:46:59.009
Let's try it out.

02:47:00.744 --> 02:47:04.280
I don't taste much the
olive oil, which is OK.

02:47:04.280 --> 02:47:06.883
It leaves you a different
feeling on the lips,

02:47:06.883 --> 02:47:08.585
like the same feeling that you get

02:47:08.585 --> 02:47:12.022
when you bite into a very oily thing.

02:47:12.022 --> 02:47:15.058
This is the moment that I've
been dreading this entire day.

02:47:15.058 --> 02:47:17.961
The oleato caffè lattes.

02:47:17.961 --> 02:47:19.829
These are basically lattes

02:47:19.829 --> 02:47:22.332
with a bunch of olive oil in them.

02:47:22.332 --> 02:47:23.900
I don't know whose idea this was.

02:47:23.900 --> 02:47:25.702
It doesn't sound like a good idea to me,

02:47:25.702 --> 02:47:29.539
but let's see which one is
better, iced or not iced.

02:47:30.874 --> 02:47:32.375
It's not bad.

02:47:32.375 --> 02:47:35.879
I can definitely taste
that there's oil in this,

02:47:35.879 --> 02:47:38.648
but it's not aggressively
oily in my mouth,

02:47:38.648 --> 02:47:40.650
which is what I was really dreading.

02:47:40.650 --> 02:47:42.252
It's really not terrible.

02:47:42.252 --> 02:47:44.421
I think it's the oat milk that's helping

02:47:44.421 --> 02:47:46.356
cover up some of what's happening.

02:47:46.356 --> 02:47:48.324
This looks terrible.

02:47:48.324 --> 02:47:51.594
The iced latte has completely separated,

02:47:51.594 --> 02:47:54.497
so the top is just a layer of olive oil,

02:47:54.497 --> 02:47:56.366
which means I'm going to get a mouthful

02:47:56.366 --> 02:47:58.168
of olive oil upon first sip.

02:48:02.972 --> 02:48:04.674
It just tastes like a
mouthful of olive oil.

02:48:04.674 --> 02:48:05.942
Let me mix it with a straw

02:48:05.942 --> 02:48:07.310
and see if that helps.

02:48:07.310 --> 02:48:09.579
To be clear, this didn't look like this

02:48:09.579 --> 02:48:10.880
when they first gave it to us.

02:48:10.880 --> 02:48:13.049
It's just been sitting around for a while.

02:48:13.049 --> 02:48:15.652
It tastes better but still
mostly tastes like olive oil.

02:48:15.652 --> 02:48:18.221
I think if I had to get an oleato again,

02:48:18.221 --> 02:48:19.456
I would only get it hot,

02:48:19.456 --> 02:48:22.859
just because it covers up
all the olive oil flavor,

02:48:22.859 --> 02:48:25.361
which kind of defeats the
purpose of getting one of these.

02:48:25.361 --> 02:48:27.030
But they're not terrible.

02:48:29.799 --> 02:48:31.668
It's quite hard actually for me to think

02:48:31.668 --> 02:48:35.071
that Starbucks is actually
competing with the cafés

02:48:35.071 --> 02:48:36.473
that you can find here,

02:48:36.473 --> 02:48:38.942
just because the offer
is very, very different.

02:48:38.942 --> 02:48:40.510
Like, it's the only place

02:48:40.510 --> 02:48:44.214
where you can find drinks
this size, this elaborate,

02:48:44.214 --> 02:48:47.250
and with this much cream and milk

02:48:47.250 --> 02:48:49.252
and syrups and all this stuff.

02:48:49.252 --> 02:48:52.689
I would say in general Starbucks
is definitely huge here.

02:48:52.689 --> 02:48:54.090
You can find them everywhere.

02:48:54.090 --> 02:48:56.526
I feel like you're either a Dunkin' person

02:48:56.526 --> 02:48:58.128
or you're a Starbucks person.

02:48:58.128 --> 02:49:01.264
And it's very common for
a chain like Starbucks

02:49:01.264 --> 02:49:03.933
to be somebody's everyday coffee shop.

02:49:03.933 --> 02:49:06.002
I will say if you live in a major city

02:49:06.002 --> 02:49:07.504
with a lot of other options,

02:49:07.504 --> 02:49:08.905
a lot of different coffee shops,

02:49:08.905 --> 02:49:11.207
you might not head to
Starbucks all the time,

02:49:11.207 --> 02:49:14.277
but it is one of the more
popular coffee options

02:49:14.277 --> 02:49:15.912
in places like suburbs.

02:49:15.912 --> 02:49:17.147
It's hard to say that it's popular

02:49:17.147 --> 02:49:20.583
because it is not really
present everywhere.

02:49:20.583 --> 02:49:23.620
Obviously it is in Milan,
Rome, and the big cities,

02:49:23.620 --> 02:49:25.522
but you won't find it in a village.

02:49:25.522 --> 02:49:28.424
What we do, I'm from a
medium-sized town in Italy,

02:49:28.424 --> 02:49:32.362
but in the evening I'll
go out to a small town.

02:49:32.362 --> 02:49:33.796
You know, during the day I'll go out

02:49:33.796 --> 02:49:35.331
for a day trip in a small town.

02:49:35.331 --> 02:49:37.901
I won't live there, but
I will hang around there.

02:49:37.901 --> 02:49:39.769
That's where you don't find the chains,

02:49:39.769 --> 02:49:43.573
and I think that is what
still makes Starbucks

02:49:43.573 --> 02:49:46.509
perceived as something a bit foreign

02:49:46.509 --> 02:49:49.379
because you still don't
see it in these tiny towns

02:49:49.379 --> 02:49:50.980
and you still see the local café.

02:49:50.980 --> 02:49:53.049
It's just in general the idea of chains

02:49:53.049 --> 02:49:54.784
doesn't really resonate well.

02:49:54.784 --> 02:49:58.855
In terms of the actual
coffees, like the long coffees,

02:49:58.855 --> 02:50:01.090
I don't know actually if
they get lots of orders

02:50:01.090 --> 02:50:02.458
from Italians.

02:50:02.458 --> 02:50:05.995
I think you either just, I
would either go personally

02:50:05.995 --> 02:50:07.664
just for a simple espresso

02:50:07.664 --> 02:50:10.833
or for the elaborate things

02:50:10.833 --> 02:50:13.203
because they are a bit
like an ice cream to me.

02:50:13.203 --> 02:50:15.471
Treat yourself, but also,
like, if I see you drinking

02:50:15.471 --> 02:50:18.608
that cookie crumble mocha
Frap at 9 in the morning,

02:50:18.608 --> 02:50:20.510
I'm gonna slap it out of your hand.

02:50:20.510 --> 02:50:22.679
Grow up, please!

02:50:22.679 --> 02:50:26.549
Just the culture of, like,
the big drink to take away,

02:50:26.549 --> 02:50:29.752
to drink on the go, drink in your car,

02:50:29.752 --> 02:50:33.456
that's just not how
things work around here.

02:50:33.456 --> 02:50:36.759
People really love the
Starbucks seasonal menus.

02:50:36.759 --> 02:50:40.230
I think every year when fall
or Christmastime rolls around,

02:50:40.230 --> 02:50:41.464
everyone gets super excited

02:50:41.464 --> 02:50:43.233
to see what new stuff is on the menu,

02:50:43.233 --> 02:50:44.934
what old stuff is coming back.

02:50:44.934 --> 02:50:46.469
I mean, yeah, speaking of the food,

02:50:46.469 --> 02:50:48.371
I think they've done a very good job

02:50:48.371 --> 02:50:52.575
sort of adapting to the Italian flavors.

02:50:52.575 --> 02:50:54.811
The drinks are a little bit different.

02:50:54.811 --> 02:50:56.579
There are some things,
like cookies and cream,

02:50:56.579 --> 02:50:57.947
that are just not Italian.

02:50:57.947 --> 02:51:01.417
We all know that Starbucks
is a big American chain,

02:51:01.417 --> 02:51:04.921
and I think they obviously
want to keep a part of that

02:51:04.921 --> 02:51:07.890
because Italians are
curious about it as well.

02:51:10.893 --> 02:51:14.264
Unfortunately, Starbucks
does not list ingredients

02:51:14.264 --> 02:51:15.698
on its website.

02:51:15.698 --> 02:51:18.001
We did try to get in contact,

02:51:18.001 --> 02:51:20.169
but we're still waiting for a reply.

02:51:20.169 --> 02:51:22.939
The US, however, does provide
all of the ingredients

02:51:22.939 --> 02:51:24.107
for their full menu.

02:51:24.107 --> 02:51:25.208
We thought it would be interesting

02:51:25.208 --> 02:51:26.909
to see what's in the oleato range,

02:51:26.909 --> 02:51:29.679
since both US and Italy
have this available.

02:51:29.679 --> 02:51:33.216
The oleato caffè latte with
oat milk contains oat milk,

02:51:33.216 --> 02:51:35.818
which is just water and oats, canola oil,

02:51:35.818 --> 02:51:38.454
dipotassium phosphate, calcium carbonate,

02:51:38.454 --> 02:51:42.358
tricalcium phosphate, sea
salt, dicalcium phosphate,

02:51:42.358 --> 02:51:46.462
riboflavin, vitamin A,
vitamin D2, vitamin B12,

02:51:46.462 --> 02:51:48.998
brewed espresso, which
is just water and coffee,

02:51:48.998 --> 02:51:50.600
and extra-virgin olive oil.

02:51:50.600 --> 02:51:52.902
The exciting thing about
this drink is the addition

02:51:52.902 --> 02:51:54.370
of extra-virgin olive oil,

02:51:54.370 --> 02:51:57.540
which is mostly associated
with a Mediterranean diet.

02:51:57.540 --> 02:52:00.877
It does ramp up the calories
compared to a normal latte,

02:52:00.877 --> 02:52:03.880
which with 2% milk is 190 calories.

02:52:03.880 --> 02:52:06.282
But there's been a lot of
research surrounding the benefits

02:52:06.282 --> 02:52:07.917
of extra-virgin olive oil,

02:52:07.917 --> 02:52:10.320
particularly around preventing diseases

02:52:10.320 --> 02:52:11.988
and decreasing cholesterol.

02:52:11.988 --> 02:52:14.824
Plus the oleato latte has
been fortified with vitamins,

02:52:14.824 --> 02:52:16.492
so sounds pretty good to me,

02:52:16.492 --> 02:52:18.194
even though I'd never order this again.

02:52:20.930 --> 02:52:24.967
In the US, a venti caramel
Frappuccino is $6.75,

02:52:24.967 --> 02:52:27.437
or 6 euro and 37 cents.

02:52:27.437 --> 02:52:29.005
Keep in mind, that's a New York price.

02:52:29.005 --> 02:52:30.740
The prices might vary slightly

02:52:30.740 --> 02:52:32.342
depending on what state you're in.

02:52:32.342 --> 02:52:37.013
In Italy, a caramel Frappuccino
is 5 euros 70 cents.

02:52:37.013 --> 02:52:41.918
That translates to roughly $6.19,

02:52:41.918 --> 02:52:44.420
so it actually works out
cheaper here in Italy.

02:52:44.420 --> 02:52:48.224
In the US, a venti cappuccino is $6.25,

02:52:48.224 --> 02:52:50.960
or 5 euro and 90 cents.

02:52:50.960 --> 02:52:54.864
In Italy, a venti
cappuccino is 3 euros 40.

02:52:54.864 --> 02:52:59.068
In dollars, that translates into $3.69.

02:52:59.068 --> 02:53:00.770
To be honest, they're
kind of fair judging by

02:53:00.770 --> 02:53:02.372
how big the things are.

02:53:02.372 --> 02:53:05.742
Coffee's always quite
cheap actually, in Italy.

02:53:05.742 --> 02:53:08.511
It's usually around 1 euro.

02:53:08.511 --> 02:53:10.313
Lately has gone up a little bit,

02:53:10.313 --> 02:53:13.716
but, like, if you pay 1.50,
it's already very expensive.

02:53:13.716 --> 02:53:17.253
Make note of the fun Colonel
Sanders doing a cartwheel.

02:53:17.253 --> 02:53:19.188
Wasn't this guy, like, 70

02:53:19.188 --> 02:53:21.290
when he started Kentucky Fried Chicken?

02:53:21.290 --> 02:53:22.225
There's no way.

02:53:22.225 --> 02:53:24.927
If he's doing that, it's against his will.

02:53:26.996 --> 02:53:28.531
Moments before the ambulance was called.

